{"question_id": "T1-F01", "tier": 1, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Nahida is Lesser Lord Kusanali, also known by her Goetic name Buer, and is the God of Wisdom and the current Dendro Archon presiding over Sumeru.", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida", "verified": true}, {"fact": "She is the youngest of The Seven.", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida", "verified": true}, {"fact": "She was created from the purest branch of Irminsul by the previous Dendro Archon, Greater Lord Rukkhadevata, to be her successor.", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida", "verified": true}, {"fact": "After all memories of Greater Lord Rukkhadevata were erased from Teyvat, Lesser Lord Kusanali is believed by all, including herself, to have always been the original Dendro Archon.", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Despite her status as Sumeru's Archon, she had little power over her nation's affairs due to her isolation inside the Sanctuary of Surasthana for 500 years since her birth.", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida", "verified": true}, {"fact": "As the First Akasha Terminal, her consciousness is linked to the Akasha System, giving her access to its stores of knowledge and allowing her to possess people by occupying their consciousnesses.", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Out of respect for her people's free will, she only chooses to possess the bionic puppet Katheryne.", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida", "verified": true}, {"fact": "She is capable of appearing in the dreams of people across Sumeru.", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida", "verified": true}, {"fact": "No one in Sumeru other than the sages of Sumeru Akademiya has seen her since her birth 500 years ago; the sages rarely speak to her and rule over Sumeru in her place.", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida", "verified": true}, {"fact": "She is a playable Dendro character in Genshin Impact.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter Nahida", "verified": true}, {"fact": "She strives to have a stronger presence in Sumeru now that she has been freed from her extensive confinement in the Sanctuary of Surasthana.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter Nahida", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Nahida", "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "Buer", "Dendro Archon", "Sumeru", "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "Irminsul", "The Seven", "Akasha System", "Sanctuary of Surasthana", "Sumeru Akademiya"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Nahida", "relation": "is_also_known_as", "tail": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida"}, {"head": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "relation": "has_goetic_name", "tail": "Buer", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida"}, {"head": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "relation": "holds_title", "tail": "God of Wisdom", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida"}, {"head": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "relation": "is_archon_of", "tail": "Sumeru", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida"}, {"head": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "relation": "is_member_of", "tail": "The Seven", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida"}, {"head": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "relation": "created", "tail": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida"}, {"head": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "relation": "was_created_from", "tail": "Irminsul (purest branch)", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida"}, {"head": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "relation": "predecessor_of", "tail": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida"}, {"head": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "relation": "confined_in", "tail": "Sanctuary of Surasthana", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida"}, {"head": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "relation": "linked_to", "tail": "Akasha System", "doc_source": "NPC Nahida"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Confusing Nahida/Lesser Lord Kusanali with Greater Lord Rukkhadevata as the original Dendro Archon.", "correct": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata was the previous Dendro Archon who created Nahida as her successor. After Rukkhadevata's memories were erased from Teyvat, everyone (including Nahida herself) believes Nahida was always the original Dendro Archon."}, {"trap": "Claiming Nahida ruled Sumeru with full authority before being freed.", "correct": "Despite her Archon status, the sages of Sumeru Akademiya ruled in her place while she was isolated in the Sanctuary of Surasthana, and she had little power over national affairs."}, {"trap": "Stating Nahida can freely possess any person she wishes without restriction.", "correct": "While she has the ability to possess people via the Akasha System, out of respect for free will she only chooses to possess the bionic puppet Katheryne."}, {"trap": "Claiming Nahida is one of the original Seven Archons.", "correct": "Nahida is the youngest of The Seven, born only 500 years ago, and was created by the previous Dendro Archon Greater Lord Rukkhadevata."}, {"trap": "Confusing Nahida's Gnosis or its fate with those of other Archons (e.g., Venti's taken by Signora, Zhongli's given to Tsaritsa).", "correct": "The provided documents do not describe the fate of Nahida's Gnosis; any claim about it would be unsupported by these documents."}, {"trap": "Claiming 'Lesser Lord Kusanali' is a dismissive or derogatory title.", "correct": "The document explicitly states that 'Lesser Lord Kusanali' is considered to be a term of endearment for the archon."}, {"trap": "Conflating Nahida's element or Archon domain with Ei/Raiden Shogun (Electro) or other Archons.", "correct": "Nahida is specifically the Dendro Archon and God of Wisdom, not to be confused with other Archons' elements or domains."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "- 缺：纳西妲诞生的具体经过和灾厄期间的完整事件细节（NPC文档History部分在'During the cataclysm five hundred years ago, the previo...'处被截断）\n- 缺：纳西妲如何被释放出净善宫的具体剧情过程（文档仅在PlayableCharacter介绍中提及她已被释放，无细节）\n- 缺：纳西妲的神之心（Gnosis）的命运或去向\n- 缺：大慈树王（Greater Lord Rukkhadevata）记忆被抹除的具体过程和原因\n- 缺：纳西妲被释放后在须弥治理中的具体角色变化", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: - 缺：纳西妲诞生的具体经过和灾厄期间的完整事件细节（NPC文档History部分在'During the cataclysm five hundred years ago, the previo.."], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T1-F01", "tier": 1, "question": "What is Nahida's true identity and role as the Dendro Archon of Sumeru?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 2, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 2}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 3082, "oracle_out": 1590, "qc_in": 5032, "qc_out": 1999, "total": 11703}, "cost_usd": 0.3909}}
{"question_id": "T1-F02", "tier": 1, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "The Wanderer's original name is Scaramouche, also known as Kunikuzushi (Japanese: 国崩)", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "His codename among the Fatui was 'The Balladeer', and he was the Sixth of the Eleven Fatui Harbingers", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Scaramouche is a puppet created by Raiden Ei", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "He erased his existence from Irminsul and became the Wanderer, going by no other title since he has no home, kin, or destination", "doc_source": "[PlayableCharacter] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Wanderer came into existence in place of his previous incarnation after the latter expunged his previous appellations and their respective histories from Irminsul", "doc_source": "[PlayableCharacter] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Nahida enrolled him to Vahumana under the name 'Hat Guy'", "doc_source": "[PlayableCharacter] Wanderer", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Wanderer", "Scaramouche", "Kunikuzushi", "The Balladeer", "Raiden Ei", "Irminsul"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Raiden Ei", "relation": "created", "tail": "Scaramouche", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Scaramouche", "relation": "also known as", "tail": "Kunikuzushi", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Scaramouche", "relation": "codename", "tail": "The Balladeer", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Scaramouche", "relation": "became", "tail": "Wanderer", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Scaramouche", "relation": "erased existence from", "tail": "Irminsul", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Confusing the creator: some may incorrectly say Scaramouche was created by Raiden Shogun (the puppet Archon body) rather than Raiden Ei (the true consciousness/Electro Archon)", "correct": "The document explicitly states 'a puppet created by Raiden Ei'; Raiden Shogun is a separate puppet Ei later created to govern Inazuma, but this detail about Raiden Shogun is not in the provided documents"}, {"trap": "Claiming the Wanderer's 'original name' is 'Hat Guy'", "correct": "'Hat Guy' is merely the name Nahida used to enroll him at Vahumana after he became the Wanderer; his original names before erasure are Scaramouche / Kunikuzushi / The Balladeer"}, {"trap": "Stating that Il Dottore created Scaramouche", "correct": "Per the document, Dottore only assisted the Sumeru Akademiya sages in ascending Scaramouche into Shouki no Kami; Raiden Ei is his creator"}, {"trap": "Confusing Scaramouche with Raiden Shogun, as both are puppets created by Raiden Ei", "correct": "The documents only describe Scaramouche as 'a puppet created by Raiden Ei'; the existence of another puppet (Raiden Shogun) is not mentioned in these documents but is a common source of confusion from training data"}, {"trap": "Attributing the name 'Kabukimono' as an original name of the Wanderer", "correct": "The name 'Kabukimono' does not appear anywhere in the provided documents; only Scaramouche, Kunikuzushi, and The Balladeer are documented as prior names"}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "- 缺：Raiden Ei创造Scaramouche的具体原因、时间和背景（文档仅说'a puppet created by Raiden Ei'，无进一步细节）\n- 缺：Scaramouche作为木偶被抛弃/觉醒的详细经历（文档未提及）\n- 缺：'Kabukimono'这一名称是否为其曾用名的信息（文档中完全未出现该名称）\n- 缺：Raiden Ei与Raiden Shogun的区别说明（文档未涉及Raiden Shogun）\n- 文档对于本题核心问题（原名和创造者）提供了充分信息：原名Scaramouche/Kunikuzushi/The Balladeer，创造者Raiden Ei", "_review_flags": ["key_facts[1]: high-risk pattern — His codename among the Fatui was 'The Balladeer', and he was", "coverage_notes: - 缺：Raiden Ei创造Scaramouche的具体原因、时间和背景（文档仅说'a puppet created by Raiden Ei'，无进一步细节）\n- 缺：Scaramouche作为木"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T1-F02", "tier": 1, "question": "What is the Wanderer's original name, and who created him?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 3, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 3}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 4043, "oracle_out": 999, "qc_in": 5403, "qc_out": 1349, "total": 11794}, "cost_usd": 0.3178}}
{"question_id": "T1-F03", "tier": 1, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "The Akasha System was developed by Greater Lord Rukkhadevata using her Gnosis and was later expanded upon by Sumeru Akademiya after her death.", "doc_source": "Akasha System", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Akasha Terminal takes the shape of an earpiece and allows the transfer and sharing of information, granting users any knowledge they desire as long as they have the required credentials.", "doc_source": "Akasha System", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Akasha System is powered by the Dendro Archon's Gnosis.", "doc_source": "Akasha System", "verified": true}, {"fact": "To activate the device, the user must hold it and say 'May the Mighty God bless us with their voice of wisdom.'", "doc_source": "Akasha System", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Akasha Terminal is capable of harvesting the Jnana Energy of Sumeru's people, which is the reason people in Sumeru do not dream.", "doc_source": "Akasha System", "verified": true}, {"fact": "By gathering people's dreams, the Akasha Terminal can combine the knowledge of all people in Sumeru City, turning it into a 'single, massive brain.'", "doc_source": "Akasha System", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata created the Akasha System to 'borrow' the dreams of her people and empower herself, as she was unable to eradicate the second coming of forbidden knowledge invading Irminsul with her strength alone.", "doc_source": "Akasha System", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Prolonged use of the Akasha System carries risks: knowledge asserts itself as true and is difficult to forget/correct, and excessive use diminishes one's ability to think.", "doc_source": "Akasha System", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Akasha System is also capable of computation, producing new data such as predicting movements of certain persons based on existing data.", "doc_source": "Akasha System", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Desert-origin people are automatically given lower clearance than Sumeru City people when they come to Sumeru City due to old prejudice between Desert and Rainforest people.", "doc_source": "Akasha System", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Lesser Lord Kusanali is referred to as 'The First Akasha Terminal' and can enter anyone's mind as long as they're wearing their Akasha Terminal.", "doc_source": "Akasha System", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Akademiya's sages maximized the Akasha's output by trapping denizens of Sumeru City in a samsara, harvesting their dreams repeatedly to elevate Scaramouche to godhood.", "doc_source": "Akasha System", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Akasha System", "Akasha Terminal", "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "Sumeru Akademiya", "Gnosis", "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "Jnana Energy", "Irminsul", "Sumeru City", "Scaramouche"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "relation": "created", "tail": "Akasha System", "doc_source": "Akasha System"}, {"head": "Akasha System", "relation": "powered_by", "tail": "Dendro Archon's Gnosis", "doc_source": "Akasha System"}, {"head": "Sumeru Akademiya", "relation": "expanded_upon", "tail": "Akasha System", "doc_source": "Akasha System"}, {"head": "Akasha Terminal", "relation": "harvests", "tail": "Jnana Energy", "doc_source": "Akasha System"}, {"head": "Akasha System", "relation": "causes_loss_of", "tail": "dreams of Sumeru's people", "doc_source": "Akasha System"}, {"head": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "relation": "referred_to_as", "tail": "The First Akasha Terminal", "doc_source": "Akasha System"}, {"head": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "relation": "purpose_of_creation", "tail": "borrow dreams to combat forbidden knowledge in Irminsul", "doc_source": "Akasha System"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Confusing who created the Akasha System — attributing it to Lesser Lord Kusanali instead of Greater Lord Rukkhadevata.", "correct": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata created the Akasha System; Kusanali inherited it and later created the Neo Akasha Terminal."}, {"trap": "Claiming the Akasha System only provides knowledge and omitting its dream-harvesting and Jnana Energy collection functions.", "correct": "The Akasha System both provides knowledge and harvests Jnana Energy / dreams from the people of Sumeru."}, {"trap": "Stating that all Sumeru residents receive equal access/clearance through the Akasha Terminal.", "correct": "Desert-origin people receive lower clearance than Sumeru City residents due to prejudice between Desert and Rainforest people."}, {"trap": "Confusing the Akasha System with the Neo Akasha Terminal — the Neo Akasha Terminal is a separate weaponized upgrade created by Kusanali.", "correct": "The Neo Akasha Terminal is a distinct weaponized device created by Kusanali, different from the standard Akasha System/Terminal."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "The Akasha System document appears to be truncated at the end (description of Neo Akasha Terminal is cut off). Full details of the Neo Akasha Terminal's capabilities and its role in the Traveler's battle are missing. Otherwise, the document provides comprehensive coverage of the Akasha System's mechanics, origins, functions, and risks.", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: The Akasha System document appears to be truncated at the end (description of Neo Akasha Terminal is"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T1-F03", "tier": 1, "question": "How does the Akasha System work and what is its function in Sumeru?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 3, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 3}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 2784, "oracle_out": 1548, "qc_in": 4692, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 11024}, "cost_usd": 0.3782}}
{"question_id": "T1-F04", "tier": 1, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "The Akademiya is described as having Six Great Sages as part of its leadership, but the six individual Darshans (schools/departments) are not explicitly named or listed in the provided documents.", "doc_source": "Concept - Akademiya", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Akademiya has three virtues: Admonition, Ingenuity, and Praxis, which are described in Sumeru's Talent Level-Up Books.", "doc_source": "Concept - Akademiya", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Akademiya has six sins which are listed, but these are prohibitions, not Darshans/schools.", "doc_source": "Concept - Akademiya", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The commonly known six Darshans are Amurta, Rtawahist, Spantamad, Haravatat, Vahumana, and Kshahrewar — but none of these names appear anywhere in the provided reference documents.", "doc_source": "N/A", "verified": false, "memory_source": true}], "required_entities": ["Sumeru Akademiya", "Darshans"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Sumeru Akademiya", "relation": "governed_by", "tail": "Six Great Sages", "doc_source": "Concept - Akademiya"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Confusing the six sins of the Akademiya with the six Darshans (schools). The six sins are prohibitions (e.g., interfering with human evolution, tampering with life and death), not academic departments.", "correct": "The six sins and the six Darshans are entirely different concepts. The provided documents do not list the six Darshans by name."}, {"trap": "Assuming the three virtues (Admonition, Ingenuity, Praxis) are Darshans. These are virtues of the Akademiya, not schools.", "correct": "Admonition, Ingenuity, and Praxis are the three virtues of the Akademiya, not Darshans. There are only three virtues but the question asks about six Darshans."}, {"trap": "A model may confidently list six Darshan names (Amurta, Rtawahist, Spantamad, Haravatat, Vahumana, Kshahrewar) from training data, but this information is NOT present in the provided reference documents and cannot be verified here.", "correct": "The provided documents do not contain the names of the six Darshans. Any such answer would be sourced from training memory, not the reference material."}, {"trap": "Confusing the number six in 'Six Great Sages' with the six Darshans — assuming each sage leads a Darshan. While this may be true in game lore, the provided documents do not establish this relationship.", "correct": "The documents only state that the Six Great Sages are leaders of the Akademiya alongside Lesser Lord Kusanali, without linking them to specific Darshans."}, {"trap": "Mixing up Darshan names with similar-sounding Zoroastrian/Avestan terms or with names of Sumeru subareas (e.g., confusing Vahumana with Vanarana, or Haravatat with Avidya).", "correct": "Darshan names and Sumeru geographic locations are distinct concepts and should not be conflated."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "CRITICAL INFORMATION GAPS:\n- 缺：六个Darshan（学院/学派）的具体名称（如Amurta、Rtawahist、Spantamad、Haravatat、Vahumana、Kshahrewar）在提供的文档中完全未出现\n- 缺：每个Darshan的研究领域或学科方向的描述\n- 缺：每个Darshan与其对应的Great Sage之间的关系说明\n- 缺：Darshan一词本身的定义或在Akademiya中的含义说明\n- 缺：各Darshan的已知成员或代表角色信息\n- 结论：本题无法仅凭提供的参考文档给出完整且经验证的答案，需要额外的Akademiya学院结构相关文档", "_review_flags": ["key_facts[3]: verified=false — The commonly known six Darshans are Amurta, Rtawahist, Spant", "coverage_notes: CRITICAL INFORMATION GAPS:\n- 缺：六个Darshan（学院/学派）的具体名称（如Amurta、Rtawahist、Spantamad、Haravatat、Vahumana、"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T1-F04", "tier": 1, "question": "What are the six Darshans (schools) of the Sumeru Akademiya?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 2, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 2}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 2680, "oracle_out": 745, "qc_in": 3785, "qc_out": 1155, "total": 8365}, "cost_usd": 0.2395}}
{"question_id": "T1-F05", "tier": 1, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Tighnari is affiliated with Gandharva Ville (listed on his profile).", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter Tighnari", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Tighnari is affiliated with the Forest Rangers.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter Tighnari", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Tighnari holds the additional title of 'Avidya Forest Watcher'.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter Tighnari", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Tighnari's region is Sumeru.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter Tighnari", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Tighnari is a graduate of Amurta (one of the Akademiya darshans).", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter Tighnari", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Tighnari", "Forest Rangers", "Gandharva Ville", "Avidya Forest", "Sumeru"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Tighnari", "relation": "affiliated_with", "tail": "Forest Rangers", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter Tighnari"}, {"head": "Tighnari", "relation": "affiliated_with", "tail": "Gandharva Ville", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter Tighnari"}, {"head": "Tighnari", "relation": "title", "tail": "Avidya Forest Watcher", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter Tighnari"}, {"head": "Tighnari", "relation": "region", "tail": "Sumeru", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter Tighnari"}, {"head": "Tighnari", "relation": "graduated_from", "tail": "Amurta", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter Tighnari"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Confusing Tighnari's organization as the Akademiya or Amurta (he graduated from Amurta but his active affiliation is with the Forest Rangers).", "correct": "Tighnari is affiliated with the Forest Rangers and Gandharva Ville; Amurta is where he graduated from."}, {"trap": "Claiming Tighnari protects the Sumeru desert or all of Sumeru's wilderness.", "correct": "His title specifies him as the Avidya Forest Watcher, indicating he is associated with the Avidya Forest area within Sumeru. The document does not explicitly state a broader protective scope."}, {"trap": "Confusing Gandharva Ville with a broader organizational body such as the Akademiya.", "correct": "Gandharva Ville is listed as a separate affiliation on Tighnari's profile alongside the Forest Rangers; it is distinct from the Akademiya."}, {"trap": "Confusing Tighnari with Collei, another Forest Ranger character from Gandharva Ville, and attributing Collei's role or backstory to Tighnari.", "correct": "The document only describes Tighnari's affiliations; Collei is a different character not mentioned in the provided documents."}, {"trap": "Claiming Tighnari is the leader or founder of the Forest Rangers based on training memory rather than document evidence.", "correct": "The document only lists Forest Rangers as an affiliation. No rank or leadership role is stated in the provided text."}, {"trap": "Stating that Tighnari protects 'the rainforest' or 'Dharma Forest' instead of using the documented title referencing 'Avidya Forest'.", "correct": "The documented additional title is specifically 'Avidya Forest Watcher'. No other forest name is mentioned in the document."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "- The document clearly states Tighnari's affiliations (Gandharva Ville, Forest Rangers, Amurta graduate), his region (Sumeru), and his additional title (Avidya Forest Watcher).\n- 缺：文档中没有明确描述Tighnari在Forest Rangers中的具体职务或级别（如是否为领队/队长）。\n- 缺：文档中没有叙述性描述说明Tighnari'保护'某个区域，'保护'关系仅能从'Avidya Forest Watcher'这一称号间接推断。\n- 缺：文档中没有详细说明Forest Rangers的组织性质或职能范围。\n- 缺：文档中没有提及Amurta属于Akademiya的哪个学科方向，'one of the Akademiya darshans'这一说明来自常识推断而非文档原文，但文档确实将Amurta列为graduate来源。", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: - The document clearly states Tighnari's affiliations (Gandharva Ville, Forest Rangers, Amurta gradu"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T1-F05", "tier": 1, "question": "What organization does Tighnari belong to, and which region does he protect?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 2, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 2}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 2630, "oracle_out": 866, "qc_in": 3856, "qc_out": 1272, "total": 8624}, "cost_usd": 0.2576}}
{"question_id": "T1-F06", "tier": 1, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Eleazar was a chronic illness unique to Sumeru, which is a manifestation of The Withering on the human body.", "doc_source": "Eleazar", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Eleazar commonly presents as dark, hardened scales growing on a person's body, with slight numbness in the affected area, causing clumsiness. As it advances, patients experience fatigue and progressive nerve damage; scales develop into ulcers and eventually necrose, rendering patients immobile or comatose.", "doc_source": "Eleazar", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Eleazar is positively correlated with a person's elemental content; people with Eleazar have a higher elemental content than ordinary people.", "doc_source": "Eleazar", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Collei was born with Eleazar (she did not contract it later in life).", "doc_source": "Eleazar", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Collei was originally an Eleazar-afflicted victim of Fatui human experimentation.", "doc_source": "Collei", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Il Dottore and a subordinate in Sumeru suppressed Collei's Eleazar symptoms by infusing her with a god's remains (originally translated as archon residue), but this left her deeply traumatized and with unstable 'black fire' power and other plague-like symptoms.", "doc_source": "Eleazar", "verified": true}, {"fact": "After Cyno sealed the god's remains inside her body, the side effects (black fire and plague symptoms) disappeared, but her Eleazar symptoms reemerged, and she was taken to Tighnari at Gandharva Ville for care.", "doc_source": "Eleazar", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Eleazar was eradicated upon the cleansing of Greater Lord Rukkhadevata's tainted consciousness from Irminsul during the Archon Quest 'Where the Boat of Consciousness Lies' in Chapter III: Act V.", "doc_source": "Eleazar", "verified": true}, {"fact": "There was no true cure for Eleazar prior to its eradication, though it could be controlled by managing and reducing elemental quantities within the bodies of those affected.", "doc_source": "Eleazar", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Eleazar", "Collei", "The Withering", "Sumeru", "Il Dottore", "Fatui", "Cyno", "Tighnari", "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "Irminsul", "Gandharva Ville"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Eleazar", "relation": "is_manifestation_of", "tail": "The Withering", "doc_source": "Eleazar"}, {"head": "Eleazar", "relation": "unique_to_region", "tail": "Sumeru", "doc_source": "Eleazar"}, {"head": "Collei", "relation": "born_with_condition", "tail": "Eleazar", "doc_source": "Eleazar"}, {"head": "Collei", "relation": "victim_of_experimentation_by", "tail": "Fatui", "doc_source": "Collei"}, {"head": "Il Dottore", "relation": "suppressed_symptoms_of", "tail": "Collei", "doc_source": "Eleazar"}, {"head": "Cyno", "relation": "sealed_god_remains_inside", "tail": "Collei", "doc_source": "Eleazar"}, {"head": "Collei", "relation": "taken_for_care_to", "tail": "Gandharva Ville", "doc_source": "Eleazar"}, {"head": "Eleazar", "relation": "eradicated_by_cleansing_of", "tail": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "doc_source": "Eleazar"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Claiming Collei contracted Eleazar through Fatui experimentation or exposure to the Withering later in life.", "correct": "Collei was born with Eleazar; the Fatui experimented on her to treat/exploit her existing condition, not to cause it."}, {"trap": "Confusing the god's remains infusion as a cure for Eleazar.", "correct": "The god's remains suppressed Eleazar symptoms but introduced new side effects (black fire, plague symptoms); it was not a true cure."}, {"trap": "Claiming Cyno cured Collei's Eleazar.", "correct": "Cyno sealed the god's remains inside her, which resolved the side effects but caused her Eleazar symptoms to reemerge."}, {"trap": "Stating Eleazar is caused by forbidden knowledge directly.", "correct": "Eleazar is defined as a manifestation of The Withering on the human body, correlated with elemental content. Forbidden knowledge is linked to historical similar symptoms under King Deshret, but the document defines Eleazar specifically as a Withering manifestation."}, {"trap": "Confusing Collei's Eleazar with Dunyarzad's Eleazar and mixing up their treatment details.", "correct": "The documents describe Collei and Dunyarzad as both born with Eleazar, but their treatment histories are entirely different. Il Dottore's god's remains infusion and Cyno's sealing pertain only to Collei."}, {"trap": "Claiming Collei met Amber in Sumeru or that Amber helped treat her Eleazar.", "correct": "Per the Collei document, Collei met Amber in Mondstadt. The document does not attribute any Eleazar treatment to Amber."}, {"trap": "Stating that Tighnari cured Collei's Eleazar at Gandharva Ville.", "correct": "Collei was taken to Tighnari at Gandharva Ville for care due to reemergence of symptoms; the documents do not say Tighnari cured her. Eleazar was ultimately eradicated by the cleansing of Rukkhadevata's tainted consciousness from Irminsul."}, {"trap": "Claiming the unnamed doctor in the Eleazar diagnostic report is confirmed to be Il Dottore.", "correct": "The document says the unnamed doctor is 'likely Zandik, who is also heavily implied to be Il Dottore' — it is not stated as confirmed fact."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "- 缺：Collei先天患有Eleazar的具体生理/遗传机制，文档未解释为何某些人生来就患此病。\n- 缺：The Withering与先天性Eleazar之间的具体因果链条，文档仅笼统描述Eleazar是Withering在人体上的表现。\n- 缺：Collei在被Fatui实验前的早期生活细节（家庭背景、出生地等），文档未提供。\n- 缺：Collei的Eleazar在Irminsul净化后是否完全痊愈的明确确认，文档仅说Eleazar整体被根除。", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: - 缺：Collei先天患有Eleazar的具体生理/遗传机制，文档未解释为何某些人生来就患此病。\n- 缺：The Withering与先天性Eleazar之间的具体因果链条，文档仅笼统描述Eleaz"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T1-F06", "tier": 1, "question": "What is Eleazar disease that afflicted Collei, and how did she contract it?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 2, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 2}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 3169, "oracle_out": 1421, "qc_in": 4950, "qc_out": 1865, "total": 11405}, "cost_usd": 0.3682}}
{"question_id": "T1-F07", "tier": 1, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Collei is a trainee Forest Ranger in the Avidya Forest", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Collei", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Collei is a Dendro character", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Collei", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Cyno is the General Mahamatra who leads the Matra and oversees researchers of the Sumeru Akademiya", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Cyno", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Cyno is an Electro character", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Cyno", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Collei was originally an Eleazar-afflicted victim of Fatui human experimentation who wandered the world as a vagrant until she met Amber in Mondstadt", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Collei", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Both Collei and Cyno are characters associated with Sumeru", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Collei", "verified": false, "memory_source": true}], "required_entities": ["Collei", "Cyno", "Sumeru", "Avidya Forest", "Sumeru Akademiya", "Matra"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Collei", "relation": "affiliated_with", "tail": "Avidya Forest (Forest Ranger trainee)", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Collei"}, {"head": "Cyno", "relation": "leads", "tail": "Matra", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Cyno"}, {"head": "Cyno", "relation": "role_in", "tail": "Sumeru Akademiya (General Mahamatra)", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Cyno"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Claiming Cyno is Collei's mentor or teacher", "correct": "The provided documents do not describe any direct mentor-student relationship between Collei and Cyno. Collei's known connection in the documents is with Amber, not Cyno."}, {"trap": "Claiming Collei met Cyno in Mondstadt", "correct": "Collei met Amber in Mondstadt, not Cyno, according to the provided documents."}, {"trap": "Assuming Collei works under Cyno or the Matra", "correct": "Collei is a trainee Forest Ranger, not a member of the Matra. The documents do not establish a hierarchical relationship between them."}, {"trap": "Claiming Cyno helped rescue Collei from Fatui experiments alongside Lisa", "correct": "While this may be part of the broader game/manga lore, the provided documents only state that Collei was a victim of Fatui human experimentation and that she met Amber in Mondstadt. No mention of Cyno's involvement in her rescue is found in these documents."}, {"trap": "Confusing Collei's relationship with Cyno with her relationship with Tighnari (her actual Forest Ranger mentor)", "correct": "The provided documents do not mention Tighnari at all. Collei's role as trainee Forest Ranger is stated but her mentor is not identified in these documents."}, {"trap": "Assuming Cyno and Collei are both Akademiya-affiliated", "correct": "Cyno is associated with the Akademiya as General Mahamatra, but Collei is described only as a Forest Ranger trainee in Avidya Forest. No Akademiya affiliation for Collei is stated in the documents."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "缺：Collei与Cyno之间直接关系的任何描述（文档中完全未提及两人之间的互动、友谊、或故事联系）。缺：Cyno在Collei被Fatui实验过程中扮演的角色（漫画剧情中Cyno参与救助Collei的情节在文档中无任何记载）。缺：两人共同出现在须弥主线剧情中的具体场景和互动内容。缺：Collei的导师Tighnari的信息（文档未提及）。缺：Cyno与Collei是否为朋友关系的明确依据。总结：提供的文档仅包含两人各自的角色简介和数值信息，不包含任何关于两人关系的直接描述，因此本题无法从文档中获得充分验证的答案。", "_review_flags": ["key_facts[5]: verified=false — Both Collei and Cyno are characters associated with Sumeru", "coverage_notes: 缺：Collei与Cyno之间直接关系的任何描述（文档中完全未提及两人之间的互动、友谊、或故事联系）。缺：Cyno在Collei被Fatui实验过程中扮演的角色（漫画剧情中Cyno参与救助Collei"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T1-F07", "tier": 1, "question": "What is the relationship between Collei and Cyno?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 2, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 2}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 3942, "oracle_out": 877, "qc_in": 5180, "qc_out": 1237, "total": 11236}, "cost_usd": 0.2954}}
{"question_id": "T1-F08", "tier": 1, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "The Shogun is an artificial body (puppet) made by Ei, which now doubles as her current vessel.", "doc_source": "[NPC] The Shogun", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Shogun is the second puppet Ei created; the first was Scaramouche, whom she deemed a failure because he shed tears upon creation.", "doc_source": "[NPC] The Shogun", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Shogun has a consciousness of her own, separate from Ei's.", "doc_source": "[NPC] The Shogun", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Shogun was created with a set list of rules that cannot be altered or shut off.", "doc_source": "[NPC] The Shogun", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Ei does not see the Shogun as an entity separate from herself, claiming the Shogun counts as a different form of her existence and that she never intended to leave Inazuma in the hands of anybody but herself.", "doc_source": "[NPC] The Shogun", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Ei resides within the Plane of Euthymia, while the Shogun governs Inazuma as the external vessel.", "doc_source": "[NPC] The Shogun", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Shogun wields the Musou Isshin sword that houses Ei in battle.", "doc_source": "[NPC] The Shogun", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Shogun, having been designed to resist change, believed Ei was succumbing to erosion when Ei tried to change her views, and refused to comply with Ei's orders.", "doc_source": "[NPC] The Shogun", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Ei created the Shogun puppet because she wanted to create a body which could resist erosion.", "doc_source": "[NPC] The Shogun", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Ei", "The Shogun", "Raiden Shogun", "Plane of Euthymia", "Musou Isshin", "Scaramouche"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Ei", "relation": "created", "tail": "The Shogun", "doc_source": "[NPC] The Shogun"}, {"head": "The Shogun", "relation": "is_vessel_of", "tail": "Ei", "doc_source": "[NPC] The Shogun"}, {"head": "The Shogun", "relation": "has_own", "tail": "consciousness", "doc_source": "[NPC] The Shogun"}, {"head": "The Shogun", "relation": "wields", "tail": "Musou Isshin", "doc_source": "[NPC] The Shogun"}, {"head": "Ei", "relation": "resides_in", "tail": "Plane of Euthymia", "doc_source": "[NPC] The Shogun"}, {"head": "Ei", "relation": "previously_created", "tail": "Scaramouche", "doc_source": "[NPC] The Shogun"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Confusing Ei with Makoto (Ei's twin sister and the original Electro Archon). The document only mentions 'Makoto's consciousness' in passing but does not elaborate on Makoto's identity or role.", "correct": "The document does not describe Makoto's identity; only states Ei created the Shogun and resides in the Plane of Euthymia. Any details about Makoto being the original Archon come from training memory, not this document."}, {"trap": "Claiming the Shogun has no will or consciousness of her own and is purely remote-controlled by Ei.", "correct": "The Shogun has her own consciousness and a fixed set of rules; she even defied Ei's orders when she believed Ei was succumbing to erosion."}, {"trap": "Stating that Scaramouche was the successful puppet and the Shogun was the failure.", "correct": "Scaramouche was deemed a failure; the Shogun is the second and successful puppet."}, {"trap": "Claiming Ei's true name is Beelzebul or referring to her Archon name as established lore — the provided document never mentions the name Beelzebul.", "correct": "The document only refers to 'Ei' without giving her Archon name. Any reference to Beelzebul would come from training memory, not the provided source."}, {"trap": "Confusing the Shogun's execution technique Musou no Hitotachi with the sword Musou Isshin.", "correct": "Per the document, Musou Isshin is the sword that houses Ei; Musou no Hitotachi is the execution technique the Shogun uses (both are mentioned separately in the document)."}, {"trap": "Mixing up details from Nahida/Sumeru storylines (from the Moseis document) with Raiden Shogun/Inazuma details.", "correct": "The two documents cover entirely different regions and characters; they should not be conflated."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "缺：Ei的完整个人背景资料（如她的神之名Beelzebul、与Makoto的具体关系），文档仅提及Makoto的意识但未解释其身份。缺：Ei作为雷神的具体职责和身份描述，文档未提供Ei的专属资料页。缺：五百年决斗的最终结果，文档文本在描述该事件时被截断。缺：'Raiden Shogun'这一称号的完整解释——文档标题为'The Shogun'，文中未明确使用'Raiden Shogun'一词来描述两个身份的统称。缺：Ei为何要追求永恒的完整动机说明。", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: 缺：Ei的完整个人背景资料（如她的神之名Beelzebul、与Makoto的具体关系），文档仅提及Makoto的意识但未解释其身份。缺：Ei作为雷神的具体职责和身份描述，文档未提供Ei的专属资料页。缺"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T1-F08", "tier": 1, "question": "What are the two identities of the Raiden Shogun (Ei), and how do they differ?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 2, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 2}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 2484, "oracle_out": 1164, "qc_in": 4008, "qc_out": 1569, "total": 9225}, "cost_usd": 0.3024}}
{"question_id": "T1-F09", "tier": 1, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Dori is the owner of The Palace of Alcazarzaray.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Dori", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Dori is a merchant of high regard, known by the title 'Lord Sangemah Bay'.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Dori", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Dori is well known for her ability to obtain anything a person needs, as long as they have enough Mora to afford her jaw-dropping prices.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Dori", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Dori's full name is Dori Sangemah Bay.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Dori", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Dori", "The Palace of Alcazarzaray", "Lord Sangemah Bay", "Mora"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Dori", "relation": "owns", "tail": "The Palace of Alcazarzaray", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Dori"}, {"head": "Dori", "relation": "known_as", "tail": "Lord Sangemah Bay", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Dori"}, {"head": "Dori", "relation": "occupation", "tail": "merchant", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Dori"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Claiming Dori specializes in specific goods such as weapons, artifacts, Vision-related items, or potions.", "correct": "The document only states she can obtain 'anything a person needs' — no specific categories of goods are mentioned."}, {"trap": "Describing The Palace of Alcazarzaray as a shop, marketplace, or trading hub with specific functions.", "correct": "The document only identifies it as something Dori owns; it does not specify its exact function or nature beyond that."}, {"trap": "Confusing Dori's business with the Sumeru Akademiya or other Sumeru institutions, or claiming she has ties to the Akademiya.", "correct": "No affiliation with the Akademiya or any other institution is mentioned in the provided document."}, {"trap": "Attributing details from other Sumeru merchants (e.g., Dehya's mercenary work, Kaveh's architectural involvement with Alcazarzaray, or Alhaitham's connections) to Dori's trade activities.", "correct": "The document only describes Dori herself as a merchant who can obtain anything for the right price; no other characters or their roles are mentioned."}, {"trap": "Claiming Dori runs a 'business empire' with multiple branches, employees, or a trade network.", "correct": "The document does not describe the scale or structure of her business beyond calling her 'a merchant of high regard' and owner of The Palace of Alcazarzaray."}, {"trap": "Stating that Dori trades in Visions, illegal goods, or black-market items based on community lore or in-game quests not present in this document.", "correct": "The provided document makes no mention of Visions, illegal goods, or black-market trading. Only the general statement about obtaining 'anything' is present."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "缺：Dori具体交易的商品类别——文档仅笼统提到她能获取'anything a person needs'，无具体商品信息。\n缺：Dori商业活动的规模、结构、员工或合作伙伴信息——文档未提及。\n缺：The Palace of Alcazarzaray的具体性质和功能——文档仅说明Dori是其owner，未描述其用途。\n缺：Dori的贸易路线、客户群体、经营方式等详细商业信息——文档未提及。\n缺：Dori与其他角色（如Kaveh）或组织的商业关系——文档未涉及任何其他角色。\n总结：题目询问'business empire'和'kinds of goods'，但文档仅提供高层角色简介，无法给出详细答案。", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: 缺：Dori具体交易的商品类别——文档仅笼统提到她能获取'anything a person needs'，无具体商品信息。\n缺：Dori商业活动的规模、结构、员工或合作伙伴信息——文档未提及。\n缺："], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T1-F09", "tier": 1, "question": "What is Dori's business empire, and what kinds of goods does she trade?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 1, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 1}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 2238, "oracle_out": 727, "qc_in": 3325, "qc_out": 1133, "total": 7423}, "cost_usd": 0.2229}}
{"question_id": "T1-F10", "tier": 1, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata was the original Dendro Archon of Sumeru and held the title of God of Wisdom.", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "verified": true}, {"fact": "She was also known as Queen Aranyani by the Aranara and was the avatar of Irminsul.", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "verified": true}, {"fact": "She was one of 'The Three Eternal Companion-Gods' who co-reigned in Sumeru alongside King Deshret and Nabu Malikata.", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "verified": true}, {"fact": "During the cataclysm 500 years ago, Greater Lord Rukkhadevata was one of the casualties of the conflict.", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Before her death, she created the Akasha System to purge forbidden knowledge from Irminsul and created her next incarnation, Lesser Lord Kusanali.", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Lesser Lord Kusanali then ascended as the current Dendro Archon and God of Wisdom, succeeding Rukkhadevata.", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "verified": true}, {"fact": "At the end of the Sumeru Archon Quests, Rukkhadevata sacrificed herself by having Lesser Lord Kusanali remove all memories of her existence from Teyvat.", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The only known person to still clearly remember her is the Traveler, because they are not from Teyvat and their memories are not under Irminsul's jurisdiction.", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "Sumeru", "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "Irminsul", "King Deshret", "Nabu Malikata", "Akasha System", "Traveler"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "relation": "held_title", "tail": "Dendro Archon / God of Wisdom", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata"}, {"head": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "relation": "avatar_of", "tail": "Irminsul", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata"}, {"head": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "relation": "co-reigned_with", "tail": "King Deshret", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata"}, {"head": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "relation": "co-reigned_with", "tail": "Nabu Malikata", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata"}, {"head": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "relation": "predecessor_of", "tail": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata"}, {"head": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "relation": "created", "tail": "Akasha System", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata"}, {"head": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "relation": "created_incarnation", "tail": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata"}, {"head": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "relation": "erased_memories_of", "tail": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata"}, {"head": "Traveler", "relation": "retains_memory_of", "tail": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Confusing Greater Lord Rukkhadevata with Lesser Lord Kusanali (Nahida) as the same active archon.", "correct": "Rukkhadevata was the original Dendro Archon who perished; Kusanali is her successor and next incarnation."}, {"trap": "Claiming Rukkhadevata was simply killed during the cataclysm with no further fate.", "correct": "Beyond her death during the cataclysm, her ultimate fate was a deliberate self-sacrifice: she had Kusanali erase all memories of her from Teyvat via Irminsul at the end of the Sumeru Archon Quests."}, {"trap": "Stating that no one remembers Rukkhadevata at all.", "correct": "The Traveler still remembers her because they are not from Teyvat and their memories are outside Irminsul's jurisdiction."}, {"trap": "Confusing Nabu Malikata (Goddess of Flowers) with Rukkhadevata.", "correct": "They were separate companion-gods; Nabu Malikata foresaw the cataclysm and entrusted part of herself to Rukkhadevata before her own death."}, {"trap": "Claiming Rukkhadevata turned against Celestia together with King Deshret and Nabu Malikata.", "correct": "Per the document, when the other two gods propagated a plan to turn against Celestia, Rukkhadevata chose NOT to stay by their sides and instead established her own territory by nurturing a rainforest."}, {"trap": "Claiming the memory erasure was performed by Rukkhadevata herself rather than by Kusanali at Rukkhadevata's behest.", "correct": "The document states Rukkhadevata sacrificed herself by having Lesser Lord Kusanali remove all memories of her existence from Teyvat."}, {"trap": "Conflating Rukkhadevata's role as 'avatar of Irminsul' with being Irminsul itself.", "correct": "The document describes her as 'the avatar of Irminsul,' not Irminsul itself."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "- 缺：Rukkhadevata具体如何诞生的细节（文档仅提及'It is unknown when or how Greater Lord Rukkhadevata came into being'）\n- 缺：记忆消除的具体机制和过程细节（文档仅概述了结果，未提供详细叙事）\n- 缺：灾变期间Rukkhadevata具体战斗或行动的详细经过（文档中该段落被截断）\n- 核心问题所需的身份信息和最终命运信息在文档中充分覆盖", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: - 缺：Rukkhadevata具体如何诞生的细节（文档仅提及'It is unknown when or how Greater Lord Rukkhadevata came into being'"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T1-F10", "tier": 1, "question": "Who was the Greater Lord Rukkhadevata of Sumeru, and what was her ultimate fate?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 3, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 3}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 2933, "oracle_out": 1469, "qc_in": 4762, "qc_out": 1801, "total": 10965}, "cost_usd": 0.3607}}
{"question_id": "T2-R01", "tier": 2, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Kaveh is the architect behind the Palace of Alcazarzaray.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Kaveh", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Kaveh was a student of the Kshahrewar Darshan of the Sumeru Akademiya and graduated with honors, earning the moniker 'Light of Kshahrewar.'", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Kaveh", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Kaveh became insolvent (financially ruined) after the construction of the Palace of Alcazarzaray.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Kaveh", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Due to his insolvency, Kaveh was forced to reside with Alhaitham.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Kaveh", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Kaveh has a complicated relationship with Alhaitham.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Kaveh", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Alhaitham is a member of the Haravatat of the Sumeru Akademiya and serves as the Akademiya's Scribe.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Alhaitham", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Kaveh is often saddled with guilt for his father's death, ashamed of his poverty, and struggling with realizing his ideals.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Kaveh", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Kaveh", "Alhaitham", "Palace of Alcazarzaray", "Kshahrewar", "Sumeru Akademiya"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Kaveh", "relation": "designed/built", "tail": "Palace of Alcazarzaray", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Kaveh"}, {"head": "Kaveh", "relation": "became insolvent due to", "tail": "Palace of Alcazarzaray", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Kaveh"}, {"head": "Kaveh", "relation": "forced to reside with", "tail": "Alhaitham", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Kaveh"}, {"head": "Kaveh", "relation": "has complicated relationship with", "tail": "Alhaitham", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Kaveh"}, {"head": "Kaveh", "relation": "graduated from (Darshan)", "tail": "Kshahrewar", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Kaveh"}, {"head": "Alhaitham", "relation": "member of (Darshan)", "tail": "Haravatat", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Alhaitham"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Claiming Kaveh and Alhaitham are from the same Darshan of the Akademiya.", "correct": "Kaveh is from Kshahrewar while Alhaitham is from Haravatat; they belong to different Darshans."}, {"trap": "Claiming Kaveh lives with Alhaitham by choice or due to friendship.", "correct": "Kaveh was forced to reside with Alhaitham because he became insolvent after constructing the Palace of Alcazarzaray."}, {"trap": "Claiming Kaveh and Alhaitham have a straightforwardly friendly or hostile relationship.", "correct": "The document describes their relationship as 'complicated.'"}, {"trap": "Claiming the Palace of Alcazarzaray belongs to Kaveh.", "correct": "Kaveh was the architect who designed/built it, but he went bankrupt in the process and does not own it."}, {"trap": "Claiming Kaveh and Alhaitham were classmates or studied together at the Akademiya.", "correct": "The documents only state Kaveh was from Kshahrewar and Alhaitham from Haravatat; no mention of them being classmates is found in the provided documents."}, {"trap": "Confusing Kaveh with Cyno or other Akademiya-related characters and their relationships to Alhaitham.", "correct": "Only Kaveh is described as residing with Alhaitham due to insolvency in the provided documents."}, {"trap": "Claiming that Alhaitham invited Kaveh to live with him out of kindness or that there is a specific stated reason for Alhaitham's acceptance.", "correct": "The documents only state Kaveh was 'forced to reside with Alhaitham'; no details about Alhaitham's motivation or the terms of the arrangement are provided."}, {"trap": "Claiming that the house they share belongs to Kaveh.", "correct": "The documents imply Kaveh moved in with Alhaitham (not the other way around) due to Kaveh's insolvency, suggesting it is Alhaitham's residence."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "- 缺：Kaveh与Alhaitham之间'complicated relationship'的具体性质和历史背景（如是否曾是同学、是否有理念冲突等），提供的文档中无详细说明。\n- 缺：Alhaitham为何同意让Kaveh同住的具体原因或条件，文档中未提及。\n- 缺：他们共住房屋的所有权归属，文档仅暗示Kaveh搬入Alhaitham处，但未明确说明房屋属于谁。\n- 缺：Palace of Alcazarzaray的委托方（Dori）等背景信息，文档中未提及导致Kaveh破产的具体财务细节。\n- 缺：Kaveh父亲去世的具体经过以及与Alhaitham关系的关联，文档仅提及Kaveh因父亲之死感到愧疚。", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: - 缺：Kaveh与Alhaitham之间'complicated relationship'的具体性质和历史背景（如是否曾是同学、是否有理念冲突等），提供的文档中无详细说明。\n- 缺：Alhaith"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T2-R01", "tier": 2, "question": "What is the relationship between Kaveh and Alhaitham, and why do they share a house?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 2, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 2}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 3849, "oracle_out": 1141, "qc_in": 5350, "qc_out": 1588, "total": 11928}, "cost_usd": 0.3427}}
{"question_id": "T2-R02", "tier": 2, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Scaramouche is a puppet created by Raiden Ei.", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Scaramouche was the Sixth of the Eleven Fatui Harbingers, with the codename 'The Balladeer'.", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "After obtaining Ei's Gnosis (negotiated by Yae Miko), Scaramouche cut off contact with the Fatui.", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "With Dottore's assistance and the Sumeru Akademiya sages, Scaramouche was to be ascended into a new God of Wisdom under the name 'Shouki no Kami, the Prodigal', powered by the Electro Gnosis.", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "After his defeat, Scaramouche erased his existence from Irminsul and became the Wanderer.", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Wanderer came into existence in place of his previous incarnation after the latter expunged his previous appellations and their respective histories from Irminsul.", "doc_source": "[PlayableCharacter] Wanderer", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Wanderer", "Scaramouche", "Raiden Ei", "Yae Miko", "Electro Gnosis", "Fatui Harbingers"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Raiden Ei", "relation": "created (as puppet)", "tail": "Scaramouche", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Scaramouche", "relation": "obtained Gnosis from", "tail": "Raiden Ei (via Yae Miko)", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Scaramouche", "relation": "became", "tail": "Wanderer", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Confusing Raiden Ei (the creator of Scaramouche) with the Raiden Shogun (the puppet currently serving as Archon). Scaramouche was created by Raiden Ei, not by the Raiden Shogun puppet.", "correct": "The document states Scaramouche is 'a puppet created by Raiden Ei.' The Raiden Shogun puppet and Scaramouche are both creations of Ei."}, {"trap": "Claiming Scaramouche stole the Gnosis by force.", "correct": "Yae Miko offered Ei's Gnosis to Scaramouche as part of a negotiation for the Traveler's safety, and he accepted."}, {"trap": "Stating that Scaramouche erased himself from existence entirely.", "correct": "He erased his previous appellations and their respective histories from Irminsul, then continued to exist as the Wanderer."}, {"trap": "Claiming Scaramouche was Raiden Ei's 'son' or 'sibling' in a familial sense.", "correct": "The documents only state he is 'a puppet created by Raiden Ei.' No familial relationship terminology is used in the provided documents."}, {"trap": "Confusing Scaramouche with the Raiden Shogun puppet that currently governs Inazuma. Both are puppets created by Ei but serve different roles.", "correct": "Scaramouche is a distinct puppet from the Raiden Shogun. The documents describe Scaramouche as a Harbinger who later became the Wanderer, not as the governing puppet of Inazuma."}, {"trap": "Stating that Scaramouche was abandoned because he could cry or had emotions, a common lore claim from training data.", "correct": "The provided documents do not mention any reason why Scaramouche was separated from Raiden Ei or why he was not used as intended. This detail is absent from the reference documents.", "memory_source": true}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "缺：Raiden Ei创造Scaramouche的原始目的（文档未提及）；缺：Scaramouche为何被Ei抛弃/遗弃的原因（文档未提及）；缺：Scaramouche与Ei之间的情感联系或互动细节（文档未提及）；缺：Raiden Shogun（统治稻妻的傀儡）与Scaramouche之间的对比或关系说明（文档未提及）；缺：Tatarasuna事件的完整内容（文档仅简略提及Dottore策划了Scaramouche的第二次'背叛'，文本被截断）", "_review_flags": ["key_facts[1]: high-risk pattern — Scaramouche was the Sixth of the Eleven Fatui Harbingers, wi", "coverage_notes: 缺：Raiden Ei创造Scaramouche的原始目的（文档未提及）；缺：Scaramouche为何被Ei抛弃/遗弃的原因（文档未提及）；缺：Scaramouche与Ei之间的情感联系或互动细节（"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T2-R02", "tier": 2, "question": "What is the connection between the Wanderer (Scaramouche) and the Raiden Shogun?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 3, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 3}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 4053, "oracle_out": 1041, "qc_in": 5454, "qc_out": 1325, "total": 11873}, "cost_usd": 0.3201}}
{"question_id": "T2-R03", "tier": 2, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Alhaitham holds the position of Scribe in the Sumeru Akademiya.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter: Alhaitham", "verified": true}, {"fact": "As the Scribe, Alhaitham is responsible for documenting the Akademiya's findings and drafting ordinances.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter: Alhaitham", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Alhaitham is a member of the Haravatat, one of the darshans of the Sumeru Akademiya.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter: Alhaitham", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Despite his brilliance and egocentricity, Alhaitham is unwilling to aspire for higher office in the Akademiya.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter: Alhaitham", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Akademiya is led by Lesser Lord Kusanali and the Six Great Sages.", "doc_source": "Concept: Akademiya", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Alhaitham", "Sumeru Akademiya", "Scribe", "Haravatat", "Six Great Sages", "Lesser Lord Kusanali"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Alhaitham", "relation": "holds_position", "tail": "Scribe of the Akademiya", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter: Alhaitham"}, {"head": "Alhaitham", "relation": "member_of", "tail": "Haravatat", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter: Alhaitham"}, {"head": "Sumeru Akademiya", "relation": "led_by", "tail": "Lesser Lord Kusanali and Six Great Sages", "doc_source": "Concept: Akademiya"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Claiming Alhaitham is one of the Six Great Sages or holds a sage-level position.", "correct": "Alhaitham is the Scribe, not a Sage. He is explicitly noted as unwilling to aspire for higher office despite his brilliance."}, {"trap": "Claiming the Scribe position gives Alhaitham direct authority over or equal standing with the Grand Sages.", "correct": "The provided documents do not specify a direct hierarchical relationship between the Scribe and the Grand Sages. The Scribe's role is documented as recording findings and drafting ordinances."}, {"trap": "Confusing Alhaitham's role as Scribe with that of Acting Grand Sage, a role he temporarily held during the Sumeru Archon Quest.", "correct": "The reference documents only mention his position as Scribe; any claim of Acting Grand Sage is not supported by the provided documents."}, {"trap": "Confusing the title 'Grand Sage' with 'Great Sage' or using these interchangeably.", "correct": "The provided documents refer to the 'Six Great Sages' as leaders of the Akademiya. The term 'Grand Sage' does not appear in the provided documents; models may import this term from training data."}, {"trap": "Attributing details from Kaveh's or other Haravatat members' lore to Alhaitham.", "correct": "Kaveh is mentioned in the Akademiya document as an early enrollee but his details should not be confused with Alhaitham's role or authority."}, {"trap": "Claiming the Matra reports to Alhaitham or that the Scribe commands the Matra.", "correct": "The Matra is listed as a subordinate faction of the Akademiya overall, not specifically under the Scribe. No such relationship is stated in the documents."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "- 缺：Scribe 职位在 Akademiya 治理架构中的具体层级地位（是否属于高层决策层、是否参与六大贤者的会议等）\n- 缺：Scribe 与 Six Great Sages 之间明确的上下级关系或权力对比\n- 缺：Alhaitham 在魔神任务中临时担任代理大贤者（Acting Grand Sage）的相关信息，文档中完全未提及\n- 缺：Scribe 职位是否为独立职位还是隶属于某个特定的 darshan 的说明\n- 缺：'Grand Sage' 这一称谓在文档中未出现，题目中的 'Grand Sages' 一词可能来自游戏剧情但在所提供文档中无直接依据（文档仅提及 'Six Great Sages'）", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: - 缺：Scribe 职位在 Akademiya 治理架构中的具体层级地位（是否属于高层决策层、是否参与六大贤者的会议等）\n- 缺：Scribe 与 Six Great Sages 之间明确的上下级关"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T2-R03", "tier": 2, "question": "What position does Alhaitham hold in the Akademiya, and how does his authority relate to the Grand Sages?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 3, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 3}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 3331, "oracle_out": 938, "qc_in": 4629, "qc_out": 1270, "total": 10168}, "cost_usd": 0.285}}
{"question_id": "T2-R04", "tier": 2, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Nilou is a dancer under the Zubayr Theater.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Nilou", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Zubayr Theater is located in the Grand Bazaar, which is a subpoint of interest within Sumeru City.", "doc_source": "Location - Sumeru City", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Sumeru City is known across Teyvat as the 'City of Wisdom.'", "doc_source": "Location - Sumeru City", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Grand Bazaar is known as a lively, artistic space, filled with merchants selling handmade products.", "doc_source": "Location - Sumeru City", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Nilou has a Story Quest called 'Lotos Somno Chapter, Act I: To the Wise' which takes place in Sumeru City, including a quest named 'The Warm Rhythm of the Streets'.", "doc_source": "Location - Sumeru City", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Nilou's dancing is described as elegant and graceful; outside the stage's spotlight, she is warm, smiling, and friendly.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Nilou", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Nilou", "Sumeru City", "Zubayr Theater", "Grand Bazaar"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Nilou", "relation": "works at", "tail": "Zubayr Theater", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Nilou"}, {"head": "Zubayr Theater", "relation": "located in", "tail": "Grand Bazaar", "doc_source": "Location - Sumeru City"}, {"head": "Grand Bazaar", "relation": "subarea of", "tail": "Sumeru City", "doc_source": "Location - Sumeru City"}, {"head": "Nilou", "relation": "has Story Quest in", "tail": "Sumeru City", "doc_source": "Location - Sumeru City"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Claiming Nilou is affiliated with the Sumeru Akademiya or is a scholar.", "correct": "Nilou is a dancer under the Zubayr Theater, not an Akademiya scholar."}, {"trap": "Claiming the Zubayr Theater is a standalone location separate from the Grand Bazaar.", "correct": "The Zubayr Theater is listed as a subpoint of interest under the Grand Bazaar in Sumeru City."}, {"trap": "Confusing the Grand Bazaar's cultural/artistic identity with the Akademiya's scholarly focus.", "correct": "The Grand Bazaar is described as a lively, artistic space with ordinary people, while the Akademiya is the scholarly institution."}, {"trap": "Claiming Nilou performs at or is connected to Lambad's Tavern or Puspa Café instead of the Zubayr Theater.", "correct": "The documents only state Nilou is a dancer under the Zubayr Theater. Lambad's Tavern and Puspa Café are separate points of interest."}, {"trap": "Attributing details from other Sumeru characters (e.g., Kaveh, Alhaitham, Layla) to Nilou's cultural role.", "correct": "The documents only describe Nilou as a dancer at the Zubayr Theater; other characters have distinct affiliations."}, {"trap": "Claiming Nilou has a direct role in the Sabzeruz Festival based on training memory.", "correct": "The provided documents list Sabzeruz Festival quests under Sumeru City but do not explicitly state Nilou's participation in the festival."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "- 缺：Nilou与须弥传统舞蹈文化的深层背景（文档仅说她是Zubayr Theater舞者，未阐述舞蹈在须弥文化中的地位）\n- 缺：Nilou与Sabzeruz Festival的具体关联（文档列出了节日任务但未明确提及Nilou参与）\n- 缺：Nilou在Grand Bazaar民间文化生活中的具体角色描述\n- 缺：Zubayr Theater本身的文化定位描述（文档仅将其列为Grand Bazaar子地点，无进一步说明）\n- 缺：Nilou Story Quest（Lotos Somno Chapter）的具体剧情内容，无法从文档确认其与须弥文化的更深层关联", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: - 缺：Nilou与须弥传统舞蹈文化的深层背景（文档仅说她是Zubayr Theater舞者，未阐述舞蹈在须弥文化中的地位）\n- 缺：Nilou与Sabzeruz Festival的具体关联（文档列出"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T2-R04", "tier": 2, "question": "What is the cultural connection between Nilou and Sumeru City?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 2, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 2}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 3567, "oracle_out": 902, "qc_in": 4829, "qc_out": 1233, "total": 10531}, "cost_usd": 0.2861}}
{"question_id": "T2-R05", "tier": 2, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Dottore is the Second of the Eleven Fatui Harbingers, making the Fatui a primary organization involved in his operations in Sumeru.", "doc_source": "NPC - Dottore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Dottore is revealed to be working with the sages of Sumeru Akademiya during Archon Quest Chapter III: Act III.", "doc_source": "NPC - Dottore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Dottore was formerly a student/researcher at Sumeru Akademiya before being expelled for murdering Sohreh and crossing moral boundaries in his Eleazar research.", "doc_source": "NPC - Dottore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Dottore researched ways to weaponize forbidden knowledge via The Withering and Eleazar, and sought to utilize the power of dreams to elevate humanity's cognitive abilities.", "doc_source": "NPC - Dottore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Dottore's operations involved Lesser Lord Kusanali, who coerced one of his segments into erasing the other segments in exchange for the Electro Gnosis.", "doc_source": "NPC - Dottore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Pantalone, another Harbinger who seeks to 'overthrow the natural imbalance between gods and humans,' works closely with Dottore.", "doc_source": "NPC - Dottore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "A Fatui division under a superior officer was operating in Sumeru, dealing with rogue agent Elchingen, with the Akademiya handling Elchingen's transfer to prison.", "doc_source": "Mysterious Fatui Letter", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Akademiya functions as both Sumeru's main governing body and its most prestigious institute of learning, led by Lesser Lord Kusanali and the Six Great Sages.", "doc_source": "Akademiya", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Dottore", "Fatui", "Eleven Fatui Harbingers", "Sumeru Akademiya", "Sages of Sumeru Akademiya", "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "Pantalone", "Collei", "Scaramouche"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Dottore", "relation": "member_of", "tail": "Eleven Fatui Harbingers", "doc_source": "NPC - Dottore"}, {"head": "Dottore", "relation": "collaborated_with", "tail": "Sages of Sumeru Akademiya", "doc_source": "NPC - Dottore"}, {"head": "Dottore", "relation": "expelled_from", "tail": "Sumeru Akademiya", "doc_source": "NPC - Dottore"}, {"head": "Dottore", "relation": "negotiated_with", "tail": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "doc_source": "NPC - Dottore"}, {"head": "Pantalone", "relation": "works_closely_with", "tail": "Dottore", "doc_source": "NPC - Dottore"}, {"head": "Dottore", "relation": "experimented_on", "tail": "Collei", "doc_source": "NPC - Dottore"}, {"head": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "relation": "leader_of", "tail": "Sumeru Akademiya", "doc_source": "Akademiya"}, {"head": "Fatui", "relation": "operated_in", "tail": "Sumeru", "doc_source": "Mysterious Fatui Letter"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Confusing Dottore's collaboration with the Akademiya sages as an official Akademiya-sanctioned operation rather than a covert alliance with corrupt sages.", "correct": "Dottore worked with the sages of Sumeru Akademiya, but he had previously been expelled from the Akademiya; the documents say he worked with 'the sages' but do not specify whether this was officially sanctioned or a corrupt faction."}, {"trap": "Claiming Dottore obtained the Dendro Gnosis from Lesser Lord Kusanali.", "correct": "Dottore's segment received the Electro Gnosis from Lesser Lord Kusanali in exchange for erasing his other segments."}, {"trap": "Attributing Scaramouche's creation to events in Sumeru.", "correct": "Dottore's experiment on the kabukimono occurred at Tatarasuna (Inazuma), not in Sumeru. The documents mention this in the context of Dottore's overall character, not his Sumeru operations."}, {"trap": "Naming specific sages such as Azar or the Grand Sage as documented collaborators of Dottore.", "correct": "The provided documents only refer to 'the sages of Sumeru Akademiya' generically without naming specific individuals like Azar. Any specific sage names would come from training memory, not from these documents."}, {"trap": "Confusing the Matra (Akademiya's subordinate enforcement faction) as directly involved in Dottore's operations.", "correct": "The documents list Matra as a subordinate faction of the Akademiya but do not explicitly connect Matra to Dottore's operations."}, {"trap": "Claiming the Eremites were involved in Dottore's operations in Sumeru.", "correct": "The Sumeru document mentions Eremites as a mercenary faction in Sumeru, but no document links them to Dottore's specific operations."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "缺：具体哪些贤者（sages）与Dottore合作的姓名，文档中未提及（如Azar等名字）。\n缺：Dottore在须弥操控Samsara/梦境（Sabzeruz Festival循环）的具体细节，文档中未详述。\n缺：Dottore在须弥与愚人众其他具体下属或分队的协作细节。\n缺：Dottore利用Akasha系统的具体操作方式，文档中未提及Akasha。\n缺：Dottore与散兵（Scaramouche/Wanderer）在须弥的对峙细节，文档仅提及散兵与Dottore断绝关系并发誓报仇，但未说明具体发生在须弥的情节。", "_review_flags": ["key_facts[0]: high-risk pattern — Dottore is the Second of the Eleven Fatui Harbingers, making", "key_facts[5]: high-risk pattern — Pantalone, another Harbinger who seeks to 'overthrow the nat", "coverage_notes: 缺：具体哪些贤者（sages）与Dottore合作的姓名，文档中未提及（如Azar等名字）。\n缺：Dottore在须弥操控Samsara/梦境（Sabzeruz Festival循环）的具体细节，文档"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T2-R05", "tier": 2, "question": "Which organizations and entities were involved in Dottore's operations in Sumeru?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 4, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 4}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 3934, "oracle_out": 1338, "qc_in": 5633, "qc_out": 1721, "total": 12626}, "cost_usd": 0.3729}}
{"question_id": "T2-R06", "tier": 2, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Cyno is the General Mahamatra, leading the Matra.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Cyno", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Matra are disciplinary officers for Sumeru Akademiya.", "doc_source": "Matra", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Matra serve as an executive branch and enforce the Akademiya's academic integrity.", "doc_source": "Matra", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Matra hand out disciplinary actions to researchers who have committed serious academic offenses, such as plagiarism or misappropriation of funds.", "doc_source": "Matra", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Matra are also the authority responsible for controls regarding Knowledge Capsules transactions, and apply a specific seal on goods that have passed their inspection.", "doc_source": "Matra", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Matra's leaders include the Sumeru Akademiya Sages and Cyno (General Mahamatra).", "doc_source": "Matra", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Cyno", "General Mahamatra", "Matra", "Sumeru Akademiya"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Cyno", "relation": "holds_title", "tail": "General Mahamatra", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Cyno"}, {"head": "Cyno", "relation": "leads", "tail": "Matra", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Cyno"}, {"head": "Matra", "relation": "serves_as_disciplinary_officers_for", "tail": "Sumeru Akademiya", "doc_source": "Matra"}, {"head": "Matra", "relation": "enforces", "tail": "academic integrity of Sumeru Akademiya", "doc_source": "Matra"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Confusing the Matra with the Mahamatra — the Mahamatra is explicitly comprised of Akademiya alumni, while this is unclear for the Matra.", "correct": "The Matra are the disciplinary officers; the Mahamatra is a related but distinct group explicitly composed of Akademiya alumni."}, {"trap": "Stating that Cyno is a renowned researcher at the Akademiya.", "correct": "A message on the Akademiya Public Message Board criticizes that Cyno is not a renowned researcher."}, {"trap": "Claiming Cyno works for the Knights of Favonius or another nation's institution rather than Sumeru Akademiya.", "correct": "Cyno serves Sumeru Akademiya as General Mahamatra."}, {"trap": "Describing the Matra as a judicial or legislative body rather than an executive/disciplinary branch.", "correct": "The document explicitly states the Matra serve as an executive branch enforcing academic integrity, not a judicial or legislative body."}, {"trap": "Conflating Cyno's role with that of the Sumeru Akademiya Sages, who are also listed as leaders of the Matra.", "correct": "Cyno leads the Matra as General Mahamatra, but the Sages are separately listed as leaders above the Matra as well."}, {"trap": "Stating that the General Mahamatra title historically belongs to Haravatat or another darshan, when the document says the previous General Mahamatra was from Rtawahist.", "correct": "The document indicates the previous General Mahamatra graduated from Rtawahist, not another darshan."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "none — The provided documents fully cover: (1) Cyno's title as General Mahamatra, (2) his association with Sumeru Akademiya via the Matra, and (3) the Matra's function as disciplinary officers enforcing academic integrity. No information gaps for this question.", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: none — The provided documents fully cover: (1) Cyno's title as General Mahamatra, (2) his associatio"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T2-R06", "tier": 2, "question": "Which institution is Cyno the General Mahamatra of, and what is that institution's function?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 2, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 2}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 2894, "oracle_out": 772, "qc_in": 4027, "qc_out": 1047, "total": 8740}, "cost_usd": 0.2402}}
{"question_id": "T2-R07", "tier": 2, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Nahida is a playable Dendro character in Genshin Impact.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Nahida", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Nahida holds the title 'Lesser Lord Kusanali'.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Nahida", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Nahida was confined extensively in the Sanctuary of Surasthana before being freed.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Nahida", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Nahida strives to have a stronger presence in Sumeru now that she has been freed.", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Nahida", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Nahida's Story Quest is called Sapientia Oromasdis Chapter: Act I - Lingering Warmth.", "doc_source": "NPC - Ata", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Nahida", "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "Sumeru", "Sanctuary of Surasthana"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Nahida", "relation": "title/identity", "tail": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Nahida"}, {"head": "Nahida", "relation": "confined_in", "tail": "Sanctuary of Surasthana", "doc_source": "PlayableCharacter - Nahida"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Claiming the provided documents explicitly describe Nahida as a reincarnation or offshoot of Greater Lord Rukkhadevata.", "correct": "The provided documents do NOT mention Greater Lord Rukkhadevata at all, nor do they describe any lineage or relationship between Nahida and Rukkhadevata. Any such claim would be based on external knowledge, not these documents."}, {"trap": "Assuming the title 'Lesser Lord' implies a direct hierarchical subordination or lineage to a 'Greater Lord' based solely on these documents.", "correct": "The documents only state that Nahida is 'Lesser Lord Kusanali'; no connection to a 'Greater Lord' figure is established in the provided text."}, {"trap": "Confusing Nahida's relationship with Rukkhadevata with other Archon succession stories, such as Raiden Ei and Makoto in Inazuma, or Zhongli stepping down in Liyue.", "correct": "Each Archon's succession or origin story is distinct. The documents here provide no details about any Archon succession involving Nahida."}, {"trap": "Claiming Nahida was 'born from' or 'created by' Irminsul based on these documents.", "correct": "The provided documents make no mention of Irminsul, nor any mechanism of Nahida's birth or creation."}, {"trap": "Stating that Rukkhadevata sacrificed herself or was erased from Irminsul and citing these documents as the source.", "correct": "No such events are described or even referenced in the provided documents. This information, while potentially accurate from game lore, cannot be verified from the given text."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "The provided documents are severely insufficient to answer this question. Specific information gaps include:\n- 缺：Greater Lord Rukkhadevata 的任何提及——文档中完全没有出现此名称\n- 缺：Nahida 的起源/诞生经过（如作为 Rukkhadevata 的分身或转世的具体描述）\n- 缺：Rukkhadevata 作为前任草神（Dendro Archon）的身份与角色\n- 缺：Rukkhadevata 牺牲自我、从世界树（Irminsul）中被抹除的事件\n- 缺：Nahida 与 Rukkhadevata 之间共享意识、记忆或神力的关系描述\n- 缺：须弥魔神任务（Sumeru Archon Quest）第四幕和第五幕的剧情文档\n- 缺：Nahida 的角色故事（Character Stories）或语音档案中关于其身世的条目\n- 缺：'Lesser Lord' 与 'Greater Lord' 称号之间关系的任何文档说明\n\n结论：仅凭当前文档，只能确认 Nahida 是草元素角色、称号为小吉祥草王（Lesser Lord Kusanali）、曾被囚禁在净善宫（Sanctuary of Surasthana）。关于与 Rukkhadevata 的关系和血脉/谱系问题，文档中无任何可验证依据。", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: The provided documents are severely insufficient to answer this question. Specific information gaps "], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T2-R07", "tier": 2, "question": "What is the relationship and lineage between Nahida and the former Greater Lord Rukkhadevata?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 2, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 2}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 2327, "oracle_out": 896, "qc_in": 3583, "qc_out": 1296, "total": 8102}, "cost_usd": 0.253}}
{"question_id": "T2-R08", "tier": 2, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Scaramouche (the Wanderer's previous incarnation) was the Sixth of the Eleven Fatui Harbingers, with the codename 'The Balladeer'.", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "After obtaining Ei's Electro Gnosis from Yae Miko and following Signora's death, Scaramouche cut off contact with the Fatui, causing them to believe he had gone rogue.", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Childe went to Inazuma to track Scaramouche down after his disappearance but to no avail.", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "With Dottore's assistance, the sages of Sumeru Akademiya worked to ascend Scaramouche into a new God of Wisdom under the name 'Shouki no Kami, the Prodigal'.", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "After his defeat by the Traveler and Nahida, Scaramouche had no allies to rely on as Dottore had left with the two Gnoses.", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "During an Irminsul investigation, Nahida left behind the true events of the Tatarasuna incident for Scaramouche to discover. He learned that his second 'betrayal' was masterminded by Dottore.", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Dottore orchestrated a cruel experiment at Tatarasuna involving murder and perceived betrayal to see how the kabukimono (Scaramouche's original identity) would respond, which indirectly led to kabukimono becoming the Harbinger Scaramouche.", "doc_source": "[NPC] Dottore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Once Dottore's involvement in his past was revealed, Scaramouche cut ties with the Fatui and swore personal vengeance on Dottore.", "doc_source": "[NPC] Dottore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Disgusted by the truth, Scaramouche decided to erase his existence from Irminsul, after which he became the Wanderer.", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Wanderer", "Scaramouche", "Fatui", "Dottore", "Nahida", "Yae Miko", "Ei", "Electro Gnosis", "Tatarasuna", "Irminsul", "Shouki no Kami"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Scaramouche", "relation": "was member of", "tail": "Eleven Fatui Harbingers", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Scaramouche", "relation": "obtained from", "tail": "Electro Gnosis (via Yae Miko)", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Scaramouche", "relation": "cut off contact with", "tail": "Fatui", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Dottore", "relation": "assisted in ascending", "tail": "Scaramouche (as Shouki no Kami)", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Dottore", "relation": "orchestrated betrayal of", "tail": "Scaramouche (at Tatarasuna)", "doc_source": "[NPC] Dottore"}, {"head": "Scaramouche", "relation": "discovered truth about", "tail": "Tatarasuna incident (via Irminsul)", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Scaramouche", "relation": "erased existence from", "tail": "Irminsul", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Scaramouche", "relation": "became", "tail": "Wanderer", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Confusing the initial defection (after obtaining the Gnosis) with the final break from the Fatui (after learning Dottore's role in Tatarasuna). The first departure was about going rogue with the Gnosis; the deeper, permanent break came from learning Dottore masterminded the Tatarasuna betrayal.", "correct": "Scaramouche first cut off contact after obtaining the Gnosis and Signora's death; the direct cause of his ultimate defection and desire for vengeance was discovering that Dottore orchestrated the Tatarasuna incident's betrayals."}, {"trap": "Claiming Scaramouche defected because of a conflict with the Tsaritsa or because he disagreed with Fatui ideology.", "correct": "The documents state the direct cause was learning Dottore masterminded his 'second betrayal' at Tatarasuna, and his initial departure was triggered by obtaining the Gnosis and Signora's death."}, {"trap": "Claiming Nahida forcibly erased Scaramouche from Irminsul.", "correct": "Scaramouche himself decided to erase his existence from Irminsul after learning the truth about Tatarasuna."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "The document text for [NPC] Wanderer appears truncated at the point describing Scaramouche's decision to erase himself from Irminsul ('decides to give his friends a second chance by erasing hi...'). The full details of what exactly he erased and the immediate aftermath are partially cut off, though the [PlayableCharacter] Wanderer document confirms the erasure and its result. Specific details about what the 'second betrayal' at Tatarasuna entailed (beyond Dottore's orchestration) are provided more in the Dottore document but the Wanderer NPC document is truncated.", "_review_flags": ["key_facts[0]: high-risk pattern — Scaramouche (the Wanderer's previous incarnation) was the Si", "key_facts[6]: high-risk pattern — Dottore orchestrated a cruel experiment at Tatarasuna involv", "coverage_notes: The document text for [NPC] Wanderer appears truncated at the point describing Scaramouche's decisio"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T2-R08", "tier": 2, "question": "What happened between the Wanderer and the Fatui, and what directly caused his defection?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 4, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 4}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 4356, "oracle_out": 1623, "qc_in": 6339, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 14318}, "cost_usd": 0.4321}}
{"question_id": "T2-R09", "tier": 2, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Layla is a student in the Rtawahist Darshan of the Sumeru Akademiya.", "doc_source": "Layla", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Layla specializes in Theoretical Astrology.", "doc_source": "Layla", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Layla is chronically sleep-deprived and of poor health as a result of her studies.", "doc_source": "Layla", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Layla believes that 'The Stars' Blessing' is the reason she wakes from sleepwalking to find her papers fully completed.", "doc_source": "Layla", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Sumeru Akademiya is Sumeru's main governing body and the most prestigious institute of learning in all of Teyvat.", "doc_source": "Akademiya", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Layla", "Sumeru Akademiya", "Rtawahist", "Theoretical Astrology"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Layla", "relation": "is student of", "tail": "Rtawahist Darshan", "doc_source": "Layla"}, {"head": "Rtawahist Darshan", "relation": "is part of", "tail": "Sumeru Akademiya", "doc_source": "Layla"}, {"head": "Layla", "relation": "specializes in", "tail": "Theoretical Astrology", "doc_source": "Layla"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Confusing Rtawahist (astrology) with other Darshans such as Haravatat or Kshahrewar.", "correct": "Layla belongs to the Rtawahist Darshan, which focuses on astrology."}, {"trap": "Claiming Layla studies Practical Astrology or astronomy instead of Theoretical Astrology.", "correct": "Layla's field is specifically Theoretical Astrology."}, {"trap": "Attributing her completed papers to her own sleepwalking efforts rather than her belief in 'The Stars' Blessing'.", "correct": "Layla herself believes 'The Stars' Blessing' is responsible for her papers being completed during sleepwalking episodes."}, {"trap": "Confusing Layla with other Rtawahist-associated characters such as Faruzan, who is also linked to the Akade