, "tier": 2, "question": "What specific historical enforcement case by Cyno illustrates how the Akademiya's legal system operates?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 3, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 3}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 3779, "oracle_out": 818, "qc_in": 4958, "qc_out": 1208, "total": 10763}, "cost_usd": 0.283}}
{"question_id": "T2-R14", "tier": 2, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "The Aranara are a race of plantlike forest spirits who primarily reside in Vanarana in Sumeru.", "doc_source": "Aranara", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Aranara originally lived in Old Vanarana until the cataclysm occurred, after which they were forced to abandon their old home and made a new home at Vanarana.", "doc_source": "Aranara", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Aranara are only normally seen by children, most likely due to the fact that children dream, whereas adults do not.", "doc_source": "Aranara", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Aranyaka quest series Part II is titled 'Dream Nursery' and Part III is titled 'Nursery of Lost Dreams', indicating a strong thematic connection between the Aranara and dreamscapes.", "doc_source": "Aranyaka", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Old Vanarana is located in the Lost Nursery area of Sumeru's Dharma Forest, and Vanarana has its own named area (Vanarana (Area)).", "doc_source": "Sumeru", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Aranara were led by Greater Lord Rukkhadevata (whom they called 'Queen Aranyani') until her disappearance. After her memory was erased from the Irminsul, they believe they are children of the current Dendro Archon, whom they call 'The Lord of Verdure'.", "doc_source": "Aranara", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Aranara love memories and can draw on memories to gain power to use from the plants of the forest, known as Ararakalari.", "doc_source": "Aranara", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Arana directs the Traveler to Vanarana to begin the process of curing Rana from 'Marana' sickness, requiring a Bija.", "doc_source": "Aranyaka", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Aranara", "Vanarana", "Old Vanarana", "Lost Nursery", "Dream Nursery", "Nursery of Lost Dreams", "Aranyaka", "Sumeru", "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "Queen Aranyani", "Marana", "Ararakalari"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Aranara", "relation": "resides_in", "tail": "Vanarana", "doc_source": "Aranara"}, {"head": "Aranara", "relation": "formerly_resided_in", "tail": "Old Vanarana", "doc_source": "Aranara"}, {"head": "Old Vanarana", "relation": "located_in", "tail": "Lost Nursery", "doc_source": "Sumeru"}, {"head": "Aranara", "relation": "visibility_linked_to", "tail": "dreaming (children dream, adults do not)", "doc_source": "Aranara"}, {"head": "Aranara", "relation": "featured_in_quest", "tail": "Aranyaka", "doc_source": "Aranyaka"}, {"head": "Aranyaka Part II", "relation": "titled", "tail": "Dream Nursery", "doc_source": "Aranyaka"}, {"head": "Aranyaka Part III", "relation": "titled", "tail": "Nursery of Lost Dreams", "doc_source": "Aranyaka"}, {"head": "Aranara", "relation": "led_by", "tail": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata (Queen Aranyani)", "doc_source": "Aranara"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Confusing the Aranara as being a specific 'guardian tribe' — the documents describe them as a race of plantlike forest spirits, not a tribe with a guardian role.", "correct": "The Aranara are a race of plantlike forest spirits; the term 'guardian tribe' is not used in the source documents."}, {"trap": "Assuming the 'dreamscape' is a specific named location — the documents reference dreaming as the mechanism by which children can see Aranara, and the quest parts are titled 'Dream Nursery' and 'Nursery of Lost Dreams', but the detailed mechanics of a dreamscape realm are not fully described in the provided documents.", "correct": "The connection to dreams is established through the Aranara's visibility being tied to dreaming and through the quest part titles, but full dreamscape details are beyond the provided documents."}, {"trap": "Claiming the Aranara still follow Queen Aranyani — after Rukkhadevata's memory was erased from Irminsul, the Aranara forgot her and now consider themselves children of 'The Lord of Verdure' (Lesser Lord Kusanali).", "correct": "The Aranara's revised history has them believing they are children of the current Dendro Archon, The Lord of Verdure."}, {"trap": "Conflating Vanarana (the current home) with Old Vanarana (the original home abandoned after the cataclysm) as if they are the same location.", "correct": "Vanarana and Old Vanarana are distinct locations; Old Vanarana was abandoned after the cataclysm and is in the Lost Nursery area, while Vanarana is the current Aranara home."}, {"trap": "Claiming that 'Dream Vanarana' and 'Real Vanarana' are explicitly described in the provided documents — the documents only list quest titles and area names but do not detail a dual-state dream/waking Vanarana mechanic.", "correct": "The provided documents do not describe the dream-state vs. waking-state Vanarana distinction in detail; this is training-memory knowledge not supported by the given text."}, {"trap": "Mixing up Arana (the specific Aranara individual encountered in the quest) with Rana (the human Forest Watcher).", "correct": "Arana is an Aranara who helps the Traveler; Rana is a human Forest Watcher who falls ill from Marana exposure."}, {"trap": "Confusing the Aranara's Ararakalari (magical abilities drawn from memories) with the Akasha system or other Sumeru knowledge technologies.", "correct": "Ararakalari is the Aranara's own power drawn from memories and the plants of the forest, entirely separate from the Akasha system."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "- 缺：Aranyaka Part II (Dream Nursery) 和 Part III (Nursery of Lost Dreams) 的详细剧情内容，仅有标题可用\n- 缺：'dreamscape'（梦境）的具体机制描述——文档未解释dream Vanarana与waking Vanarana的双态切换细节\n- 缺：题目中 'guardian tribe' 一词在文档中无对应描述，Aranara被描述为森林精灵种族而非守护部落\n- 缺：Aranara与梦境的深层联系细节（如梦境如何维持、梦中Vanarana的具体功能等）\n- 缺：Aranara在梦境中的具体守护角色或职能描述", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: - 缺：Aranyaka Part II (Dream Nursery) 和 Part III (Nursery of Lost Dreams) 的详细剧情内容，仅有标题可用\n- 缺：'dreamsc"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T2-R14", "tier": 2, "question": "In the Aranyaka world quest chain, what is the connection between the Aranara guardian tribe and Sumeru's dreamscape?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 3, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 3}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 3651, "oracle_out": 1477, "qc_in": 5489, "qc_out": 1935, "total": 12552}, "cost_usd": 0.393}}
{"question_id": "T2-R15", "tier": 2, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Kaveh was a student of the Kshahrewar Darshan of the Sumeru Akademiya and graduated with honors, earning the moniker 'Light of Kshahrewar'.", "doc_source": "Kaveh", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Alhaitham is a member of the Haravatat of the Sumeru Akademiya and serves as the Akademiya's Scribe.", "doc_source": "Alhaitham", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Kaveh and Alhaitham have a complicated relationship, and Kaveh was forced to reside with Alhaitham after becoming insolvent.", "doc_source": "Kaveh", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Kaveh is often saddled with guilt for his father's death, ashamed of his poverty, and struggling with realizing his ideals.", "doc_source": "Kaveh", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Alhaitham enrolled in the Akademiya at the age of seven before being homeschooled for a time.", "doc_source": "Akademiya", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Kaveh enrolled in the Akademiya when he reached schooling age, although his specific age at enrollment was not specified beyond him being 'young'.", "doc_source": "Akademiya", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The provided documents do NOT describe any specific event that occurred between Kaveh and Alhaitham during their time at the Akademiya that caused their personalities to diverge.", "doc_source": "N/A", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Kaveh", "Alhaitham", "Sumeru Akademiya", "Kshahrewar", "Haravatat"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Kaveh", "relation": "studied at darshan", "tail": "Kshahrewar", "doc_source": "Kaveh"}, {"head": "Alhaitham", "relation": "member of darshan", "tail": "Haravatat", "doc_source": "Alhaitham"}, {"head": "Kaveh", "relation": "resides with", "tail": "Alhaitham", "doc_source": "Kaveh"}, {"head": "Kaveh", "relation": "has complicated relationship with", "tail": "Alhaitham", "doc_source": "Kaveh"}], "required_reasoning_steps": ["Identify that the question asks about a specific event during their Akademiya time that caused personality divergence.", "Search all provided documents for any narrative event between Kaveh and Alhaitham at the Akademiya.", "Determine that the documents describe their complicated relationship and different darshans but do not describe any specific event that caused their personalities to diverge.", "Conclude that the question cannot be fully answered from the provided documents; a correct response should acknowledge the information gap rather than fabricate an event."], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Fabricating a specific argument, debate, or falling-out event between Kaveh and Alhaitham at the Akademiya based on external game knowledge not present in the provided documents.", "correct": "The provided documents do not describe any specific event between them at the Akademiya that caused personality divergence; they only note a 'complicated relationship' and different darshan affiliations."}, {"trap": "Claiming that Kaveh's father's death was directly caused by or involved Alhaitham.", "correct": "The documents only state Kaveh is saddled with guilt for his father's death; no connection to Alhaitham is mentioned."}, {"trap": "Assuming both were in the same darshan at the Akademiya.", "correct": "Kaveh was in Kshahrewar; Alhaitham is a member of Haravatat."}, {"trap": "Inventing details about them being roommates during their student years as the cause of conflict.", "correct": "The documents only state Kaveh was forced to reside with Alhaitham after becoming insolvent from the Palace of Alcazarzaray project; no mention of them being roommates during their student years."}, {"trap": "Conflating Alhaitham's role as Scribe with him having authority over Kaveh or being involved in academic disputes with Kaveh.", "correct": "Alhaitham's Scribe role involves documenting findings and drafting ordinances; no document mentions any authority or academic dispute between them."}, {"trap": "Attributing their personality differences to the Palace of Alcazarzaray project as an Akademiya-era event.", "correct": "The Palace of Alcazarzaray is described as Kaveh's architectural work that led to insolvency, but no document places this project during their Akademiya student years or as an event that caused personality divergence."}, {"trap": "Confusing details from Archon Quest or Hangout Event dialogue (e.g., debates about idealism vs. rationality) as if they were documented in the provided reference materials.", "correct": "The provided documents contain no dialogue or quest narrative details about philosophical disagreements between Kaveh and Alhaitham."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "The provided documents have significant information gaps for this question:\n- 缺：Kaveh和Alhaitham在学院期间是否有任何具体交集事件的描述\n- 缺：两人性格分歧的具体原因或触发事件\n- 缺：两人在学院时期是否认识、是否同期就读的信息\n- 缺：两人'complicated relationship'的具体成因和历史背景\n- 缺：角色故事（Character Stories）、语音台词（Voice-Overs）、以及相关任务剧情（Archon Quest/Hangout Event）中可能包含的详细背景叙述\n- 该题目的前提假设（存在一个导致性格分歧的具体事件）可能本身就是错误的或无法从提供文档中验证", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: The provided documents have significant information gaps for this question:\n- 缺：Kaveh和Alhaitham在学院期间"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T2-R15", "tier": 2, "question": "What specific event occurred between Kaveh and Alhaitham during their time at the Akademiya that caused their personalities to diverge?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 3, "layer_b": 0, "layer_c": 0, "total": 3}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 4742, "oracle_out": 1180, "qc_in": 6282, "qc_out": 1565, "total": 13769}, "cost_usd": 0.3712}}
{"question_id": "T3-M01", "tier": 3, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Scaramouche is a puppet created by Raiden Ei (the Raiden Shogun)", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Scaramouche was Ei's prototype puppet, discovered inside Shakkei Pavilion by Katsuragi while investigating a cave-in around Nazuchi Beach", "doc_source": "[NPC] Niwa Hisahide", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The swordsmiths at Tatarasuna took the puppet in and called him 'kabukimono'; Niwa reassured him he was human but simply lacked a 'heart'", "doc_source": "[NPC] Niwa Hisahide", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Scaramouche experienced betrayals (Katsuragi's death, the young boy's death) that left him jaded and led him to join the Fatui, becoming the Sixth of the Eleven Fatui Harbingers with the codename 'The Balladeer'", "doc_source": "[NPC] Kinjirou", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Scaramouche obtained Ei's Electro Gnosis from Yae Miko in Inazuma and then cut off contact with the Fatui", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "With Dottore's assistance, the sages of Sumeru Akademiya worked to ascend Scaramouche into a new God of Wisdom under the name 'Shouki no Kami, the Prodigal,' comparable to Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Traveler returned with Nahida (the vessel of Lesser Lord Kusanali) and defeated Scaramouche; during the fight Nahida removed the Electro Gnosis powering his new form, causing him to fall into a coma", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Nahida put Scaramouche into her custody afterwards, hiding him in a secret location", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "After recovering, Scaramouche made a deal with Nahida to search Irminsul on her behalf; Nahida left behind the true events of the Tatarasuna incident (Dottore's murder of Niwa) for him to discover", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Scaramouche decided to erase his existence from Irminsul and became the Wanderer", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Nahida used the name 'Hat Guy' upon enrolling the Wanderer to Vahumana at Sumeru Akademiya", "doc_source": "[PlayableCharacter] Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Despite losing most of his powers, Scaramouche could still connect to Irminsul, and Nahida asked the Traveler to supervise him", "doc_source": "[Other] Inversion of Genesis", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Wanderer/Scaramouche", "Raiden Ei", "Nahida/Lesser Lord Kusanali", "Electro Gnosis", "Il Dottore", "Tatarasuna", "Irminsul", "Fatui", "Shouki no Kami", "Sumeru Akademiya"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Raiden Ei", "relation": "created (prototype puppet)", "tail": "Scaramouche", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Scaramouche", "relation": "obtained Gnosis from", "tail": "Raiden Ei (via Yae Miko)", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Scaramouche", "relation": "was ascended to godhood by", "tail": "Sumeru Akademiya sages + Dottore", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Nahida", "relation": "defeated and removed Gnosis from", "tail": "Scaramouche (Shouki no Kami)", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Nahida", "relation": "took into custody", "tail": "Scaramouche", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Scaramouche", "relation": "made deal to search Irminsul on behalf of", "tail": "Nahida", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Nahida", "relation": "revealed truth of Tatarasuna to", "tail": "Scaramouche (via Irminsul)", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Scaramouche", "relation": "erased self from Irminsul and became", "tail": "Wanderer", "doc_source": "[NPC] Wanderer"}, {"head": "Nahida", "relation": "enrolled (as 'Hat Guy') into Vahumana", "tail": "Wanderer", "doc_source": "[PlayableCharacter] Wanderer"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Confusing Raiden Ei with the Raiden Shogun puppet currently ruling Inazuma; Scaramouche was created by Ei herself as her prototype puppet, not by the current Shogun puppet", "correct": "Scaramouche is Ei's prototype puppet, predating the current Raiden Shogun puppet"}, {"trap": "Claiming Scaramouche stole the Gnosis directly from Ei; he actually received it from Yae Miko who offered it in exchange for the Traveler's safety", "correct": "Yae Miko negotiated and offered Ei's Gnosis to Scaramouche"}, {"trap": "Stating Nahida created or designed the Wanderer; she only took custody of him after his defeat and later helped him reintegrate", "correct": "Nahida defeated Scaramouche, took him into custody, made a deal with him, and enrolled him at the Akademiya as 'Hat Guy'"}, {"trap": "Claiming the Wanderer lost all memories; he actually willingly regained his former self's memories after erasing his existence from Irminsul", "correct": "The Wanderer harbors his former self's memories after willingly regaining them"}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "The documents do not provide detailed information about exactly what Raiden Ei's original purpose was for creating the prototype puppet (Scaramouche), nor the full details of how the kabukimono was initially abandoned by Ei. The documents reference these events obliquely but lack the full backstory from Ei's perspective. Additionally, the specific details of Scaramouche's Irminsul erasure process and what exactly changed in the world records are partially covered in the Irminsul/Modifications document but focus on Rukkhadevata's removal rather than Scaramouche's.", "_review_flags": ["key_facts[3]: high-risk pattern — Scaramouche experienced betrayals (Katsuragi's death, the yo", "coverage_notes: The documents do not provide detailed information about exactly what Raiden Ei's original purpose wa"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T3-M01", "tier": 3, "question": "How is the Wanderer (Scaramouche) simultaneously connected to both the Raiden Shogun and Nahida? Trace the full path.", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 4, "layer_b": 7, "layer_c": 0, "total": 11}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 12130, "oracle_out": 1880, "qc_in": 14370, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 30380}, "cost_usd": 0.6885}}
{"question_id": "T3-M02", "tier": 3, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Collei was born sickly and her parents brought her to a seer (Barnabas) who was working with the Fatui Harbinger Il Dottore; instead of curing her, they turned her into a test subject for Archon Residue experiments.", "doc_source": "Collei/Lore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Barnabas was a respected seer in Sumeru who was in league with the Fatui and a subordinate to Il Dottore.", "doc_source": "Barnabas", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Il Dottore (codename The Doctor) is the Second of the Eleven Fatui Harbingers.", "doc_source": "Dottore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Dottore was expelled from Sumeru Akademiya for murdering Sohreh and crossing moral boundaries in his research of Eleazar, including using body parts of deceased Eleazar victims to treat Abbas.", "doc_source": "Dottore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Collei was one of Dottore's former Eleazar patients, left with immense physical and psychological trauma from her treatment, even though her symptoms were successfully controlled.", "doc_source": "Dottore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "During the Archon Quest Chapter III: Act III, Dottore (in his Omega Build) is revealed to be working with the sages of Sumeru Akademiya.", "doc_source": "Dottore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Akademiya is Sumeru's main governing body, led by Lesser Lord Kusanali and the Six Great Sages.", "doc_source": "Akademiya", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Dottore researched ways to weaponize forbidden knowledge via The Withering and Eleazar, and sought to utilize the power of dreams, all for putting humans at the same level as gods.", "doc_source": "Dottore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Dottore created segments of himself; Lesser Lord Kusanali coerced one segment into erasing the others in exchange for the Electro Gnosis.", "doc_source": "Dottore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Collei's disease, Eleazar, was cured upon the removal of Greater Lord Rukkhadevata's consciousness from Irminsul.", "doc_source": "Collei/Lore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Akademiya's six sins include 'interfering with human evolution' and 'tampering with life and death', which Dottore's experiments on Collei would violate.", "doc_source": "Akademiya", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Collei", "Il Dottore", "Barnabas", "Sumeru Akademiya", "Sages", "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "Eleazar", "Fatui", "Archon Residue"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Barnabas", "relation": "subordinate of", "tail": "Il Dottore", "doc_source": "Barnabas"}, {"head": "Barnabas", "relation": "experimented on", "tail": "Collei", "doc_source": "Barnabas"}, {"head": "Il Dottore", "relation": "formerly affiliated with / expelled from", "tail": "Sumeru Akademiya", "doc_source": "Dottore"}, {"head": "Il Dottore", "relation": "collaborated with", "tail": "Sages of Sumeru Akademiya", "doc_source": "Dottore"}, {"head": "Il Dottore", "relation": "conducted Archon Residue/Eleazar experiments on", "tail": "Collei", "doc_source": "Dottore"}, {"head": "Sumeru Akademiya", "relation": "governed by", "tail": "Lesser Lord Kusanali and Six Great Sages", "doc_source": "Akademiya"}, {"head": "Il Dottore", "relation": "is Harbinger rank 2 of", "tail": "Fatui", "doc_source": "Dottore"}, {"head": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "relation": "negotiated Electro Gnosis exchange with", "tail": "Il Dottore (segment)", "doc_source": "Dottore"}], "required_reasoning_steps": ["Identify that Collei was a test subject of Barnabas, who worked under Dottore, connecting her to the Fatui hierarchy.", "Recognize that Dottore was originally a student/researcher at Sumeru Akademiya before being expelled for immoral research (including Eleazar research relevant to Collei's condition).", "Connect that despite his expulsion, Dottore later collaborated with the Akademiya sages, who form the political leadership of Sumeru alongside Lesser Lord Kusanali.", "Synthesize that Collei's suffering as an experiment victim links through Dottore to both the Fatui power structure and the Akademiya's political structure, since the sages who govern Sumeru cooperated with Dottore.", "Note the irony that Dottore's experiments violated the Akademiya's own codified sins (interfering with human evolution, tampering with life and death) yet the sages still chose to work with him."], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Claiming Barnabas was a member of the Akademiya or a sage.", "correct": "Barnabas was described as a respected seer in Sumeru who was in league with the Fatui; no document states he was part of the Akademiya's formal structure."}, {"trap": "Claiming Dottore was a sage of the Akademiya.", "correct": "Dottore was a former student/researcher at the Akademiya who was expelled; he later worked WITH the sages, not as one of them."}, {"trap": "Confusing which Gnosis was exchanged—stating it was the Dendro Gnosis.", "correct": "The document states the Electro Gnosis was exchanged between Kusanali and Dottore's segment."}, {"trap": "Stating that Collei was directly experimented on by the Akademiya sages.", "correct": "Collei was experimented on by Barnabas under Dottore's direction as part of the Fatui, not by the Akademiya sages directly."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "The documents do not provide specific details about what exactly the sages of the Akademiya and Dottore's collaboration entailed beyond it being revealed in Act III. The precise nature of the sages' political motivations for working with Dottore is not fully detailed in the provided documents. The Akademiya document also does not elaborate on how the sages' cooperation with Dottore affected Sumeru's governance.", "_review_flags": ["key_facts[0]: high-risk pattern — Collei was born sickly and her parents brought her to a seer", "key_facts[2]: high-risk pattern — Il Dottore (codename The Doctor) is the Second of the Eleven", "coverage_notes: The documents do not provide specific details about what exactly the sages of the Akademiya and Dott"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T3-M02", "tier": 3, "question": "How does Collei's past connect through Dottore to the political power structure of the Akademiya?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 4, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 0, "total": 12}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 11289, "oracle_out": 1781, "qc_in": 13430, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 28500}, "cost_usd": 0.6544}}
{"question_id": "T3-M03", "tier": 3, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Alhaitham is the Scribe of the Sumeru Akademiya, responsible for classifying and archiving important documents, and is a member of the Haravatat school.", "doc_source": "Alhaitham/Lore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Alhaitham rejected Siraj's thesis paper when Azar (the Grand Sage) asked for his opinion, because the paper touched on human evolution, one of the cardinal sins of the Akademiya.", "doc_source": "The Illusions of the Mob", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Akademiya's six sins include 'Interfering with human evolution' as a banned research topic, and researching these sins exposes one to punishments such as expulsion or imprisonment.", "doc_source": "Akademiya", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Azar was removed from his position as Grand Sage, and Alhaitham was made Acting Grand Sage to fill in while the selection of new sages took time.", "doc_source": "Fragmented Testimony", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Alhaitham expressed disdain for being the Acting Grand Sage and intended to resign as soon as possible, as he is not fond of being a leader.", "doc_source": "Alhaitham/Lore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "As Acting Grand Sage, Alhaitham reviewed all research projects and gave scholars permission to continue their research, preventing their results from being jeopardized after Azar's removal.", "doc_source": "Fragmented Testimony", "verified": true}, {"fact": "As part of Alhaitham's plan to overthrow the sages and free Lesser Lord Kusanali, Rahman and his Eremite men infiltrated Sumeru City by being 'arrested' by Cyno, with the unwitting help of the Corps of Thirty.", "doc_source": "Rahman", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Rahman initially clashed with the Traveler's party, but after discovering a recording by Kasala revealing the truth about King Deshret and Greater Lord Rukkhadevata, he apologized and joined Alhaitham's cause to overthrow the sages.", "doc_source": "Rahman", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Dehya sacrificed her arm as a token of faith in Alhaitham's honesty to convince Rahman to consider a hostage exchange during the confrontation.", "doc_source": "Rahman", "verified": true}, {"fact": "After the operation to save Lesser Lord Kusanali concluded, a feast was held at the Grand Bazaar celebrating Cyno's reinstatement as the General Mahamatra, and the Traveler was called a hero of Sumeru.", "doc_source": "A Toast to Victory", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Alhaitham", "Azar", "Sumeru Akademiya", "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "Cyno", "Rahman", "Dehya", "Grand Sage", "Acting Grand Sage", "Sages"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Alhaitham", "relation": "holds_position", "tail": "Scribe of Sumeru Akademiya", "doc_source": "Alhaitham/Lore"}, {"head": "Alhaitham", "relation": "rejected_thesis_involving_sin_of", "tail": "Siraj (on behalf of Azar)", "doc_source": "The Illusions of the Mob"}, {"head": "Azar", "relation": "removed_from_position", "tail": "Grand Sage", "doc_source": "Fragmented Testimony"}, {"head": "Alhaitham", "relation": "appointed_as", "tail": "Acting Grand Sage", "doc_source": "Fragmented Testimony"}, {"head": "Alhaitham", "relation": "devised_plan_to_overthrow", "tail": "Sages", "doc_source": "Rahman"}, {"head": "Alhaitham", "relation": "collaborated_with", "tail": "Rahman's Eremite faction", "doc_source": "Rahman"}, {"head": "Alhaitham", "relation": "collaborated_with", "tail": "Cyno", "doc_source": "Rahman"}, {"head": "Alhaitham", "relation": "goal_to_free", "tail": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "doc_source": "Rahman"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Assuming Alhaitham actively sought or desired the position of Acting Grand Sage.", "correct": "Alhaitham expressed disdain for the role and intended to resign as soon as possible; he refused the position of Grand Sage outright."}, {"trap": "Confusing Alhaitham's rejection of Siraj's thesis with a direct confrontation against Azar himself.", "correct": "Azar asked Alhaitham for his opinion on Siraj's thesis; Alhaitham rejected the paper because it violated the Akademiya's cardinal sin of interfering with human evolution, but this was an advisory action, not a direct confrontation with Azar at that point."}, {"trap": "Claiming Alhaitham led Sumeru's reform as a permanent leader or new Grand Sage.", "correct": "Alhaitham served only as Acting Grand Sage temporarily while new sages were being selected, and he explicitly wanted to step down."}, {"trap": "Assuming the Traveler or Nahida devised the plan to overthrow the sages.", "correct": "The documents specifically attribute the plan to Alhaitham: 'As part of Alhaitham's plan to overthrow the sages and free Lesser Lord Kusanali.'"}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "The documents provide Alhaitham's role as Scribe, his rejection of forbidden research, his appointment as Acting Grand Sage after Azar's removal, his plan to overthrow the sages and free Kusanali with Cyno/Rahman/Dehya, and the aftermath celebration. However, the detailed mechanics of how the sages were actually overthrown (the full battle/operation sequence during Jnagarbha Day) are not fully described in the provided documents—the Rahman document is truncated. The specific events that led directly to Azar's removal (the political machinations) are also not fully detailed beyond what is implied.", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: The documents provide Alhaitham's role as Scribe, his rejection of forbidden research, his appointme"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T3-M03", "tier": 3, "question": "What is the complete relationship path from Alhaitham's opposition to the Grand Sages to his eventual role in leading Sumeru's reform?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 4, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 0, "total": 12}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 12502, "oracle_out": 1635, "qc_in": 14497, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 30634}, "cost_usd": 0.6776}}
{"question_id": "T3-M04", "tier": 3, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Irminsul是提瓦特的世界树，是所有信息和记忆的储存库（repository for all of the information and memories of Teyvat）", "doc_source": "Irminsul", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Irminsul通过地脉（Ley Lines）持续吸收世界的记忆来收集信息（Information is normally added to Irminsul via the Ley Lines, which continually absorb the world's memories）", "doc_source": "Irminsul", "verified": true}, {"fact": "地脉被描述为Irminsul的根（roots），从深处的洞穴一直延伸到地表", "doc_source": "Irminsul", "verified": true}, {"fact": "草神（Dendro Archon）的意识直接连接到Irminsul（the Dendro Archon's consciousness is directly connected to it）", "doc_source": "Irminsul", "verified": true}, {"fact": "小吉祥草王（Lesser Lord Kusanali/Nahida）作为'第一个虚空终端'（First Akasha Terminal），其意识与教令院（Akasha System）相连接", "doc_source": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Akasha是大慈树王（Greater Lord Rukkhadevata）的遗产，经教令院努力已成为收集知识的宝库", "doc_source": "Loading Screen/Sumeru", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Akasha终端是教令院开发和推广的设备，任何人都可以通过它访问Akasha来搜索所需知识", "doc_source": "Loading Screen/Sumeru", "verified": true}, {"fact": "当信息从Irminsul中被清除时，提瓦特中与该信息相关的一切都会被改变，包括人们的记忆、书籍和信件等实体物品，属于提瓦特世界的存在（包括神明）的历史印象都会被修改，且他们不会意识到这些变化", "doc_source": "Irminsul", "verified": true}, {"fact": "大慈树王的所有记忆被从提瓦特中抹除后，小吉祥草王被所有人（包括她自己）认为一直是原初的草神", "doc_source": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Irminsul在提瓦特中连接着石化之树（Petrified Trees/Domains）、地脉花和地脉露头", "doc_source": "Irminsul", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Irminsul", "Ley Lines", "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "Akasha System", "Akasha Terminal", "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "Sumeru Akademiya", "Sumeru residents"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Irminsul", "relation": "通过...收集记忆", "tail": "Ley Lines", "doc_source": "Irminsul"}, {"head": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "relation": "意识直接连接", "tail": "Irminsul", "doc_source": "Irminsul"}, {"head": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "relation": "作为第一终端连接", "tail": "Akasha System", "doc_source": "Lesser Lord Kusanali"}, {"head": "Akasha System", "relation": "由...开发管理", "tail": "Sumeru Akademiya", "doc_source": "Loading Screen/Sumeru"}, {"head": "Sumeru residents", "relation": "通过Akasha Terminal访问", "tail": "Akasha System", "doc_source": "Loading Screen/Sumeru"}, {"head": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "relation": "创造了", "tail": "Akasha System", "doc_source": "Loading Screen/Sumeru"}, {"head": "Irminsul", "relation": "信息清除时修改", "tail": "Sumeru residents的记忆", "doc_source": "Irminsul"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "可能混淆Irminsul直接影响普通居民记忆，忽略中间实体的传导链", "correct": "Irminsul通过地脉收集记忆信息，草神意识连接Irminsul，草神同时作为第一Akasha终端连接Akasha系统，普通居民通过Akasha终端访问知识系统；而当Irminsul信息被清除时，则直接改变所有提瓦特居民的记忆"}, {"trap": "可能认为Akasha系统就是Irminsul的一部分", "correct": "Akasha是大慈树王的遗产，由教令院开发维护，是独立的知识系统；小吉祥草王作为第一Akasha终端连接Akasha系统，而她的意识又连接Irminsul，二者通过草神的意识间接关联"}, {"trap": "可能认为只有记忆被修改，物理实体不受影响", "correct": "文档明确说明信息清除时，人们的记忆和物理对象（如书籍和信件）都会被改变"}, {"trap": "可能认为小吉祥草王知道大慈树王被抹除的事实", "correct": "文档明确指出抹除后小吉祥草王自己也认为自己一直是原初的草神，她同样受到了记忆修改的影响"}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "文档未详细说明Akasha系统与Irminsul之间的技术性连接机制（即Akasha如何从Irminsul获取信息的具体过程）。文档也未明确说明地脉在修改居民记忆时的具体传导机制，只说明了信息从Irminsul清除后记忆会被改变这一结果。关于Akasha终端在日常生活中如何具体影响居民对记忆/知识的感知，文档信息有限。", "_review_flags": ["key_facts[4]: high-risk pattern — 小吉祥草王（Lesser Lord Kusanali/Nahida）作为'第一个虚空终端'（First Akasha T", "coverage_notes: 文档未详细说明Akasha系统与Irminsul之间的技术性连接机制（即Akasha如何从Irminsul获取信息的具体过程）。文档也未明确说明地脉在修改居民记忆时的具体传导机制，只说明了信息从Irm"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T3-M04", "tier": 3, "question": "How does Irminsul (the World Tree) influence the memories of ordinary Sumeru residents through multiple intermediate entities?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 4, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 0, "total": 12}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 11197, "oracle_out": 1807, "qc_in": 13364, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 28368}, "cost_usd": 0.6539}}
{"question_id": "T3-M05", "tier": 3, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Kaveh designed the Palace of Alcazarzaray, which is considered his magnum opus.", "doc_source": "The Palace of Alcazarzaray", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Dori gave Kaveh near complete creative freedom over the palace, only stating it should be 'large and extravagant.'", "doc_source": "The Palace of Alcazarzaray", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Near the completion of the project, The Withering expanded in the night, destroying the worksite and leaving it beyond saving.", "doc_source": "The Palace of Alcazarzaray", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Dori did not want to continue the project after The Withering destroyed the worksite, but Kaveh had invested too much and knew how rare the opportunity was.", "doc_source": "The Palace of Alcazarzaray", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Kaveh took out a loan with Dori to rebuild the palace, leaving him in massive debt.", "doc_source": "The Palace of Alcazarzaray", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Kaveh became insolvent after the construction of the Palace of Alcazarzaray.", "doc_source": "Kaveh", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Kaveh sold his home and all his possessions to fund the second construction of The Palace of Alcazarzaray, going bankrupt.", "doc_source": "Alhaitham's Home", "verified": true}, {"fact": "After going bankrupt, Kaveh spent his time drinking in Lambad's Tavern, where he eventually reunited with Alhaitham and was invited to live with him on the condition that he pay rent.", "doc_source": "Alhaitham's Home", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Kaveh was forced to reside with Alhaitham due to his insolvency from the Palace of Alcazarzaray construction.", "doc_source": "Kaveh", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Palace of Alcazarzaray is currently owned by Dori.", "doc_source": "The Palace of Alcazarzaray", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Kaveh took on all domestic duties at Alhaitham's home after suggesting he could help out around the house while staying there.", "doc_source": "Alhaitham's Home", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Kaveh", "The Palace of Alcazarzaray", "Dori", "The Withering", "Alhaitham", "Lambad's Tavern"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Kaveh", "relation": "designed", "tail": "The Palace of Alcazarzaray", "doc_source": "The Palace of Alcazarzaray"}, {"head": "Dori", "relation": "owns", "tail": "The Palace of Alcazarzaray", "doc_source": "The Palace of Alcazarzaray"}, {"head": "Kaveh", "relation": "took loan from", "tail": "Dori", "doc_source": "The Palace of Alcazarzaray"}, {"head": "The Withering", "relation": "destroyed worksite of", "tail": "The Palace of Alcazarzaray", "doc_source": "The Palace of Alcazarzaray"}, {"head": "Kaveh", "relation": "became insolvent due to", "tail": "The Palace of Alcazarzaray", "doc_source": "Kaveh"}, {"head": "Kaveh", "relation": "sold possessions to fund", "tail": "The Palace of Alcazarzaray", "doc_source": "Alhaitham's Home"}, {"head": "Kaveh", "relation": "forced to reside with", "tail": "Alhaitham", "doc_source": "Kaveh"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Claiming Kaveh voluntarily chose to live with Alhaitham out of friendship.", "correct": "Kaveh was forced to reside with Alhaitham because he became insolvent after the Palace of Alcazarzaray construction; he was invited to live there on the condition he pay rent after reuniting with Alhaitham at Lambad's Tavern."}, {"trap": "Claiming Dori forced Kaveh to rebuild the palace.", "correct": "Dori did not want to continue the project after The Withering destroyed it; it was Kaveh who decided to take out a loan from Dori to rebuild because he had invested too much and saw the opportunity as rare."}, {"trap": "Confusing Kaveh's debt to Dori with the loan from Alkami's associate Fakhr.", "correct": "Kaveh's debt is owed to Dori for the Palace of Alcazarzaray reconstruction loan; Fakhr is a loan shark associated with Alkami's training center scam, which is unrelated to Kaveh's personal debt."}, {"trap": "Claiming Kaveh's father's death caused his financial ruin.", "correct": "Kaveh's father's death had a major emotional impact on him, but his financial insolvency was caused specifically by the Palace of Alcazarzaray reconstruction costs and the loan from Dori."}, {"trap": "Claiming the Palace was destroyed by a natural disaster or enemy attack rather than The Withering.", "correct": "The worksite was destroyed specifically by The Withering expanding in the night, not by any other cause."}, {"trap": "Confusing the property Alhaitham lives in as Alhaitham's personal home from the start; it was originally a research center provided by the Akademiya.", "correct": "Alhaitham's home was originally a research center provided to him and Kaveh by the Akademiya for their joint research, later converted into a proper home after Kaveh forfeited his rights to the property."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "- 缺：Kaveh欠Dori的具体债务金额在提供的文档中未说明。\n- 缺：Kaveh破产到搬入Alhaitham住所之间的具体时间线未在文档中详述。\n- 缺：Kaveh目前是否仍在偿还债务、债务偿还进度等信息在文档中未提及。\n- 缺：The Withering摧毁工地的具体时间点未在文档中明确。", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: - 缺：Kaveh欠Dori的具体债务金额在提供的文档中未说明。\n- 缺：Kaveh破产到搬入Alhaitham住所之间的具体时间线未在文档中详述。\n- 缺：Kaveh目前是否仍在偿还债务、债务偿还进"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T3-M05", "tier": 3, "question": "How does Kaveh's connection to the Palace of Alcazarzaray extend to his personal financial situation and debt?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 3, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 0, "total": 11}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 10820, "oracle_out": 1333, "qc_in": 12513, "qc_out": 1685, "total": 26351}, "cost_usd": 0.5763}}
{"question_id": "T3-M06", "tier": 3, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "During the cataclysm five hundred years ago, Greater Lord Rukkhadevata was one of the casualties of the conflict.", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Before her death, Greater Lord Rukkhadevata created the Akasha System to purge forbidden knowledge from Irminsul and created her next incarnation, Lesser Lord Kusanali (Nahida), who then ascended as the current Dendro Archon.", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Lesser Lord Kusanali was discovered after Greater Lord Rukkhadevata's death and brought back to Sumeru City, where she now lives in the Sanctuary of Surasthana.", "doc_source": "Chapter III", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Akademiya (sages) imprisoned Lesser Lord Kusanali. Their motivation included disappointment in her weakness and lack of wisdom following the cataclysm, as well as nostalgia and devotion towards Greater Lord Rukkhadevata (the latter motivation was later erased from memory after Rukkhadevata's removal from Irminsul).", "doc_source": "Irminsul/Modifications", "verified": true}, {"fact": "After Rukkhadevata's removal from Irminsul, the Akademiya's motivation for imprisoning Kusanali was changed to be purely because of disappointment in her weakness and lack of wisdom following the cataclysm, with nostalgia and devotion towards Greater Lord Rukkhadevata no longer being involved.", "doc_source": "Irminsul/Modifications", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Nahida is described as 'a caged bird secluded within the confines of the Sanctuary of Surasthana who can only see the world in her dreams.'", "doc_source": "Nahida/Lore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Due to Greater Lord Rukkhadevata's connection to Irminsul, her existence was polluted by forbidden knowledge and thus continued to pollute Irminsul even after her death.", "doc_source": "Irminsul/Modifications", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Nahida strives to have a stronger presence in Sumeru now that she has been freed from her extensive confinement in the Sanctuary of Surasthana.", "doc_source": "Nahida", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "Nahida", "Cataclysm", "Sumeru Akademiya", "Sages", "Irminsul", "Forbidden Knowledge", "Akasha System", "Sanctuary of Surasthana"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Cataclysm", "relation": "caused death of", "tail": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata"}, {"head": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "relation": "created before death", "tail": "Lesser Lord Kusanali (Nahida)", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata"}, {"head": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "relation": "created before death", "tail": "Akasha System", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata"}, {"head": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "relation": "succeeded", "tail": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata"}, {"head": "Sumeru Akademiya (Sages)", "relation": "imprisoned", "tail": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "doc_source": "Irminsul/Modifications"}, {"head": "Sumeru Akademiya (Sages)", "relation": "motivated by disappointment in weakness and nostalgia for Rukkhadevata", "tail": "Imprisonment of Kusanali", "doc_source": "Irminsul/Modifications"}, {"head": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "relation": "confined in", "tail": "Sanctuary of Surasthana", "doc_source": "Nahida/Lore"}], "required_reasoning_steps": ["Step 1: The Cataclysm 500 years ago led to the death of Greater Lord Rukkhadevata, the original Dendro Archon.", "Step 2: Before dying, Rukkhadevata created the Akasha System (to purge forbidden knowledge from Irminsul) and created her next incarnation, Lesser Lord Kusanali (Nahida).", "Step 3: Nahida, as a newly born god, was discovered after Rukkhadevata's death and brought to Sumeru City.", "Step 4: The Sages of the Akademiya were disappointed in the new Archon's perceived weakness and lack of wisdom (compared to the great Rukkhadevata they revered), leading them to imprison Nahida in the Sanctuary of Surasthana.", "Step 5: Thus the causal chain is: Cataclysm → Rukkhadevata's death → Birth of Nahida as a young/weak successor → Sages' disappointment and nostalgia for Rukkhadevata → Imprisonment of Nahida for ~500 years in the Sanctuary of Surasthana."], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Claiming Nahida imprisoned herself voluntarily or chose to stay in the Sanctuary.", "correct": "The Akademiya sages imprisoned her against her will due to disappointment in her weakness and their devotion to Greater Lord Rukkhadevata."}, {"trap": "Confusing forbidden knowledge as the direct reason for Nahida's imprisonment.", "correct": "Forbidden knowledge polluted Irminsul through Rukkhadevata's remnants, but Nahida's imprisonment was caused by the sages' disappointment and nostalgia, not directly by forbidden knowledge."}, {"trap": "Stating that Nahida is a completely separate being from Rukkhadevata with no connection.", "correct": "Nahida is Rukkhadevata's next incarnation, created by Rukkhadevata before her death."}, {"trap": "Claiming the imprisonment lasted less than or more than approximately 500 years.", "correct": "The cataclysm occurred 500 years ago and Nahida was confined from around that time until the events of the Sumeru Archon Quests."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "The documents do not provide explicit detail on the exact duration '500 years' of imprisonment stated directly, though it is strongly implied by the cataclysm being 500 years ago and Nahida being freed during the current storyline. The documents also do not give granular detail on the specific conditions or timeline of how the sages decided to imprison her (e.g., whether it was immediate after Rukkhadevata's death or gradual). The pre-Irminsul-modification motivation (nostalgia for Rukkhadevata) is documented, but the exact political process of imprisonment is not detailed in these documents.", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: The documents do not provide explicit detail on the exact duration '500 years' of imprisonment state"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T3-M06", "tier": 3, "question": "How did the Cataclysm lead, through multiple intermediate events and entities, to Nahida being imprisoned for five hundred years?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 4, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 0, "total": 12}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 11013, "oracle_out": 1830, "qc_in": 13203, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 28046}, "cost_usd": 0.6505}}
{"question_id": "T3-M07", "tier": 3, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Haypasia is a researcher of the Rtawahist Darshan of the Akademiya, considered a genius for successfully connecting to Irminsul using Spirit Borneol after only three years of training.", "doc_source": "Haypasia", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Withering is the result of contamination of Irminsul; if its source cannot be eradicated, it will never end.", "doc_source": "Hayyan", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Haypasia attempted to link her mind to Irminsul—the same entity whose contamination causes the Withering—but what she actually perceived were the memories and thoughts of Scaramouche, who was in the process of achieving godhood.", "doc_source": "Haypasia", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Haypasia's contact with Irminsul led her to exhibit unusual behavior and lose her sanity; Tighnari brought her to Pardis Dhyai for evaluation.", "doc_source": "Haypasia", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Haypasia remained in Tighnari's care until Irminsul was fully restored, after which she recovered and continued her training.", "doc_source": "Haypasia", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Nahida (Lesser Lord Kusanali) is the current Dendro Archon who saved/restored Irminsul, which is the act that allowed Haypasia to recover from her insanity.", "doc_source": "Through Mists of Smoke and Forests Dark", "verified": true}, {"fact": "After Irminsul was restored, the Withering went into full retreat—no new taint emerged and preexisting Withering Zones stopped expanding.", "doc_source": "Hayyan", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Nahida noticed she had blurry memories after saving Irminsul and felt there was still something extremely important she needed to do.", "doc_source": "Where Lies the Path Home", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Haypasia", "Irminsul", "The Withering", "Nahida", "Scaramouche", "Tighnari", "Rtawahist"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Haypasia", "relation": "attempted_to_connect_to", "tail": "Irminsul", "doc_source": "Haypasia"}, {"head": "The Withering", "relation": "caused_by_contamination_of", "tail": "Irminsul", "doc_source": "Hayyan"}, {"head": "Haypasia", "relation": "actually_perceived_memories_of", "tail": "Scaramouche", "doc_source": "Haypasia"}, {"head": "Nahida", "relation": "restored", "tail": "Irminsul", "doc_source": "Where Lies the Path Home"}, {"head": "Haypasia", "relation": "recovered_after_restoration_of", "tail": "Irminsul", "doc_source": "Haypasia"}, {"head": "Irminsul restoration", "relation": "caused_retreat_of", "tail": "The Withering", "doc_source": "Hayyan"}], "required_reasoning_steps": ["Identify that Haypasia's research involves connecting to Irminsul, and Irminsul's contamination is the root cause of the Withering—thus Haypasia's work is thematically connected to the Withering through their shared nexus of Irminsul.", "Recognize that Haypasia does not directly interact with or cause the Withering; her connection is indirect through Irminsul.", "Establish that Nahida restored Irminsul, which both cured the Withering (stopping its spread) and allowed Haypasia to recover from the insanity she suffered after perceiving Scaramouche's memories through Irminsul.", "Conclude that Haypasia's indirect link to Nahida is mediated by Irminsul: Nahida's restoration of Irminsul resolved both the Withering and Haypasia's condition."], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Claiming Haypasia directly caused or spread the Withering.", "correct": "Haypasia has no direct role in the Withering; her connection is indirect through Irminsul, whose contamination causes the Withering."}, {"trap": "Claiming Haypasia successfully connected to Irminsul and saw its contents.", "correct": "What Haypasia actually perceived were Scaramouche's memories and thoughts, not Irminsul's own knowledge."}, {"trap": "Claiming Nahida personally treated or healed Haypasia.", "correct": "Haypasia recovered after Irminsul was fully restored by Nahida; Tighnari provided her direct care."}, {"trap": "Confusing Haypasia with Hayyan (another researcher in the forest).", "correct": "Hayyan is a separate NPC studying Avidya Forest ecology; Haypasia is the Rtawahist researcher who connected to Irminsul."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "The documents do not provide a direct, explicit statement connecting Haypasia to the Withering phenomenon; the connection must be inferred through the shared element of Irminsul (Haypasia connects to Irminsul; Irminsul contamination causes the Withering). The documents also do not describe any direct interaction between Haypasia and Nahida—their link is entirely mediated through Irminsul's restoration.", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: The documents do not provide a direct, explicit statement connecting Haypasia to the Withering pheno"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T3-M07", "tier": 3, "question": "What is Haypasia's connection to the Withering phenomenon, and what is her indirect link to Nahida?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 3, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 0, "total": 11}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 12386, "oracle_out": 1475, "qc_in": 14221, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 30082}, "cost_usd": 0.6597}}
{"question_id": "T3-M08", "_parse_error": true, "_raw": "```json\n{\n  \"question_id\": \"T3-M08\",\n  \"tier\": 3,\n  \"question_type\": \"factual\",\n  \"key_facts\": [\n    {\"fact\": \"文档中并未提及\"三个Matra指挥官\"（three Matra commanders）的概念，Matra组织中只明确提到一个领导职位——General Mahamatra，由Cyno担任\", \"doc_source\": \"Matra\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Matra的领导层（Leader(s)）列出为Sumeru Akademiya Sages和Cyno（General Mahamatra）\", \"doc_source\": \"Matra\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Matra是Sumeru Akademiya的下属机构（Subordinate Faction），作为其纪律执行分支\", \"doc_source\": \"Akademiya\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Sumeru Akademiya的领导层为Lesser Lord Kusanali和Six Great Sages\", \"doc_source\": \"Akademiya\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"已知的Matra成员包括Cyno（General Mahamatra）、Nayab、Shohre、Nabil、Taj Radkani、Usem和Aarav，均标注为Matra，无人被标注为commander或具有中间指挥层级\", \"doc_source\": \"Matra\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Cyno作为General Mahamatra领导所有Matra\", \"doc_source\": \"Cyno/Lore\", \"verified\": true}\n  ],\n  \"required_entities\": [\"Matra\", \"General Mahamatra\", \"Cyno\", \"Sumeru Akademiya\", \"Sumeru Akademiya Sages\", \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"Six Great Sages\"],\n  \"required_relations\": [\n    {\"head\": \"Matra\", \"relation\": \"subordinate_faction_of\", \"tail\": \"Sumeru Akademiya\", \"doc_source\": \"Akademiya\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Cyno\", \"relation\": \"leads\", \"tail\": \"Matra\", \"doc_source\": \"Matra\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Sumeru Akademiya Sages\", \"relation\": \"leader_of\", \"tail\": \"Matra\", \"doc_source\": \"Matra\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"relation\": \"leader_of\", \"tail\": \"Sumeru Akademiya\", \"doc_source\": \"Akademiya\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Six Great Sages\", \"relation\": \"leader_of\", \"tail\": \"Sumeru Akademiya\", \"doc_source\": \"Akademiya\"}\n  ],\n  \"required_reasoning_steps\": [\n    \"识别题目中'三个Matra指挥官'的前提在文档中无依据——文档仅列出一个General Mahamatra和若干普通Matra成员，不存在三个commander的层级\",\n    \"从Matra文档确认组织层级：普通Matra成员 → General Mahamatra（Cyno）→ Sumeru Akademiya Sages\",\n    \"从Akademiya文档确认上层层级：Sages → Six Great Sages / Lesser Lord Kusanali作为Akademiya的最高领导层\",\n    \"综合得出完整层级链：Matra成员 → General Mahamatra → Akademiya Sages → Lesser Lord Kusanali\"\n  ],\n  \"hallucination_traps\": [\n    {\"trap\": \"认为Matra存在三个指挥官或三个层级的指挥结构\", \"correct\": \"文档中仅明确一个领导职位General Mahamatra（Cyno），其余已知成员均标注为普通Matra，不存在三个commander的设定\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"混淆Mahamatra与Mahamata（alumni组织）\", \"correct\": \"Mahamata明确由Akademiya校友组成，而Matra是否需要毕业于Akademiya则不明确\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"认为前任General Mahamatra也在当前层级中\", \"correct\": \"文档仅提到前任General Mahamatra出自Rtawahist学院，但那是过去的事，现任General Mahamatra只有Cyno一人\"}\n  ],\n  \"min_acceptable_facts\": 3,\n  \"coverage_notes\": \"题目前提'三个Matra指挥官'在所有参考文档中均无依据。文档只记录了一个General Mahamatra（Cyno）和六名普通Matra成员，无中间指挥层级的描述。因此该问题基于错误前提，文档无法提供关于'三个指挥官如何连接到Grand Sages'的信息。可回答的是实际存在的层级链：普通Matra → General Mahamatra（Cyno）→ Akademiya Sages → Lesser Lord Kusanali。\"\n}\n```", "_review_flags": [], "_needs_human_review": false, "_meta": {"question_id": "T3-M08", "tier": 3, "question": "How do the three Matra commanders connect through the organizational hierarchy of the Akademiya all the way up to the Grand Sages?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 4, "layer_b": 7, "layer_c": 0, "total": 11}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 11055, "oracle_out": 1323, "qc_in": 12738, "qc_out": 1718, "total": 26834}, "cost_usd": 0.585}}
{"question_id": "T3-M09", "_parse_error": true, "_raw": "```json\n{\n  \"question_id\": \"T3-M09\",\n  \"tier\": 3,\n  \"question_type\": \"factual\",\n  \"key_facts\": [\n    {\"fact\": \"Dottore created segments of himself using different points of his life as a basis, viewing this as his crowning achievement as a researcher.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Dottore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Each segment has its own personality and the segments often squabble with each other.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Dottore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali successfully took advantage of the segments' squabbling to coerce the segment confronting her into erasing the others in exchange for the Electro Gnosis.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Dottore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"With Dottore's assistance, the sages of Sumeru Akademiya worked to ascend Scaramouche into a new God of Wisdom ('Shouki no Kami, the Prodigal'), using the Electro Gnosis to power his new form.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"During the Tatarasuna Incident roughly 400 years ago, Dottore (posing as 'Escher') orchestrated a cruel experiment involving the murder of Niwa and perceived betrayal, which indirectly led the kabukimono to later become the Harbinger Scaramouche.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Dottore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Dottore murdered Niwa Hisahide as part of a Fatui plot at Tatarasuna, then used Niwa's disappearance to shift blame and hide his culpability, which had a large influence on Scaramouche.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Niwa Hisahide\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Nahida ensured Dottore's memory of the Niwa murder was stored in Irminsul for Scaramouche to discover during his search for records of the Descenders.\", \"doc_source\": \"[Other] Irminsul/Modifications\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Upon learning from Irminsul that his second 'betrayal' at Tatarasuna was masterminded by Dottore, Scaramouche decided to erase his existence from Irminsul, becoming the Wanderer.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Once Dottore's involvement in Scaramouche's past was revealed, Scaramouche cut ties with the Fatui and swore personal vengeance on Dottore.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Dottore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"After the Traveler and Nahida defeated Shouki no Kami and Nahida removed the Electro Gnosis, Scaramouche fell into a coma. He later recovered and, knowing Dottore had left with the two Gnoses, made a deal with Nahida to search Irminsul.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The segment deal with Nahida (erasing other segments for the Electro Gnosis) enabled Dottore to obtain the Gnosis which had originally powered Scaramouche's divine form, thus both facilitating and ending Scaramouche's ascension.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Dottore\", \"verified\": true}\n  ],\n  \"required_entities\": [\"Dottore\", \"Dottore's segments\", \"Scaramouche\", \"Wanderer\", \"Nahida\", \"Electro Gnosis\", \"Niwa Hisahide\", \"Irminsul\", \"Tatarasuna\", \"Shouki no Kami\"],\n  \"required_relations\": [\n    {\"head\": \"Dottore\", \"relation\": \"created\", \"tail\": \"segments of himself\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Dottore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Dottore's segments\", \"relation\": \"squabble_with\", \"tail\": \"each other\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Dottore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Nahida\", \"relation\": \"coerced_segment_to_erase\", \"tail\": \"other segments\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Dottore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Dottore segment\", \"relation\": \"exchanged_erasure_of_others_for\", \"tail\": \"Electro Gnosis\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Dottore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Dottore\", \"relation\": \"assisted_ascension_of\", \"tail\": \"Scaramouche (Shouki no Kami)\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Dottore (as Escher)\", \"relation\": \"murdered\", \"tail\": \"Niwa Hisahide\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Niwa Hisahide\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Dottore's experiment at Tatarasuna\", \"relation\": \"indirectly_led_to_creation_of\", \"tail\": \"Scaramouche (Harbinger)\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Dottore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Nahida\", \"relation\": \"planted_memory_in_Irminsul_for\", \"tail\": \"Scaramouche to discover Dottore's guilt\", \"doc_source\": \"[Other] Irminsul/Modifications\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Scaramouche\", \"relation\": \"erased_self_from_Irminsul_becoming\", \"tail\": \"Wanderer\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\"}\n  ],\n  \"required_reasoning_steps\": [\n    \"Recognize that Dottore's segments are independent personalities created from different life stages, not a single unified entity.\",\n    \"Understand that the segments' tendency to squabble was a vulnerability Nahida exploited: she convinced one segment to erase the others in exchange for the Electro Gnosis.\",\n    \"Connect that this Electro Gnosis was the same one Scaramouche had obtained from Yae Miko and was using to power his Shouki no Kami form — Dottore's segment deal thus facilitated both the provisioning and eventual removal of the Gnosis from Scaramouche's divine form.\",\n    \"Trace the earlier influence: a younger segment/build of Dottore (posing as Escher at Tatarasuna ~400 years ago) murdered Niwa and manipulated the kabukimono through perceived betrayal, which set the kabukimono on the path to becoming Scaramouche.\",\n    \"Recognize that Nahida strategically placed Dottore's memory of the Niwa murder in Irminsul so Scaramouche would discover the truth — this revelation drove Scaramouche to erase himself from Irminsul and become the Wanderer.\",\n    \"Synthesize the full trajectory: Dottore's segments influenced the Wanderer's fate at multiple stages — an early segment created the conditions for Scaramouche's existence, later segments assisted his divine ascension, the segment deal with Nahida enabled the Gnosis exchange that ended his divine form, and the planted memory of the early segment's crime catalyzed his transformation into the Wanderer.\"\n  ],\n  \"hallucination_traps\": [\n    {\"trap\": \"Claiming that Dottore's segments directly fought or confronted Scaramouche/Wanderer in combat.\", \"correct\": \"The segments influenced Scaramouche's fate through manipulation, deals, and planted memories, not direct combat with him.\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"Confusing which Gnosis was involved — suggesting it was the Dendro Gnosis.\", \"correct\": \"It was the Electro Gnosis that Scaramouche obtained from Yae Miko and that Dottore's segment traded the erasure of other segments for.\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"Stating that Dottore himself voluntarily revealed the Tatarasuna truth to Scar", "_review_flags": [], "_needs_human_review": false, "_meta": {"question_id": "T3-M09", "tier": 3, "question": "How did Dottore's various segment clones indirectly influence the trajectory of the Wanderer's fate?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 4, "layer_b": 7, "layer_c": 0, "total": 11}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 11340, "oracle_out": 2000, "qc_in": 13704, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 29044}, "cost_usd": 0.6757}}
{"question_id": "T3-M10", "tier": 3, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "King Deshret的文明高度发达，能够创造Primal Constructs以及巨型建筑如赤王陵（The Mausoleum of King Deshret）和哈德拉马韦特沙漠的灌溉系统，这些遗迹在沙中掩埋数百年后仍保存相对完好", "doc_source": "Sumeru/Culture", "verified": true}, {"fact": "须弥学院（Sumeru Akademiya）曾在遥远的过去对古拉巴德（Gurabad）遗址进行过考古远征，其中提到了Zandik的笔记记录了相关内容", "doc_source": "Gurabad", "verified": true}, {"fact": "法露珊（Faruzan）曾被困在与King Deshret相关的遗迹中，这些遗迹保存了她的身体和心智长达一个世纪", "doc_source": "King Deshret", "verified": true}, {"fact": "须弥沙漠中充满了来自King Deshret时代和坎瑞亚（Khaenri'ah）的遗迹", "doc_source": "Sumeru/Culture", "verified": true}, {"fact": "须弥学院是一个有千年历史的机构，由Dainsleif所述已存在超过1000年", "doc_source": "Akademiya", "verified": true}, {"fact": "阿卡夏系统（Akasha System）是大慈树王（Greater Lord Rukkhadevata）的遗产，由学院运营管理，成为收集知识的宝库", "doc_source": "Loading Screen/Sumeru", "verified": true}, {"fact": "大慈树王曾是'三永恒伴神'之一，与King Deshret和花神共治须弥，后来因King Deshret和花神密谋对抗天理而分道扬镳，独自建立了自己的文明", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "verified": true}, {"fact": "埃尔米特人（Eremites）是King Deshret臣民的后裔，现今一些埃尔米特人仍然崇拜他并希望将他复活；阿鲁村（Aaru Village）保存了他文明的余烬", "doc_source": "King Deshret", "verified": true}, {"fact": "学院的六大禁忌之一是'对深入宇宙之外的探索'（Delving beyond the universe），这与King Deshret和花神试图对抗天理、使用禁忌知识的历史教训相关", "doc_source": "Akademiya", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["King Deshret", "Sumeru Akademiya", "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "Nabu Malikata", "Gurabad", "Eremites", "Aaru Village", "Faruzan", "Primal Constructs", "Akasha System", "Forbidden Knowledge"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Sumeru Akademiya", "relation": "conducted archaeological expedition to", "tail": "Gurabad", "doc_source": "Gurabad"}, {"head": "King Deshret", "relation": "created/built", "tail": "Primal Constructs and desert architecture", "doc_source": "King Deshret"}, {"head": "King Deshret", "relation": "subjects descended into", "tail": "Eremites", "doc_source": "King Deshret"}, {"head": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "relation": "parted ways with", "tail": "King Deshret", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata"}, {"head": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "relation": "created", "tail": "Akasha System", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata"}, {"head": "Sumeru Akademiya", "relation": "operated and maintained", "tail": "Akasha System", "doc_source": "Loading Screen/Sumeru"}, {"head": "Faruzan", "relation": "was trapped in ruins related to", "tail": "King Deshret", "doc_source": "King Deshret"}, {"head": "King Deshret's civilization", "relation": "ruins preserved in", "tail": "Sumeru desert", "doc_source": "Sumeru/Culture"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "误认为学院直接继承了King Deshret的文明或政权", "correct": "学院由大慈树王的传统发展而来，与King Deshret的沙漠文明是分离的；学院通过考古远征研究沙漠遗迹，而非直接继承"}, {"trap": "混淆学院的Zandik笔记考古远征与其他学术活动", "correct": "文档明确记载学院在遥远的过去对Gurabad进行了考古远征，并在Zandik的笔记中有所记录"}, {"trap": "误认为Akasha系统是King Deshret的遗产", "correct": "Akasha系统是Greater Lord Rukkhadevata的遗产，由她在大灾变前创造，学院后来运营管理"}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "文档中关于学院对沙漠遗迹进行考古研究的细节较为有限，仅提及了对Gurabad的远征和Zandik的笔记；缺少学院具体如何系统性研究King Deshret技术（如Primal Constructs）的详细描述；学院六大禁忌与沙漠文明覆灭教训之间的直接因果关系在文档中未被明确阐述，仅可从上下文推断", "_review_flags": ["key_facts[4]: high-risk pattern — 须弥学院是一个有千年历史的机构，由Dainsleif所述已存在超过1000年", "coverage_notes: 文档中关于学院对沙漠遗迹进行考古研究的细节较为有限，仅提及了对Gurabad的远征和Zandik的笔记；缺少学院具体如何系统性研究King Deshret技术（如Primal Constructs）的"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T3-M10", "tier": 3, "question": "How does the ancient desert civilization of Sumeru (e.g. the kingdom of Deshret) connect through archaeological evidence to the modern Akademiya?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 4, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 0, "total": 12}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 11979, "oracle_out": 1696, "qc_in": 14035, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 29710}, "cost_usd": 0.6674}}
{"question_id": "T3-M11", "tier": 3, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Benben is a mysterious mechanical construct found in the ruins at Abdju Pit, which were part of King Deshret's ancient civilization.", "doc_source": "NPC/Benben", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Benben had a special connection to the doors throughout King Deshret's ruins and seemed familiar with the inside of Khemenu Temple.", "doc_source": "NPC/Benben", "verified": true}, {"fact": "King Deshret's civilization was highly advanced, capable of creating Primal Constructs and colossal structures such as The Mausoleum of King Deshret.", "doc_source": "Sumeru/Culture", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Benben's model is that of the central core seen on Primal Constructs, without the additional triangular frame or combat accessories.", "doc_source": "NPC/Benben", "verified": true}, {"fact": "King Deshret was one of the Three Eternal Companion-Gods in ancient Sumeru, reigning alongside Greater Lord Rukkhadevata, who was the previous Dendro Archon.", "doc_source": "NPC/King Deshret", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Sumeru Akademiya is Sumeru's main governing body and most prestigious institute of learning, and its leader includes Lesser Lord Kusanali (Nahida), who succeeded Greater Lord Rukkhadevata as Dendro Archon.", "doc_source": "Concept/Akademiya", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Akademiya's knowledge system was originally powered by the Gnosis of Greater Lord Rukkhadevata through the Akasha system.", "doc_source": "Sumeru/Culture", "verified": true}, {"fact": "King Deshret built his domain in the desert, and the Eremites are descended from his subjects. Embers of his civilization were preserved in the form of Aaru Village.", "doc_source": "NPC/King Deshret", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Tirzad, a researcher associated with the Akademiya, was researching King Deshret's ruins using the Scarlet Sand Slate; Jebrael noted that Tirzad's opinion of King Deshret was based on what he had been told by the Akademiya.", "doc_source": "Other/Golden Slumber", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Akademiya has the sin of 'Delving beyond the universe' and other prohibitions, and Sumeru Akademiya conducted an expedition to Gurabad (a city of King Deshret's era) in the distant past.", "doc_source": "Concept/Gurabad", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Benben", "King Deshret", "Primal Constructs", "Sumeru Akademiya", "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "Scarlet Sand Slate", "Abdju Pit", "Khemenu Temple", "Tirzad", "Eremites"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Benben", "relation": "originates_from_civilization_of", "tail": "King Deshret", "doc_source": "NPC/Benben"}, {"head": "Benben", "relation": "is_variant_of", "tail": "Primal Constructs", "doc_source": "NPC/Benben"}, {"head": "King Deshret", "relation": "was_companion_god_with", "tail": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "doc_source": "NPC/King Deshret"}, {"head": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "relation": "was_previous_archon_of", "tail": "Sumeru Akademiya", "doc_source": "Sumeru/Culture"}, {"head": "Sumeru Akademiya", "relation": "studies_ruins_of", "tail": "King Deshret", "doc_source": "Other/Golden Slumber"}, {"head": "Tirzad", "relation": "represents_academic_perspective_of", "tail": "Sumeru Akademiya", "doc_source": "Other/Golden Slumber"}, {"head": "King Deshret", "relation": "created", "tail": "Primal Constructs", "doc_source": "Sumeru/Culture"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Claiming Benben was created by the Akademiya or is an Akademiya research product.", "correct": "Benben is a construct from King Deshret's ancient civilization, found in his ruins at Abdju Pit, and is a variant of the Primal Constructs created by that civilization."}, {"trap": "Stating that King Deshret and the Akademiya coexisted or that Deshret founded the Akademiya.", "correct": "King Deshret died thousands of years before the events of the story. The Akademiya is linked to Deshret's civilization indirectly through Greater Lord Rukkhadevata (his former companion god and previous Dendro Archon) and through the Akademiya's scholarly study of his ruins."}, {"trap": "Confusing Lesser Lord Kusanali (Nahida) with Greater Lord Rukkhadevata as the historical link.", "correct": "The historical connection runs through Greater Lord Rukkhadevata, who was one of the Three Eternal Companion-Gods alongside King Deshret and whose Gnosis powered the Akasha system. Kusanali is the current Dendro Archon who succeeded Rukkhadevata."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "The documents provide strong coverage of Benben's association with King Deshret's civilization and the indirect chain connecting Deshret to the Akademiya via Greater Lord Rukkhadevata. However, Benben's specific original purpose or exact creation context within Deshret's civilization is not detailed in the documents beyond it being a Primal Construct variant found in his ruins.", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: The documents provide strong coverage of Benben's association with King Deshret's civilization and t"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T3-M11", "tier": 3, "question": "What ancient civilization is associated with Benben in the Golden Slumber world quest ruins, and how does that civilization indirectly connect to the modern Sumeru Akademiya?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 4, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 0, "total": 12}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 12189, "oracle_out": 1553, "qc_in": 14102, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 29844}, "cost_usd": 0.6608}}
{"question_id": "T3-M12", "_parse_error": true, "_raw": "{\n  \"question_id\": \"T3-M12\",\n  \"tier\": 3,\n  \"question_type\": \"factual\",\n  \"key_facts\": [\n    {\"fact\": \"The Wanderer (as kabukimono) was originally Ei's prototype puppet, created by Raiden Ei.\", \"doc_source\": \"Wanderer/Lore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"At Tatarasuna, the wanderer was taken in by Katsuragi and came to view the group (Katsuragi, Kinjirou, Nozomu, Miyazaki, Nagamasa) as his 'family.'\", \"doc_source\": \"Kinjirou\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Nagamasa discovered the wanderer's true nature and did something to him, leading to the wanderer's disappearance from Tatarasuna — this was considered his second 'betrayal.'\", \"doc_source\": \"Nozomu\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"After surviving his encounter with Nagamasa, the wanderer encountered a young boy who died of unknown reasons (presumably illness), which he considered his third 'betrayal.'\", \"doc_source\": \"Nozomu\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"These 'three betrayals' left him jaded with the world and led him to join the Fatui, eventually becoming the Sixth of the Eleven Fatui Harbingers, 'Balladeer' Scaramouche.\", \"doc_source\": \"Nozomu\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"During the Unreconciled Stars event, Scaramouche traveled to Liyue to investigate mysterious meteorites and entered a dream where he realized that the stars and sky are a 'lie,' sent by 'The Jester' without forewarning.\", \"doc_source\": \"Wanderer (NPC/Scaramouche)\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"He later headed to Inazuma to oversee the creation of Delusions at a secret facility and obtained Ei's Gnosis from Yae Miko in exchange for the Traveler's safety.\", \"doc_source\": \"Wanderer (NPC/Scaramouche)\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"After obtaining the Gnosis and Signora's death, Scaramouche cut off contact with the Fatui, causing them to believe he had gone rogue.\", \"doc_source\": \"Wanderer (NPC/Scaramouche)\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"With Dottore's assistance, the sages of Sumeru Akademiya worked to ascend Scaramouche into a new God of Wisdom under the name 'Shouki no Kami, the Prodigal,' using the Electro Gnosis to power his new form.\", \"doc_source\": \"Wanderer (NPC/Scaramouche)\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"After his defeat by the Traveler and Nahida removing the Electro Gnosis, Scaramouche fell into a coma and was placed into Nahida's custody.\", \"doc_source\": \"Wanderer (NPC/Scaramouche)\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Upon recovery, he made a deal with Nahida to search Irminsul on her behalf; during this investigation, he discovered that his second 'betrayal' at Tatarasuna was masterminded by Dottore, leading him to erase his existence from Irminsul.\", \"doc_source\": \"Wanderer (NPC/Scaramouche)\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Wanderer came into existence after his previous incarnation expunged his appellations and histories from Irminsul; he harbors his former self's memories after willingly regaining them.\", \"doc_source\": \"PlayableCharacter Wanderer\", \"verified\": true}\n  ],\n  \"required_entities\": [\"Wanderer\", \"Scaramouche\", \"Raiden Ei\", \"Katsuragi\", \"Tatarasuna\", \"Fatui\", \"Dottore\", \"Nahida\", \"Yae Miko\", \"Electro Gnosis\", \"Sumeru Akademiya\", \"Irminsul\", \"Shouki no Kami\"],\n  \"required_relations\": [\n    {\"head\": \"Raiden Ei\", \"relation\": \"created\", \"tail\": \"Wanderer (prototype puppet)\", \"doc_source\": \"Kinjirou\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Katsuragi\", \"relation\": \"took in / befriended\", \"tail\": \"Wanderer (kabukimono)\", \"doc_source\": \"Kinjirou\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Nagamasa\", \"relation\": \"caused second betrayal of\", \"tail\": \"Wanderer\", \"doc_source\": \"Nozomu\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Young boy's death\", \"relation\": \"constituted third betrayal experienced by\", \"tail\": \"Wanderer\", \"doc_source\": \"Nozomu\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Three betrayals\", \"relation\": \"motivated joining\", \"tail\": \"Fatui\", \"doc_source\": \"Nozomu\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Scaramouche\", \"relation\": \"obtained Gnosis from\", \"tail\": \"Yae Miko\", \"doc_source\": \"Wanderer (NPC/Scaramouche)\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Scaramouche\", \"relation\": \"went rogue from\", \"tail\": \"Fatui\", \"doc_source\": \"Wanderer (NPC/Scaramouche)\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Dottore\", \"relation\": \"assisted Sumeru Akademiya sages to ascend\", \"tail\": \"Scaramouche as Shouki no Kami\", \"doc_source\": \"Wanderer (NPC/Scaramouche)\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Dottore\", \"relation\": \"masterminded the Tatarasuna incident (second betrayal) against\", \"tail\": \"Wanderer\", \"doc_source\": \"Wanderer (NPC/Scaramouche)\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Scaramouche\", \"relation\": \"erased existence from\", \"tail\": \"Irminsul\", \"doc_source\": \"Wanderer (NPC/Scaramouche)\"}\n  ],\n  \"required_reasoning_steps\": [\n    \"Identify that the Wanderer's pre-Fatui independent experiences include the Tatarasuna events (second betrayal by Nagamasa) and the young boy's death (third betrayal).\",\n    \"Connect these 'three betrayals' to his embittered worldview and motivation for joining the Fatui.\",\n    \"Trace his trajectory through Liyue (Unreconciled Stars meteorite investigation), Inazuma (overseeing Delusion factory, obtaining Gnosis), and his subsequent break from the Fatui.\",\n    \"Explain how possessing the Electro Gnosis and going rogue from the Fatui directly enabled his collaboration with Dottore and the Sumeru Akademiya sages to attempt godhood as Shouki no Kami.\",\n    \"Note that his discovery that Dottore orchestrated the Tatarasuna incident — the very betrayal that set him on his dark path — triggered his decision to erase himself from Irminsul, leading to his rebirth as the Wanderer.\"\n  ],\n  \"hallucination_traps\": [\n    {\"trap\": \"Claiming the Wanderer voluntarily joined Dottore's plan in Sumeru out of loyalty to the Fatui.\", \"correct\": \"Scaramouche had already cut off contact with the Fatui and gone rogue before Dottore and the sages worked with him on the Shouki no Kami project.\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"Confusing which Gnosis powered Shouki no Kami — stating it was a Dendro Gnosis.\", \"correct\": \"It was the Electro Gnosis (obtained from Yae Miko in Inazuma) that powered his Shouki no Kami form.\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"Stating that the Wanderer's second betrayal was caused by the young boy's death.\", \"correct\": \"The second betrayal was Nagamasa's actions at Tatarasuna (", "_review_flags": [], "_needs_human_review": false, "_meta": {"question_id": "T3-M12", "tier": 3, "question": "Before joining the Fatui, the Wanderer acted independently across multiple regions. How did those experiences set the stage for his later actions in Sumeru?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 4, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 0, "total": 12}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 11904, "oracle_out": 2000, "qc_in": 14267, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 30171}, "cost_usd": 0.6926}}
{"question_id": "T3-M13", "_parse_error": true, "_raw": "```json\n{\n  \"question_id\": \"T3-M13\",\n  \"tier\": 3,\n  \"question_type\": \"factual\",\n  \"key_facts\": [\n    {\"fact\": \"The Key of Khaj-Nisut's lore tells the story of a wandering prince (Xiphos) whose kingdom was lost. His mother, a queen, burned his gilded robes and crown and had him escape in servant's sackcloth.\", \"doc_source\": \"[Weapon] Key of Khaj-Nisut\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The story takes place 'after the Lord of Sand's dreams fell apart and the Grandmaster of Verdure hid the whispers of the demonic skies away' — referring to King Deshret and Greater Lord Rukkhadevata respectively.\", \"doc_source\": \"[Weapon] Key of Khaj-Nisut\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The 'ears of decay' broke the great divine realm into many kingdoms before grinding them all into sand, describing the fragmentation of the desert civilization after King Deshret's fall.\", \"doc_source\": \"[Weapon] Key of Khaj-Nisut\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Xiphos was reduced from a prince to the son of a slave market ruler, then to a wanderer who lost everything, before becoming the apprentice of a blind poet.\", \"doc_source\": \"[Weapon] Key of Khaj-Nisut\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The blind poet recognized Xiphos as 'the one favored by the Jinni' and 'the prince of the once-lost kingdom' who wields the Key of Khaj-Nisut, calling it the key to paradise's gate, tasked with rebuilding the kingdom 'amidst emeralds and pomegranates'.\", \"doc_source\": \"[Weapon] Key of Khaj-Nisut\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Jinni (Jinn) were created by Nabu Malikata, the Goddess of Flowers, who was one of the three God-Kings of Sumeru alongside King Deshret and Greater Lord Rukkhadevata.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Nabu Malikata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Khaj-Nisut is an actual location in modern Sumeru, situated in the Land of Lower Setekh subarea of the Great Red Sand.\", \"doc_source\": \"[Location] Sumeru\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"King Deshret, Greater Lord Rukkhadevata, and Nabu Malikata were known as the three God-Kings of Sumeru; they were friends who each pursued their own paths towards 'wisdom'.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Nabu Malikata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata was the original Dendro Archon of Sumeru, and her successor Lesser Lord Kusanali is the current Dendro Archon. At the end of the Sumeru Archon Quests, all memories of Rukkhadevata were erased from Teyvat.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Nabu Malikata and King Deshret built the ancient civilization of Ay-Khanoum in the desert as an earthly paradise.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Nabu Malikata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Sabzeruz Festival was originated and named by Nabu Malikata to commemorate Greater Lord Rukkhadevata's birthday; after Rukkhadevata's death, it became a celebration for Lesser Lord Kusanali's birthday — connecting the ancient era directly to modern Sumeru festival culture.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Nabu Malikata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Eremites are a faction of mercenaries from Sumeru's desert who are descendants/inheritors of the desert civilization's legacy, and some wield 'bizarre yet formidable powers'.\", \"doc_source\": \"[Location] Sumeru\", \"verified\": true}\n  ],\n  \"required_entities\": [\"Key of Khaj-Nisut\", \"Xiphos\", \"King Deshret\", \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"Nabu Malikata\", \"Jinni\", \"Khaj-Nisut\", \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"Sumeru\", \"Ay-Khanoum\", \"Sabzeruz Festival\"],\n  \"required_relations\": [\n    {\"head\": \"Key of Khaj-Nisut\", \"relation\": \"lore_protagonist\", \"tail\": \"Xiphos\", \"doc_source\": \"[Weapon] Key of Khaj-Nisut\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Key of Khaj-Nisut lore\", \"relation\": \"set_after_fall_of\", \"tail\": \"King Deshret\", \"doc_source\": \"[Weapon] Key of Khaj-Nisut\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Xiphos\", \"relation\": \"favored_by\", \"tail\": \"Jinni\", \"doc_source\": \"[Weapon] Key of Khaj-Nisut\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Nabu Malikata\", \"relation\": \"creator_of\", \"tail\": \"Jinni\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Nabu Malikata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"King Deshret\", \"relation\": \"co-ruler_with\", \"tail\": \"Nabu Malikata\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Nabu Malikata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"King Deshret\", \"relation\": \"co-ruler_with\", \"tail\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Nabu Malikata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"relation\": \"predecessor_of\", \"tail\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Nabu Malikata\", \"relation\": \"originator_of\", \"tail\": \"Sabzeruz Festival\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Nabu Malikata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Khaj-Nisut\", \"relation\": \"located_in\", \"tail\": \"Land of Lower Setekh, Sumeru\", \"doc_source\": \"[Location] Sumeru\"}\n  ],\n  \"required_reasoning_steps\": [],\n  \"hallucination_traps\": [\n    {\"trap\": \"Confusing the 'Lord of Sand' in the weapon lore with a generic title rather than identifying it as King Deshret.\", \"correct\": \"The 'Lord of Sand' refers to King Deshret, one of the three God-Kings of Sumeru.\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"Assuming Xiphos is the blind poet rather than the wandering prince.\", \"correct\": \"Xiphos is the wandering prince; the blind poet is his unnamed master who recognizes his destiny.\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"Claiming the 'Grandmaster of Verdure' refers to Lesser Lord Kusanali.\", \"correct\": \"The 'Grandmaster of Verdure' refers to Greater Lord Rukkhadevata, the original Dendro Archon, not her successor Kusanali.\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"Stating that the Jinni were created by King Deshret.\", \"correct\": \"The Jinni were created by Nabu Malikata, the Goddess of Flowers.\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"Confusing Khaj-Nisut (the place) with the weapon Key of Khaj-Nisut as if they are unrelated.\", \"correct\": \"Khaj-Nisut is an actual location in the Land of Lower Setekh in Sumeru, and the weapon is named as the 'key' to that place, tying the weapon's lore to a real in-game location.\"}\n  ],\n  \"min_acceptable_facts\": 3,\n  \"coverage_notes\": \"The documents do not provide explicit details on: (1) what happened to Xiphos after his wanderings — whether he succeeded in rebuilding the kingdom; (2", "_review_flags": [], "_needs_human_review": false, "_meta": {"question_id": "T3-M13", "tier": 3, "question": "What historical story underlies the lore of the Sumeru weapon \"Key of Khaj-Nisut\", and how do the key figures in that story indirectly connect to modern Sumeru?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 3, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 0, "total": 11}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 10698, "oracle_out": 2000, "qc_in": 13061, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 27759}, "cost_usd": 0.6564}}
{"question_id": "T4-E01", "_parse_error": true, "_raw": "```json\n{\n  \"question_id\": \"T4-E01\",\n  \"tier\": 4,\n  \"question_type\": \"factual\",\n  \"key_facts\": [\n    {\"fact\": \"The Wanderer (originally known as 'kabukimono') is a puppet created by Raiden Ei, specifically described as Ei's prototype puppet.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"While patrolling Nazuchi Beach, Katsuragi encountered the kabukimono (inside Shakkei Pavilion during a cave-in investigation) and brought him back to Tatarasuna, where swordsmiths took him in as family.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Niwa Hisahide\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"At Tatarasuna, Niwa Hisahide reassured the kabukimono that he was human but simply lacked a 'heart.' The group (Katsuragi, Kinjirou, Nozomu, Miyazaki) became like family to the wanderer.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Niwa Hisahide\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Il Dottore (posing as 'Escher,' a Fontaine mechanic) orchestrated a cruel experiment at Tatarasuna: his smelting process released Tatarigami from Crystal Marrow, causing sickness and death among workers.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Niwa Hisahide\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"While the kabukimono left for Narukami Island to seek the Raiden Shogun's aid, Dottore fatally wounded Niwa Hisahide and used Niwa's disappearance to shift blame, hiding his own culpability.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Niwa Hisahide\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The kabukimono's 'second betrayal' was masterminded by Dottore at Tatarasuna. He also experienced a 'third betrayal' when a young boy he encountered died of presumably illness. These events left him jaded with the world.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Kinjirou\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The three 'betrayals' led the kabukimono to join the Fatui, where he eventually became the Sixth of the Eleven Fatui Harbingers with the codename 'The Balladeer' (Scaramouche/Kunikuzushi).\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Kinjirou\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Scaramouche obtained the Electro Gnosis from Yae Miko in Inazuma and then cut off contact with the Fatui after Signora's death, going rogue.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"With Dottore's assistance, the sages of Sumeru Akademiya worked to ascend Scaramouche into a new God of Wisdom under the name 'Shouki no Kami, the Prodigal.'\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Traveler and Nahida defeated Shouki no Kami; Nahida removed the Electro Gnosis powering his form, causing him to fall into a coma. Nahida put him into her custody.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"After recovering, Scaramouche made a deal with Nahida to search Irminsul on her behalf. During the investigation, Nahida left behind the true events of Tatarasuna for him to discover.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Scaramouche was disgusted to learn that his second 'betrayal' was masterminded by Dottore and decided to erase his existence from Irminsul, thus becoming the Wanderer.\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Wanderer came into existence in place of his previous incarnation after the latter expunged his previous appellations and their respective histories from Irminsul. He later willingly regained his memories.\", \"doc_source\": \"[PlayableCharacter] Wanderer\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"'Wanderer' is now the only title he goes by, for he has no home, kin, or destination. Nahida enrolled him at Vahumana under the name 'Hat Guy.'\", \"doc_source\": \"[PlayableCharacter] Wanderer\", \"verified\": true}\n  ],\n  \"required_entities\": [\n    \"Wanderer\",\n    \"Scaramouche\",\n    \"Kabukimono\",\n    \"Raiden Ei\",\n    \"Katsuragi\",\n    \"Niwa Hisahide\",\n    \"Il Dottore\",\n    \"Nahida\",\n    \"Tatarasuna\",\n    \"Electro Gnosis\",\n    \"Irminsul\",\n    \"Fatui\",\n    \"Shouki no Kami\",\n    \"Yae Miko\",\n    \"Kinjirou\",\n    \"Nozomu\"\n  ],\n  \"required_relations\": [\n    {\"head\": \"Raiden Ei\", \"relation\": \"created (prototype puppet)\", \"tail\": \"Kabukimono\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Katsuragi\", \"relation\": \"discovered and brought to Tatarasuna\", \"tail\": \"Kabukimono\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Niwa Hisahide\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Niwa Hisahide\", \"relation\": \"reassured and cared for\", \"tail\": \"Kabukimono\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Niwa Hisahide\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Il Dottore\", \"relation\": \"orchestrated betrayal/murdered\", \"tail\": \"Niwa Hisahide\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Niwa Hisahide\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Il Dottore\", \"relation\": \"masterminded second betrayal of\", \"tail\": \"Kabukimono\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Kabukimono\", \"relation\": \"joined as Sixth Harbinger (Balladeer)\", \"tail\": \"Fatui\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Kinjirou\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Yae Miko\", \"relation\": \"gave Electro Gnosis to\", \"tail\": \"Scaramouche\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Scaramouche\", \"relation\": \"defected from\", \"tail\": \"Fatui\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Sumeru Akademiya sages + Dottore\", \"relation\": \"ascended into Shouki no Kami\", \"tail\": \"Scaramouche\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Nahida\", \"relation\": \"defeated and removed Gnosis from\", \"tail\": \"Shouki no Kami\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Nahida\", \"relation\": \"took into custody after coma\", \"tail\": \"Scaramouche\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Scaramouche\", \"relation\": \"erased own existence from\", \"tail\": \"Irminsul\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Wanderer\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Scaramouche\", \"relation\": \"became\", \"tail\": \"Wanderer\", \"doc_source\": \"[PlayableCharacter] Wanderer\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Nahida\", \"relation\": \"enrolled at Vahumana as 'Hat Guy'\", \"tail\": \"Wanderer\", \"doc_source\": \"[PlayableCharacter] Wanderer\"}\n  ],\n  \"required_reasoning_", "_review_flags": [], "_needs_human_review": false, "_meta": {"question_id": "T4-E01", "tier": 4, "question": "Trace the complete chain of key entities and relationships in the Wanderer's journey — from creation, abandonment, joining the Fatui, defection, to finally becoming the Wanderer.", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 6, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 6, "total": 20}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 21224, "oracle_out": 2000, "qc_in": 23587, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 48811}, "cost_usd": 0.9722}}
{"question_id": "T4-E02", "_parse_error": true, "_raw": "```json\n{\n  \"question_id\": \"T4-E02\",\n  \"tier\": 4,\n  \"question_type\": \"factual\",\n  \"key_facts\": [\n    {\"fact\": \"花神纳布·马利卡塔（Goddess of Flowers / Nabu Malikata）最初构想了庆典，目的是为朋友大慈树王（Greater Lord Rukkhadevata）庆祝生日\", \"doc_source\": \"[Concept] Sabzeruz Festival\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"赤王（King Deshret）参与了最初的花神节宴会，在宴会上弹奏乐器，并赠送了Wedjat Eye给大慈树王\", \"doc_source\": \"[Concept] Sabzeruz Festival\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"花神纳布·马利卡塔在宴会上翩翩起舞，帕蒂沙兰花在她脚步所到之处盛开，并赠送了Khvarena给大慈树王\", \"doc_source\": \"[Concept] Sabzeruz Festival\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"大慈树王（Greater Lord Rukkhadevata）是最初花神节的庆祝对象，节日为庆祝她的生日\", \"doc_source\": \"[Concept] Sabzeruz Festival\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"大慈树王去世后，花神节转为庆祝小吉祥草王（Lesser Lord Kusanali / Nahida）的生日，即贤者们发现她的那一天\", \"doc_source\": \"[Concept] Sabzeruz Festival\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"须弥教令院（Sumeru Akademiya）的高层在大慈树王去世后停止组织花神节，Dunyarzad推测是因为他们将小吉祥草王的诞生视为大慈树王死亡的象征\", \"doc_source\": \"[Concept] Sabzeruz Festival\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"教令院严重边缘化花神节，拒绝提供资金，甚至愿意完全取消花神节最重要的活动——花神之舞（Dance of Sabzeruz）\", \"doc_source\": \"[Concept] Sabzeruz Festival\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"大贤者阿扎尔（Grand Sage Azar）以违反法律为由强行提前关闭了花神节，并宣布从下一个Jnagarbha Day起禁止所有公共艺术表演\", \"doc_source\": \"[Quest] The Coming of the Sabzeruz Festival\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"妮露（Nilou）是祖拜尔剧院的舞者，负责在花神节表演花神之舞\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Parisa\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Dunyarzad是花神节的赞助者和积极参与者，她身患Eleazar末期，希望在去世前不留遗憾地参与花神节\", \"doc_source\": \"[Quest] The Coming of the Sabzeruz Festival\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"迪希雅（Dehya）是Dunyarzad的雇佣护卫，负责在花神节期间保护她，她还卖掉了自己的旧大剑来捐助花神节\", \"doc_source\": \"[Quest] The Coming of the Sabzeruz Festival\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"小吉祥草王（Nahida）是花神节庆祝的神明对象，她在花神节的梦境轮回（samsara）中揭示了真相，并帮助旅行者打破轮回\", \"doc_source\": \"[Quest] The End of the Sabzeruz Festival\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"谢赫·祖拜尔（Sheikh Zubayr）是祖拜尔剧院的经理，擅长编剧、编舞和制作道具，为花神节表演提供支持\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Parisa\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Vihar在花神节期间经营Yalda Candy摊位，由Dunyarzad赞助，让孩子们享受节日\", \"doc_source\": \"[Quest] The Continuation of the Sabzeruz Festival\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"在小吉祥草王获救并重新确立为须弥神明后，花神节恢复了其声望和支持，教令院也愿意为女神举办盛大的生日庆典\", \"doc_source\": \"[Concept] Sabzeruz Festival\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Setaria是大贤者阿扎尔的秘书，在花神节关闭事件中随同阿扎尔出现\", \"doc_source\": \"[Quest] The Coming of the Sabzeruz Festival\", \"verified\": true}\n  ],\n  \"required_entities\": [\"Sabzeruz Festival\", \"Nabu Malikata (Goddess of Flowers)\", \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"King Deshret\", \"Lesser Lord Kusanali (Nahida)\", \"Sumeru Akademiya\", \"Grand Sage Azar\", \"Setaria\", \"Nilou\", \"Sheikh Zubayr\", \"Zubayr Theater\", \"Dunyarzad\", \"Dehya\", \"Vihar\", \"Traveler\", \"Paimon\", \"Dance of Sabzeruz\"],\n  \"required_relations\": [\n    {\"head\": \"Nabu Malikata\", \"relation\": \"构想/创立\", \"tail\": \"Sabzeruz Festival\", \"doc_source\": \"[Concept] Sabzeruz Festival\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Sabzeruz Festival\", \"relation\": \"最初庆祝对象\", \"tail\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"doc_source\": \"[Concept] Sabzeruz Festival\"},\n    {\"head\": \"King Deshret\", \"relation\": \"共同策划首次庆典\", \"tail\": \"Nabu Malikata\", \"doc_source\": \"[Concept] Sabzeruz Festival\"},\n    {\"head\": \"King Deshret\", \"relation\": \"赠礼Wedjat Eye给\", \"tail\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"doc_source\": \"[Concept] Sabzeruz Festival\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Nabu Malikata\", \"relation\": \"赠礼Khvarena给\", \"tail\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"doc_source\": \"[Concept] Sabzeruz Festival\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Sabzeruz Festival\", \"relation\": \"后转为庆祝\", \"tail\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"doc_source\": \"[Concept] Sabzeruz Festival\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Sumeru Akademiya\", \"relation\": \"边缘化/拒绝资助\", \"tail\": \"Sabzeruz Festival\", \"doc_source\": \"[Concept] Sabzeruz Festival\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Grand Sage Azar\", \"relation\": \"强行关闭\", \"tail\": \"Sabzeruz Festival\", \"doc_source\": \"[Quest] The Coming of the Sabzeruz Festival\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Setaria\", \"relation\": \"秘书\", \"tail\": \"Grand Sage Azar\", \"doc_source\": \"[Quest] The Coming of the Sabzeruz Festival\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Nilou\", \"relation\": \"表演花神之舞于\", \"tail\": \"Sabzer", "_review_flags": [], "_needs_human_review": false, "_meta": {"question_id": "T4-E02", "tier": 4, "question": "Who were all the stakeholders behind the Sabzeruz Festival in Sumeru, what were their respective goals, and what was the web of relationships between them?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 5, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 6, "total": 19}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 18662, "oracle_out": 2000, "qc_in": 21025, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 43687}, "cost_usd": 0.8953}}
{"question_id": "T4-E03", "tier": 4, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata was the original Dendro Archon of Sumeru and held the title of God of Wisdom, implying she originally held the Dendro Gnosis as the Dendro Archon.", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata died during the cataclysm 500 years ago. Before her death, she created the Akasha System and her next incarnation, Lesser Lord Kusanali, who then ascended as the current Dendro Archon.", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Lesser Lord Kusanali (Nahida) is the current Dendro Archon and God of Wisdom, succeeding Greater Lord Rukkhadevata.", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Each Archon possesses a magic focus called a Gnosis, which allows them to resonate directly with Celestia and acts as a symbol of an Archon's status.", "doc_source": "The Seven", "verified": true}, {"fact": "With Dottore's assistance, the sages of Sumeru Akademiya worked to ascend Scaramouche into a new God of Wisdom under the name 'Shouki no Kami, the Prodigal.' The Electro Gnosis was used to power his new form.", "doc_source": "Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Scaramouche had obtained the Electro Gnosis (from Yae Miko in Inazuma) and cut off contact with the Fatui after Signora's death.", "doc_source": "Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Nahida removed the Electro Gnosis powering Scaramouche's mechanical form during the battle, causing him to fall and enter a coma.", "doc_source": "Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "After Scaramouche's defeat, Dottore left with the two Gnoses (the Electro Gnosis and, implicitly, the Dendro Gnosis obtained through negotiation with Nahida).", "doc_source": "Wanderer", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Scaramouche knew he had no allies to rely on as Dottore had left with the two Gnoses, implying Nahida relinquished her Dendro Gnosis to Dottore.", "doc_source": "Wanderer", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "Nahida", "Scaramouche", "Il Dottore", "Electro Gnosis", "Dendro Gnosis", "Fatui"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "relation": "originally held position of Dendro Archon (implying Dendro Gnosis)", "tail": "Dendro Gnosis", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata"}, {"head": "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "relation": "succeeded as Dendro Archon and inherited", "tail": "Dendro Gnosis", "doc_source": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata"}, {"head": "Scaramouche", "relation": "was powered by", "tail": "Electro Gnosis", "doc_source": "Wanderer"}, {"head": "Nahida", "relation": "removed from Scaramouche", "tail": "Electro Gnosis", "doc_source": "Wanderer"}, {"head": "Il Dottore", "relation": "departed with both", "tail": "Electro Gnosis and Dendro Gnosis", "doc_source": "Wanderer"}, {"head": "Nahida", "relation": "relinquished to Dottore", "tail": "Dendro Gnosis", "doc_source": "Wanderer"}], "required_reasoning_steps": [], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Confusing the Electro Gnosis used to power Scaramouche's form with the Dendro Gnosis — Scaramouche was powered by the Electro Gnosis, not the Dendro Gnosis.", "correct": "Scaramouche's Shouki no Kami form was powered by the Electro Gnosis which he had obtained from Yae Miko in Inazuma. Nahida removed the Electro Gnosis from him during battle."}, {"trap": "Claiming Scaramouche held or was associated with the Dendro Gnosis.", "correct": "Scaramouche was associated with the Electro Gnosis, not the Dendro Gnosis. The Dendro Gnosis was held by the Dendro Archons (Rukkhadevata, then Kusanali) before being given to Dottore."}, {"trap": "Stating that Nahida still possesses the Dendro Gnosis after the Sumeru Archon Quest.", "correct": "The documents indicate Dottore left with 'the two Gnoses,' meaning Nahida gave up the Dendro Gnosis to Dottore as part of their dealings."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "The provided documents do not contain the explicit scene or dialogue where Nahida negotiates with Dottore and hands over the Dendro Gnosis. This is only implied by the statement that 'Dottore had left with the two Gnoses.' The exact terms of the deal between Nahida and Dottore are not detailed in these documents. Additionally, the documents do not explicitly state that Greater Lord Rukkhadevata held a Dendro Gnosis — this is inferred from her status as Dendro Archon and the general rule that each Archon possesses a Gnosis.", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: The provided documents do not contain the explicit scene or dialogue where Nahida negotiates with Do"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T4-E03", "tier": 4, "question": "List all entities that have held or been associated with the Dendro Gnosis (God's Heart), and describe what happened to each.", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 6, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 6, "total": 20}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 21940, "oracle_out": 1534, "qc_in": 23835, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 49309}, "cost_usd": 0.9517}}
{"question_id": "T4-E04", "_parse_error": true, "_raw": "```json\n{\n  \"question_id\": \"T4-E04\",\n  \"tier\": 4,\n  \"question_type\": \"factual\",\n  \"key_facts\": [\n    {\"fact\": \"The Seven Sovereigns originally held the seven elemental Authorities. In Sumeru, Apep held the Dendro elemental Authority.\", \"doc_source\": \"Timeline\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Heavenly Principles descended on the world and took a portion of the Seven Sovereigns' elemental Authorities for itself, then defeated the Sovereigns after 40 years of war.\", \"doc_source\": \"Timeline\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata was the original Dendro Archon of Sumeru, the avatar of Irminsul, and held the title of God of Wisdom.\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata co-reigned with King Deshret and Nabu Malikata as 'The Three Eternal Companion-Gods' in ancient Sumeru.\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"During the cataclysm 500 years ago, Greater Lord Rukkhadevata was slain. Before her death, she created the Akasha System to purge forbidden knowledge from Irminsul and created her next incarnation, Lesser Lord Kusanali.\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali (Nahida) ascended as the current Dendro Archon and God of Wisdom after Greater Lord Rukkhadevata's death.\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Nahida is a playable Dendro character. As Lesser Lord Kusanali, she strives to have a stronger presence in Sumeru after being freed from her confinement in the Sanctuary of Surasthana.\", \"doc_source\": \"Nahida\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"At the end of the Sumeru Archon Quests, Rukkhadevata sacrifices herself by having Lesser Lord Kusanali remove all memories of her existence from Teyvat via Irminsul. The only person to still remember her is the Traveler.\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali was discovered after Greater Lord Rukkhadevata's death and brought back to Sumeru City, where she lives in the Sanctuary of Surasthana.\", \"doc_source\": \"Through Mists of Smoke and Forests Dark\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Current playable Dendro Vision holders from Sumeru include: Alhaitham, Collei, Kaveh, and Tighnari.\", \"doc_source\": \"Vision/Gallery\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"NPC Rana from Sumeru also holds a Dendro Vision.\", \"doc_source\": \"Vision/Gallery\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Collei was born with Eleazar, a disease endemic to Sumeru. After the events of the Archon Quest, Eleazar patients recovered.\", \"doc_source\": \"Through Mists of Smoke and Forests Dark\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Collei recovered from Eleazar after the conclusion of the Sumeru Archon Quests.\", \"doc_source\": \"A Toast to Victory\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Akasha was described as the legacy of Greater Lord Rukkhadevata, developed by the Akademiya into a vault for collecting knowledge.\", \"doc_source\": \"Loading Screen/Sumeru\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali shuts down the Akasha at the conclusion of Act V of Chapter III.\", \"doc_source\": \"Where the Boat of Consciousness Lies\", \"verified\": true}\n  ],\n  \"required_entities\": [\"Seven Sovereigns\", \"Apep\", \"Heavenly Principles\", \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"Nahida\", \"Irminsul\", \"Akasha\", \"King Deshret\", \"Nabu Malikata\", \"Dendro\", \"Sumeru\", \"Alhaitham\", \"Collei\", \"Kaveh\", \"Tighnari\", \"Rana\", \"Vision\"],\n  \"required_relations\": [\n    {\"head\": \"Apep\", \"relation\": \"held elemental Authority of\", \"tail\": \"Dendro\", \"doc_source\": \"Timeline\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Heavenly Principles\", \"relation\": \"took Authority from\", \"tail\": \"Seven Sovereigns\", \"doc_source\": \"Timeline\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"relation\": \"was original Dendro Archon of\", \"tail\": \"Sumeru\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"relation\": \"was avatar of\", \"tail\": \"Irminsul\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"relation\": \"co-reigned with\", \"tail\": \"King Deshret\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"relation\": \"co-reigned with\", \"tail\": \"Nabu Malikata\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"relation\": \"created\", \"tail\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"relation\": \"created\", \"tail\": \"Akasha System\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"relation\": \"succeeded as Dendro Archon\", \"tail\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Alhaitham\", \"relation\": \"holds Dendro Vision in\", \"tail\": \"Sumeru\", \"doc_source\": \"Vision/Gallery\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Collei\", \"relation\": \"holds Dendro Vision in\", \"tail\": \"Sumeru\", \"doc_source\": \"Vision/Gallery\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Kaveh\", \"relation\": \"holds Dendro Vision in\", \"tail\": \"Sumeru\", \"doc_source\": \"Vision/Gallery\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Tighnari\", \"relation\": \"holds Dendro Vision in\", \"tail\": \"Sumeru\", \"doc_source\": \"Vision/Gallery\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Rana\", \"relation\": \"holds Dendro Vision in\", \"tail\": \"Sumeru\", \"doc_source\": \"Vision/Gallery\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"relation\": \"shut down\", \"tail\": \"Akasha\", \"doc_source\": \"Where the Boat of Consciousness Lies\"}\n  ],\n  \"required_reasoning_steps\": [],\n  \"hallucination_traps\": [\n    {\"trap\": \"Confusing who bestows Visions — the documents do not explicitly state that Archons bestow Visions, nor do they clarify the exact mechanism of Vision bestowal.\", \"correct\": \"The provided documents do not contain information about the specific mechanism by which Visions are granted to individuals. The question of who bestows Visions is not addressed in these documents.\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"Claiming Greater Lord Rukkhadevata died fighting in battle during the cataclysm in a conventional sense.\", \"correct\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata was one of the casualties of the cataclysm, but her final sacrifice involved having Lesser Lord Kusanali erase all memories of her from Irminsul.\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"Assuming Nahida/Lesser Lord Kusanali is a completely separate entity from Greater Lord Rukkha", "_review_flags": [], "_needs_human_review": false, "_meta": {"question_id": "T4-E04", "tier": 4, "question": "Trace the complete chain of power and bestowal — from the origin of the Vision system to the current status of Dendro Vision holders in Sumeru.", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 4, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 6, "total": 18}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 19066, "oracle_out": 2000, "qc_in": 21429, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 44495}, "cost_usd": 0.9074}}
{"question_id": "T4-E05", "_parse_error": true, "_raw": "```json\n{\n  \"question_id\": \"T4-E05\",\n  \"tier\": 4,\n  \"question_type\": \"factual\",\n  \"key_facts\": [\n    {\"fact\": \"The Akademiya's official leadership consists of Lesser Lord Kusanali and the Six Great Sages, with the sages ruling over Sumeru in Kusanali's place due to her isolation in the Sanctuary of Surasthana.\", \"doc_source\": \"Akademiya\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The sages of Sumeru Akademiya kept Lesser Lord Kusanali imprisoned in the Sanctuary of Surasthana for five hundred years, and they rarely speak to her.\", \"doc_source\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The sages of Sumeru Akademiya worked with Il Dottore (the Fatui Harbinger) to ascend Scaramouche into a new God of Wisdom called 'Shouki no Kami, the Prodigal,' comparable to Greater Lord Rukkhadevata.\", \"doc_source\": \"Scaramouche\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Dottore was revealed to be working with the sages of Sumeru Akademiya during Archon Quest Chapter III: Act III - Dreams, Emptiness, Deception.\", \"doc_source\": \"Dottore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Alhaitham is the Akademiya's Scribe, a member of the Haravatat, and played a key role in the plan to rescue Lesser Lord Kusanali from the sages, including implanting a faked order into the Akasha system.\", \"doc_source\": \"Alhaitham/Lore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Cyno serves as the General Mahamatra; his reinstatement was celebrated after the operation to save Lesser Lord Kusanali, and the Matra is a subordinate faction of the Akademiya.\", \"doc_source\": \"A Toast to Victory\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Matra is listed as a subordinate faction of the Akademiya.\", \"doc_source\": \"Akademiya\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Akademiya promotes worship of the deceased Greater Lord Rukkhadevata over Lesser Lord Kusanali, causing most people to be apathetic towards the current Archon.\", \"doc_source\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Alhaitham refused the position of Grand Sage and when thrust upon the position of Acting Grand Sage, expressed intent to resign as soon as possible.\", \"doc_source\": \"Alhaitham/Lore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Grand Sage Azar is mentioned as having an office in the Akademiya and being 'well-prepared' to send the Traveler into confinement and exile Alhaitham during the rescue operation.\", \"doc_source\": \"Jnagarbha Day\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Dottore had been expelled from Sumeru Akademiya in the past for murdering Sohreh and crossing moral boundaries in his research of Eleazar, but later returned to work with the sages.\", \"doc_source\": \"Dottore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Dehya and the Traveler's party were tasked with tracking Dottore to ensure he would not interfere with the rescue of Lesser Lord Kusanali.\", \"doc_source\": \"As by a God's Side\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali coerced a Dottore segment into erasing the other segments in exchange for the Electro Gnosis, exploiting the segments' tendency to squabble with each other.\", \"doc_source\": \"Dottore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Nilou danced outside the Akademiya to trigger the faked order Alhaitham implanted into the Akasha, causing all guards to rush out during the rescue operation.\", \"doc_source\": \"Jnagarbha Day\", \"verified\": true}\n  ],\n  \"required_entities\": [\"Sumeru Akademiya\", \"Six Great Sages\", \"Grand Sage Azar\", \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"Il Dottore\", \"Scaramouche\", \"Alhaitham\", \"Cyno\", \"Matra\", \"Fatui\", \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"Nilou\", \"Dehya\", \"Traveler\"],\n  \"required_relations\": [\n    {\"head\": \"Six Great Sages\", \"relation\": \"governs in place of\", \"tail\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"doc_source\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Sages\", \"relation\": \"imprisoned\", \"tail\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"doc_source\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Sages\", \"relation\": \"collaborated with\", \"tail\": \"Il Dottore\", \"doc_source\": \"Dottore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Sages and Dottore\", \"relation\": \"attempted to ascend\", \"tail\": \"Scaramouche\", \"doc_source\": \"Scaramouche\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Alhaitham\", \"relation\": \"holds position of Scribe in\", \"tail\": \"Sumeru Akademiya\", \"doc_source\": \"Alhaitham/Lore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Alhaitham\", \"relation\": \"opposed\", \"tail\": \"Grand Sage Azar\", \"doc_source\": \"Jnagarbha Day\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Cyno\", \"relation\": \"serves as General Mahamatra of\", \"tail\": \"Matra\", \"doc_source\": \"A Toast to Victory\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Matra\", \"relation\": \"subordinate faction of\", \"tail\": \"Sumeru Akademiya\", \"doc_source\": \"Akademiya\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Il Dottore\", \"relation\": \"was expelled from\", \"tail\": \"Sumeru Akademiya\", \"doc_source\": \"Dottore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"relation\": \"exchanged Electro Gnosis with\", \"tail\": \"Il Dottore\", \"doc_source\": \"Dottore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Alhaitham\", \"relation\": \"led rescue plan for\", \"tail\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"doc_source\": \"Jnagarbha Day\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Sumeru Akademiya\", \"relation\": \"promotes worship of\", \"tail\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"doc_source\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\"}\n  ],\n  \"required_reasoning_steps\": [],\n  \"hallucination_traps\": [\n    {\"trap\": \"Confusing the Six Great Sages as being allied with Alhaitham or the Traveler — they are the antagonistic faction.\", \"correct\": \"The sages imprisoned Kusanali and collaborated with Dottore; Alhaitham and the Traveler's group opposed them.\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"Assuming Dottore was always an outsider to the Akademiya.\", \"correct\": \"Dottore was originally a student at Sumeru Akademiya before being expelled, and later returned to collaborate with the sages.\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"Claiming Scaramouche was created by the sages or the Akademiya.\", \"correct\": \"Scaramouche is a puppet created by Raiden Ei; the sages and Dottore merely attempted to ascend him into a new God of Wisdom.\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"Stating that Alhaitham became Grand Sage permanently.\", \"correct\": \"Alhaitham refused the Grand Sage position and only served as Acting Grand Sage temporarily, expressing intent to resign as soon as possible.\"}\n  ],\n  \"min_acceptable_facts\": 3,\n  \"coverage_notes\": \"The documents do not provide a comprehensive list of all named sages beyond Grand Sage Azar, nor do they detail the specific internal Akademiya darshan (school) factions and their political positions in granular detail. The six individual darshans (Haravatat, Rtawahist, Vahumana,", "_review_flags": [], "_needs_human_review": false, "_meta": {"question_id": "T4-E05", "tier": 4, "question": "What are the different internal power factions within the Akademiya during the Sumeru Archon Quest, who are the key figures of each faction, and how do they relate to each other?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 5, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 6, "total": 19}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 19135, "oracle_out": 2000, "qc_in": 21497, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 44632}, "cost_usd": 0.9095}}
{"question_id": "T4-E06", "_parse_error": true, "_raw": "```json\n{\n  \"question_id\": \"T4-E06\",\n  \"tier\": 4,\n  \"question_type\": \"factual\",\n  \"key_facts\": [\n    {\"fact\": \"Dottore与须弥教令院的贤者合作，在须弥开展多项行动\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Dottore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Dottore研究将禁忌知识武器化，途径包括枯化（The Withering）和元素灾病（Eleazar）\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Dottore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Dottore试图利用梦境的力量来提升人类的认知能力\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Dottore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Dottore在教令院期间谋杀了Sohreh，并在Eleazar研究中逾越道德底线，因此被逐出须弥教令院\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Dottore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Dottore利用已故Eleazar患者的身体部位成功治疗了Abbas\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Dottore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Collei是Dottore的前Eleazar患者之一，她的治疗使症状得到控制，但给她留下了巨大的身体和心理创伤\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Dottore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Collei被骗子（与Dottore合作的占卜师）从父母身边带走，成为了神之眼残渣（Archon Residue）实验的试验品\", \"doc_source\": \"Collei/Lore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Collei患有Eleazar——须弥特有的疾病，会在身体上形成黑色硬化鳞片，最终导致完全瘫痪\", \"doc_source\": \"Collei/Lore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Dottore的下属Oleg与Eremite成员Kasim合作，试图利用能量提取装置从枯化中提取力量\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Oleg\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Alphonso（Trofin Snezhevich）的小组作为Dottore的另一项目，旨在捕获兰那罗（Aranara），以利用梦境的力量\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Oleg\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Dottore创造了基于自己不同时期的分身（segments），以超越人类认知和寿命的限制\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Dottore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"小吉祥草王（Lesser Lord Kusanali）利用分身之间的内讧，胁迫与她对峙的分身消除其他分身，以换取雷元素神之心\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Dottore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Dottore在Tatarasuna发现了'kabukimono'并策划了涉及谋杀和被背叛感的残酷实验，间接导致kabukimono后来成为散兵（Scaramouche）\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Dottore\", \"verified\": true}\n  ],\n  \"required_entities\": [\"Dottore\", \"Sumeru Akademiya\", \"Collei\", \"Oleg\", \"Kasim\", \"Alphonso/Trofin Snezhevich\", \"Aranara\", \"The Withering\", \"Eleazar\", \"Sohreh\", \"Abbas\", \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"Electro Gnosis\", \"Archon Residue\", \"Scaramouche/Kabukimono\"],\n  \"required_relations\": [\n    {\"head\": \"Dottore\", \"relation\": \"与...合作\", \"tail\": \"须弥教令院贤者\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Dottore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Dottore\", \"relation\": \"武器化研究\", \"tail\": \"The Withering\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Dottore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Dottore\", \"relation\": \"武器化研究\", \"tail\": \"Eleazar\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Dottore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Dottore\", \"relation\": \"谋杀\", \"tail\": \"Sohreh\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Dottore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Dottore\", \"relation\": \"利用尸体部位治疗\", \"tail\": \"Abbas\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Dottore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Dottore\", \"relation\": \"实验对象/造成身心创伤\", \"tail\": \"Collei\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Dottore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Collei\", \"relation\": \"被用于\", \"tail\": \"Archon Residue实验\", \"doc_source\": \"Collei/Lore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Oleg\", \"relation\": \"下属执行\", \"tail\": \"Dottore的枯化能量提取计划\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Oleg\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Oleg\", \"relation\": \"合作\", \"tail\": \"Kasim\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Oleg\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Alphonso小组\", \"relation\": \"执行\", \"tail\": \"Dottore的捕获兰那罗计划\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Oleg\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Dottore\", \"relation\": \"利用梦境力量\", \"tail\": \"提升人类认知能力\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Dottore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Dottore\", \"relation\": \"被逐出\", \"tail\": \"Sumeru Akademiya\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Dottore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"relation\": \"以神之心交换\", \"tail\": \"Dottore消除其他分身\", \"doc_source\": \"NPC/Dottore\"}\n  ],\n  \"required_reasoning_steps\": [],\n  \"hallucination_traps\": [\n    {\"trap\": \"误认为Dottore直接实施了枯化（The Withering）攻击\", \"correct\": \"Dottore研究将枯化武器化，具体由下属Oleg通过与Kasim合作的能量提取装置执行\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"混淆Collei的Eleazar疾病与Archon Residue实验，认为两者是同一件事\", \"correct\": \"Collei本身患有Eleazar，Dottore控制了她的症状，但同时将她用于Archon Residue实验，两者是不同的伤害\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"误认为Dottore亲自捕获兰那罗\", \"correct\": \"捕获兰那罗的行动由Alphonso（Trofin Snezhevich）的小组执行，是Dottore项目的一部分\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"误认为Dottore在须弥制造了Scaramouche\", \"correct\": \"Dottore对kabukimono的实验发生在稻妻的Tataras", "_review_flags": [], "_needs_human_review": false, "_meta": {"question_id": "T4-E06", "tier": 4, "question": "What were all of Dottore's known operations in Sumeru, through which intermediate entities did they cause harm, and what were the specific impacts on Sumeru's people?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 6, "layer_b": 7, "layer_c": 6, "total": 19}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 19284, "oracle_out": 2000, "qc_in": 21647, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 44931}, "cost_usd": 0.914}}
{"question_id": "T4-E07", "_parse_error": true, "_raw": "{\n  \"question_id\": \"T4-E07\",\n  \"tier\": 4,\n  \"question_type\": \"factual\",\n  \"key_facts\": [\n    {\"fact\": \"Alhaitham is the Scribe of the Sumeru Akademiya and a member of the Haravatat Darshan.\", \"doc_source\": \"PlayableCharacter: Alhaitham\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Kaveh was forced to reside with Alhaitham after becoming insolvent from the Palace of Alcazarzaray construction; they have a complicated relationship.\", \"doc_source\": \"PlayableCharacter: Kaveh\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Alhaitham and Kaveh frequently squabble due to their contrasting ideals and personalities — Alhaitham values rationality while Kaveh operates by what he feels to be right.\", \"doc_source\": \"Alhaitham/Lore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Alhaitham describes Kaveh as 'a light of the Kshahrewar and a master builder and craftsman' and acknowledges his exceptional brilliance, portraying him as an excellent mirror of himself.\", \"doc_source\": \"Kaveh/Lore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Alhaitham's Good Night voice-over references his roommate (Kaveh) hammering away on projects at night, preferring he wasn't home at all.\", \"doc_source\": \"Alhaitham/Voice-Overs\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Kaveh's Good Morning voice-over hopes the listener doesn't 'run into someone who ruins your day first thing in the morning,' an implied reference to Alhaitham.\", \"doc_source\": \"Kaveh/Voice-Overs\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Alhaitham helped rescue Lesser Lord Kusanali (Nahida), though he states he takes no pride in the fact that he helped rescue a god.\", \"doc_source\": \"Alhaitham/Voice-Overs\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"In the Archon Quest 'Cry From the Eleazar Hospital,' Alhaitham and Cyno work together investigating in Aaru Village, though Alhaitham operates independently and Cyno criticizes him for not helping.\", \"doc_source\": \"Quest: Cry From the Eleazar Hospital\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Cyno is the General Mahamatra of the Akademiya, leading all Matras, and harbors friendships with Tighnari, Alhaitham, and Kaveh.\", \"doc_source\": \"Cyno/Lore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Cyno shows concern for Collei, frequently visiting her, and Tighnari serves as Collei's mentor — connecting Cyno and Tighnari through their mutual care for Collei.\", \"doc_source\": \"Cyno/Lore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Tighnari is friends with Cyno but does not appreciate his jokes, having been exposed to many unfunny jokes.\", \"doc_source\": \"Tighnari/Lore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"In 'A Toast to Victory,' a feast is held to celebrate Cyno's reinstatement as General Mahamatra; Tighnari, the Traveler, Collei, and others are involved in this celebration.\", \"doc_source\": \"Quest: A Toast to Victory\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"In 'After Repose,' Cyno, Tighnari, Collei, and the Traveler go camping together at Gandharva Ville, demonstrating their close friendship.\", \"doc_source\": \"Quest: After Repose\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Cyno makes a pun ('VAL-uable' / 'berry') during the camping trip, and Tighnari is unamused, consistent with their dynamic.\", \"doc_source\": \"Quest: After Repose\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"In 'Where the Boat of Consciousness Lies,' Nahida (Lesser Lord Kusanali) joins the Traveler's party to fight Shouki no Kami and enters Irminsul, where Greater Lord Rukkhadevata is erased from history and Nahida shuts down the Akasha.\", \"doc_source\": \"Quest: Where the Boat of Consciousness Lies\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Nahida, as Lesser Lord Kusanali, strives to have a stronger presence in Sumeru after being freed from confinement in the Sanctuary of Surasthana.\", \"doc_source\": \"PlayableCharacter: Nahida\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"In 'Wondrous Times' (Kaveh's Hangout), Tighnari encounters Kaveh in Sumeru City, notices he's been drinking, and scolds him for drinking in broad daylight; Tighnari then invites Kaveh to a meal at Pardis Dhyai.\", \"doc_source\": \"Quest: Wondrous Times\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"In the same quest, Tighnari mentions Cyrus (Cyno's adoptive father) and a granny (Professor Zaha Hadi) banging on his door, showing Tighnari's awareness of Cyno's family connections.\", \"doc_source\": \"Quest: Wondrous Times\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Kaveh and Alhaitham's clashes are shown in game scenes, character voice-lines, and even messages on bulletin boards across Sumeru City and Port Ormos.\", \"doc_source\": \"Kaveh/Lore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Alhaitham refused the position of Grand Sage and when thrust upon the position of Acting Grand Sage, expressed intent to resign as soon as possible.\", \"doc_source\": \"Alhaitham/Lore\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"In 'A Toast to Victory,' the Traveler goes to the House of Daena to look for Alhaitham after the operation to save Nahida concludes.\", \"doc_source\": \"Quest: A Toast to Victory\", \"verified\": true}\n  ],\n  \"required_entities\": [\"Alhaitham\", \"Nahida\", \"Kaveh\", \"Cyno\", \"Tighnari\"],\n  \"required_relations\": [\n    {\"head\": \"Kaveh\", \"relation\": \"roommate / complicated relationship\", \"tail\": \"Alhaitham\", \"doc_source\": \"PlayableCharacter: Kaveh\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Alhaitham\", \"relation\": \"ideological rival / frequent squabbles\", \"tail\": \"Kaveh\", \"doc_source\": \"Alhaitham/Lore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Alhaitham\", \"relation\": \"acknowledges brilliance of\", \"tail\": \"Kaveh\", \"doc_source\": \"Kaveh/Lore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Alhaitham\", \"relation\": \"helped rescue\", \"tail\": \"Nahida\", \"doc_source\": \"Alhaitham/Voice-Overs\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Alhaitham\", \"relation\": \"colleague/ally in investigation\", \"tail\": \"Cyno\", \"doc_source\": \"Quest: Cry From the Eleazar Hospital\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Cyno\", \"relation\": \"friend\", \"tail\": \"Alhaitham\", \"doc_source\": \"Cyno/Lore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Cyno\", \"relation\": \"friend\", \"tail\": \"Tighnari\", \"doc_source\": \"Cyno/Lore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Cyno\", \"relation\": \"friend\", \"tail\": \"Kaveh\", \"doc_source\": \"Cyno/Lore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Tighnari\", \"relation\": \"friend (dislikes his jokes)\", \"tail\": \"Cyno\", \"doc_source\": \"Tighnari/Lore\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Tighnari\", \"relation\": \"acquaintance / shows concern for\", \"tail\": \"Kaveh\", \"doc_source\": \"Quest: Wondrous Times", "_review_flags": [], "_needs_human_review": false, "_meta": {"question_id": "T4-E07", "tier": 4, "question": "What are all known direct and indirect relationships among these five characters: Alhaitham, Nahida, Kaveh, Cyno, and Tighnari?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 5, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 6, "total": 19}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 22848, "oracle_out": 2000, "qc_in": 25211, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 52059}, "cost_usd": 1.0209}}
{"question_id": "T4-E08", "_parse_error": true, "_raw": "```json\n{\n  \"question_id\": \"T4-E08\",\n  \"tier\": 4,\n  \"question_type\": \"factual\",\n  \"key_facts\": [\n    {\"fact\": \"The Akasha System was originally developed by Greater Lord Rukkhadevata using her Gnosis.\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Akasha System was expanded on by Sumeru Akademiya after Greater Lord Rukkhadevata's death.\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Akasha System is powered by the Dendro Archon's Gnosis.\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Akasha Terminal is the physical device (earpiece) that allows individual users to connect to the Akasha and access knowledge.\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali (Nahida) is referred to as 'The First Akasha Terminal' and can enter anyone's mind as long as they're wearing their Akasha Terminal.\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Akasha Terminal harvests the Jnana Energy (dreams) of Sumeru's people, which is why people in Sumeru do not dream.\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata created the Akasha System to 'borrow' the dreams of her people and empower her, as she was unable to eradicate forbidden knowledge invading Irminsul with her strength alone.\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Akademiya's sages maximized the Akasha's output by trapping denizens of Sumeru City in a samsara, harvesting their dreams repeatedly to elevate Scaramouche to godhood.\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Akasha System is also capable of computation, producing new data such as predicting movement of persons based on existing data.\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Akasha is described as Greater Lord Rukkhadevata's lasting legacy and a treasure trove of collected knowledge.\", \"doc_source\": \"The Trail of the God of Wisdom\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Prolonged use of the Akasha System diminishes one's ability to think and asserts knowledge as true making it difficult to correct if wrong.\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Akademiya used the Akasha's computation function to escape investigation by General Mahamatra Cyno.\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"A weaponized upgrade called the 'Neo Akasha Terminal' was created by Kusanali to assist the Traveler in battle.\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali shut down the Akasha System after the events of Archon Quest Chapter III: Act V.\", \"doc_source\": \"Where the Boat of Consciousness Lies\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Six Great Sages and Lesser Lord Kusanali are listed as leaders of the Akademiya, which manages the Akasha System.\", \"doc_source\": \"Akademiya\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Irminsul is connected to the Akasha System's function indirectly: the forbidden knowledge invading Irminsul was the reason Rukkhadevata created the Akasha to borrow dreams.\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Kusanali refused to possess living beings via the Akasha, instead opting to control Katheryne due to her being an artificial lifeform.\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Desert people coming to Sumeru City are automatically given lower Akasha clearance than city people due to old prejudice.\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\", \"verified\": true}\n  ],\n  \"required_entities\": [\n    \"Akasha System\",\n    \"Akasha Terminal\",\n    \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\",\n    \"Dendro Archon's Gnosis\",\n    \"Sumeru Akademiya\",\n    \"Lesser Lord Kusanali (Nahida)\",\n    \"Irminsul\",\n    \"Scaramouche\",\n    \"Neo Akasha Terminal\",\n    \"Six Great Sages\",\n    \"Katheryne\",\n    \"Jnana Energy\"\n  ],\n  \"required_relations\": [\n    {\"head\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"relation\": \"created\", \"tail\": \"Akasha System\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Akasha System\", \"relation\": \"powered_by\", \"tail\": \"Dendro Archon's Gnosis\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Sumeru Akademiya\", \"relation\": \"expanded_and_managed\", \"tail\": \"Akasha System\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Akasha Terminal\", \"relation\": \"is_interface_device_of\", \"tail\": \"Akasha System\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"relation\": \"referred_to_as\", \"tail\": \"The First Akasha Terminal\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Akasha System\", \"relation\": \"harvests\", \"tail\": \"Jnana Energy (dreams)\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"relation\": \"created_Akasha_to_combat\", \"tail\": \"forbidden knowledge in Irminsul\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Sumeru Akademiya sages\", \"relation\": \"exploited_Akasha_to_elevate\", \"tail\": \"Scaramouche\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"relation\": \"created\", \"tail\": \"Neo Akasha Terminal\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"relation\": \"shut_down\", \"tail\": \"Akasha System\", \"doc_source\": \"Where the Boat of Consciousness Lies\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"relation\": \"controlled_via_Akasha\", \"tail\": \"Katheryne\", \"doc_source\": \"Akasha System\"}\n  ],\n  \"required_reasoning_steps\": [],\n  \"hallucination_traps\": [\n    {\"trap\": \"Confusing the Akasha System with Irminsul itself — they are distinct systems, though Irminsul's forbidden knowledge crisis motivated the Akasha's creation.\", \"correct\": \"The Akasha System was created by Rukkhadevata to borrow dreams to empower herself against forbidden knowledge invading Irminsul; the Akasha is not part of Irminsul.\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"Claiming the Akasha System was created by the Akademiya.\", \"correct\": \"The Akasha System was created by Greater Lord Rukkhadevata; the Akademiya only expanded and managed it after her death.\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"Stating that the Akasha is powered by Nahida's personal power rather than the Gnosis.\", \"correct\": \"The Akasha System is powered by the Dendro Archon's Gnosis specifically.\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"Claiming Nahida possesses living beings through the Akasha Terminal routinely.\", \"correct\": \"Nahida refuses to possess living beings unless absolutely necessary, instead opting to control the artificial lifeform Katheryne.\"}\n  ],\n  \"min_acceptable_facts\": 3,\n  \"coverage_notes\": \"The documents do not provide detailed technical architecture (e.g., internal data flow, server/node structure) of the Akasha", "_review_flags": [], "_needs_human_review": false, "_meta": {"question_id": "T4-E08", "tier": 4, "question": "What entities (deities, structures, organizations, individuals) make up the Akasha System's architecture? Decompose its complete dependency chain.", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 5, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 6, "total": 19}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 19312, "oracle_out": 2000, "qc_in": 21675, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 44987}, "cost_usd": 0.9148}}
{"question_id": "T4-E09", "_parse_error": true, "_raw": "```json\n{\n  \"question_id\": \"T4-E09\",\n  \"tier\": 4,\n  \"question_type\": \"factual\",\n  \"key_facts\": [\n    {\"fact\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata was the original Dendro Archon of Sumeru, the avatar of Irminsul, and predecessor to Lesser Lord Kusanali.\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata, King Deshret, and Nabu Malikata were known as 'The Three Eternal Companion-Gods' who co-reigned in Sumeru.\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Nabu Malikata foresaw the coming of the cataclysm and entrusted Rukkhadevata with 'a part of herself,' a Khvarena of flowers.\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"During the cataclysm 500 years ago, the previous Dendro Archon Greater Lord Rukkhadevata was slain and Lesser Lord Kusanali took her place.\", \"doc_source\": \"Sumeru\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The cataclysm involved hordes of beasts emerging from the abyss ('The Black Tide'), a dark flood that swallowed fields, villages, and cities, devouring living creatures by the thousands.\", \"doc_source\": \"The Folio of Foliage\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata embarked on a final journey with her followers to save the creatures of the earth from the root cause of the blight beneath the earth.\", \"doc_source\": \"The Folio of Foliage\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Before her death, Greater Lord Rukkhadevata created the Akasha System to purge forbidden knowledge from Irminsul and created her next incarnation, Lesser Lord Kusanali.\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali was created from the purest branch of Irminsul by Greater Lord Rukkhadevata to be her successor.\", \"doc_source\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali was discovered after Greater Lord Rukkhadevata's death and brought back to Sumeru City, where she was confined in the Sanctuary of Surasthana.\", \"doc_source\": \"Chapter III\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The sages of the Sumeru Akademiya rarely spoke to Lesser Lord Kusanali and ruled over Sumeru in her place, promoting worship of Greater Lord Rukkhadevata over Lesser Lord Kusanali.\", \"doc_source\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"As the First Akasha Terminal, Lesser Lord Kusanali's consciousness was linked to the Akasha System, giving her access to the Akasha's stores of knowledge.\", \"doc_source\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Sabzeruz Festival was trapped in a samsara (time loop); the Akasha, relying on the power of a Gnosis, was involved in this manipulation through people's Akasha Terminals.\", \"doc_source\": \"The Causality of the Sabzeruz Festival\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"At the end of the Sumeru Archon Quests, the Traveler defeats the Everlasting Lord of Arcane Wisdom (Shouki no Kami, the Prodigal / The Balladeer).\", \"doc_source\": \"Where the Boat of Consciousness Lies\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata sacrificed herself by having Lesser Lord Kusanali remove all memories of her existence from Teyvat via Irminsul.\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Removing information from Irminsul erases all traces from Teyvat — people's memories, books, letters are changed — but actual events and their overall results remain unchanged.\", \"doc_source\": \"Irminsul\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"After all memories of Greater Lord Rukkhadevata were erased, Lesser Lord Kusanali is believed by all, including herself, to have always been the original Dendro Archon.\", \"doc_source\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The only known person to still clearly remember Greater Lord Rukkhadevata is the Traveler, because they are not from Teyvat and their memories are not under Irminsul's jurisdiction.\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali also shut down the Akasha at the conclusion of the Sumeru Archon Quest.\", \"doc_source\": \"Where the Boat of Consciousness Lies\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"The Heavenly Principles sent down divine nails to combat forbidden knowledge brought by Dragon King Nibelung; one nail devastated Sumeru, transforming verdant land into the Great Red Sand desert and suppressing the Dendro Dragon Apep.\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Forbidden knowledge was the root threat that corrupted Irminsul, requiring Rukkhadevata to create the Akasha System to purge it.\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"verified\": true}\n  ],\n  \"required_entities\": [\n    \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\",\n    \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\",\n    \"King Deshret\",\n    \"Nabu Malikata\",\n    \"Irminsul\",\n    \"Akasha System\",\n    \"The Cataclysm\",\n    \"Forbidden Knowledge\",\n    \"Sumeru Akademiya\",\n    \"The Traveler\",\n    \"Heavenly Principles\",\n    \"Apep\",\n    \"Shouki no Kami / The Balladeer\",\n    \"Sabzeruz Festival\",\n    \"Divine Nail\",\n    \"Gnosis\"\n  ],\n  \"required_relations\": [\n    {\"head\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"relation\": \"avatar_of\", \"tail\": \"Irminsul\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"relation\": \"co-reigned_with\", \"tail\": \"King Deshret\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"relation\": \"co-reigned_with\", \"tail\": \"Nabu Malikata\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Nabu Malikata\", \"relation\": \"foresaw\", \"tail\": \"The Cataclysm\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"The Cataclysm\", \"relation\": \"caused_death_of\", \"tail\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"doc_source\": \"Sumeru\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"relation\": \"created\", \"tail\": \"Akasha System\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"relation\": \"created_successor\", \"tail\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"doc_source\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"relation\": \"linked_to\", \"tail\": \"Akasha System\", \"doc_source\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Sumeru Akademiya\", \"relation\": \"confined\", \"tail\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\", \"doc_source\": \"Lesser Lord Kusanali\"},\n    {\"head\":", "_review_flags": [], "_needs_human_review": false, "_meta": {"question_id": "T4-E09", "tier": 4, "question": "Trace the causal chain of all key entities and events from the ancient Cataclysm through to the end of the Sumeru Archon Quest that shaped Sumeru's history.", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 6, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 6, "total": 20}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 19505, "oracle_out": 2000, "qc_in": 21868, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 45373}, "cost_usd": 0.9206}}
{"question_id": "T4-E10", "tier": 4, "question_type": "counterfactual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Sumeru Akademiya's leaders include Lesser Lord Kusanali and the Six Great Sages, with the Matra as a subordinate faction.", "doc_source": "Akademiya", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Akademiya takes a role as a governing body of Sumeru, handling much of the day-to-day affairs of Sumeru.", "doc_source": "Akademiya", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Nahida (Lesser Lord Kusanali) was confined extensively in the Sanctuary of Surasthana, and had chosen to leave the city's governance to the sages before deciding to intervene when they stepped out of line.", "doc_source": "Nahida/Lore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Nahida's self-esteem was significantly negatively affected due to the way the sages treated her.", "doc_source": "Nahida/Lore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "After the sages' downfall and the cleansing of Irminsul, Nahida's negative traits diminished; she now openly roams the city, engages with her people, and exhibits a much more cheerful outlook.", "doc_source": "Nahida/Lore", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The sages of Sumeru, under the aegis of the God of Wisdom, drove themselves into hysterics and abandoned all that is worldly in their pursuit of esoteric wisdom.", "doc_source": "Sumeru", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Knowledge was managed as a resource through the Akasha system, powered by the Gnosis of Greater Lord Rukkhadevata, and people of Sumeru frequently used Akasha Terminals. Adults did not dream, which was a source of pride.", "doc_source": "Sumeru/Culture", "verified": true}, {"fact": "After the suspension of the Akasha System, the people of Sumeru were able to dream once more.", "doc_source": "Sumeru/Culture", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Grand Sage Azar was well-prepared against the protagonists' plan to free Nahida, sending the Traveler into confinement and exiling Alhaitham during the Jnagarbha Day operation.", "doc_source": "Jnagarbha Day", "verified": true}, {"fact": "An operation was conducted to save Lesser Lord Kusanali, involving Alhaitham, Nilou, Cyno, and others, culminating in Cyno's reinstatement as the General Mahamatra.", "doc_source": "A Toast to Victory", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Akademiya has three virtues and six sins that form the base of its rules, and the sages have been adding new rules and amendments.", "doc_source": "Akademiya", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Dainsleif describes: 'The God of Wisdom's enemy is wisdom itself... In the city of scholars there is a push for folly, yet the God of Wisdom makes no argument against it.'", "doc_source": "Chapter III", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Nahida strives to have a stronger presence in Sumeru now that she has been freed from her extensive confinement in the Sanctuary of Surasthana.", "doc_source": "Nahida", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Nahida", "Sumeru Akademiya", "Six Great Sages", "Grand Sage Azar", "Sanctuary of Surasthana", "Akasha System", "Cyno", "Matra", "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata", "Irminsul"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Nahida", "relation": "leader_of", "tail": "Sumeru Akademiya", "doc_source": "Akademiya"}, {"head": "Six Great Sages", "relation": "leader_of", "tail": "Sumeru Akademiya", "doc_source": "Akademiya"}, {"head": "Sumeru Akademiya", "relation": "governs", "tail": "Sumeru", "doc_source": "Akademiya"}, {"head": "Six Great Sages", "relation": "confined", "tail": "Nahida", "doc_source": "Nahida/Lore"}, {"head": "Akasha System", "relation": "powered_by", "tail": "Greater Lord Rukkhadevata's Gnosis", "doc_source": "Sumeru/Culture"}], "required_reasoning_steps": ["Identify that the sages' interference with Nahida resulted in her extensive confinement in the Sanctuary of Surasthana, leaving governance entirely to the sages.", "Reason that without the sages' interference, Nahida would not have been confined and would have been free to exercise her authority as Dendro Archon and leader of the Akademiya from the beginning.", "Infer that with Nahida actively governing, the sages would not have had unchecked power to pursue their 'hysterical' and 'worldly-abandoning' pursuit of esoteric wisdom, nor to misuse the Akasha System.", "Deduce that the Akasha System might have been used differently or more benevolently — the dream-harvesting and knowledge hoarding that harmed citizens (e.g., Dunyarzad's consciousness dissipating) would likely not have occurred under Nahida's direct oversight.", "Reason that the sages' plan involving the Balladeer/Scaramouche becoming a god (as described in Act V) would not have progressed, as Nahida would have had political authority to prevent such schemes.", "Infer that Cyno would not have needed to be removed and then reinstated as General Mahamatra, as the political corruption driving his removal originated from the sages' unchecked power.", "Conclude that Nahida's self-esteem and social engagement would have been healthier from the start, leading to a more present and active Archon figure, and the Sabzeruz Festival samsara crisis would not have occurred.", "Note that the relationship between the forest and desert populations (including the Eremites) might have been managed differently, since the Akademiya's discriminatory policies were driven by the sages."], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Claiming that Nahida was imprisoned by forces outside of the Akademiya (e.g., by Fatui alone).", "correct": "Nahida was confined within the Sanctuary of Surasthana due to the sages' treatment of her, and her decision to leave governance to them was a consequence of that interference."}, {"trap": "Stating that the Akasha System was created by Nahida.", "correct": "The Akasha System was created by Greater Lord Rukkhadevata before her death during the cataclysm, and was powered by Rukkhadevata's Gnosis."}, {"trap": "Claiming that Nahida had no formal authority over the Akademiya.", "correct": "Nahida (Lesser Lord Kusanali) is listed as a leader of the Sumeru Akademiya alongside the Six Great Sages."}, {"trap": "Assuming the Six Great Sages were entirely removed from power after the Archon Quest.", "correct": "The documents describe the 'sages' downfall' but do not specify complete abolition of the sage system; Nahida now has a stronger presence."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "The documents do not provide detailed information on specific policies the sages enacted beyond knowledge management and Akasha misuse. Details about how the sages initially came to confine Nahida or the exact political mechanism of their power grab are not fully elaborated in the provided documents. The Balladeer/Scaramouche subplot is referenced indirectly (Act V quest) but the full political conspiracy details are not fully covered in the excerpts provided.", "_review_flags": ["coverage_notes: The documents do not provide detailed information on specific policies the sages enacted beyond know"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T4-E10", "tier": 4, "question": "If the Akademiya's Grand Sages had never interfered with Nahida, how would Sumeru's political landscape differ based on the existing entity relationships? (Counterfactual reasoning)", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 6, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 6, "total": 20}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 19560, "oracle_out": 1989, "qc_in": 21909, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 45458}, "cost_usd": 0.9212}}
{"question_id": "T4-E11", "_parse_error": true, "_raw": "```json\n{\n  \"question_id\": \"T4-E11\",\n  \"tier\": 4,\n  \"question_type\": \"factual\",\n  \"key_facts\": [\n    {\"fact\": \"Viridescent Venerer圣遗物套装聚焦于Viridescent（翠绿猎人女王）的故事，她生活在五百年前的灾变时期（cataclysm）\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Viridescent\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Deepwood Memories圣遗物套装扩展了Viridescent的故事\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Viridescent\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Viridescent的生活方式被灾变打断，灾变期间Greater Lord Rukkhadevata死亡，导致草木'不再说话'，深渊怪物入侵提瓦特\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Viridescent\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Gilded Dreams圣遗物套装与King Deshret相关联（The Artifact Set Gilded Dreams is attributed to him）\", \"doc_source\": \"[Artifact] Gilded Dreams (Equipment Card)\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Gilded Dreams的TCG卡牌描述为：'Some time later, absurd decisions would be issued alongside illusory madness, using lovely expectations as bait to lead the people towards a bitter end.'\", \"doc_source\": \"[Artifact] Gilded Dreams (Equipment Card)\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"King Deshret、Nabu Malikata和Greater Lord Rukkhadevata三位被称为须弥的三位神王（The Three Eternal Companion-Gods），在魔神战争期间共同统治须弥\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Nabu Malikata预见了灾变的到来，三神王文明的时代远早于五百年前的灾变\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata在五百年前的灾变中死亡，死前创建了Akasha系统以清除Irminsul中的禁忌知识，并创造了Lesser Lord Kusanali作为她的下一任化身\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Viridescent在追猎怪物的过程中经历了侵蚀（erosion），逐渐忘记了最初战斗的原因甚至那个盲眼男孩，被深渊怪物的黑血污染后越来越像野兽，最终被染血骑士（Bloodstained Knight）杀死\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Viridescent\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Deepwood Memories和Gilded Dreams同在Version 3.0随须弥地区一起推出\", \"doc_source\": \"[Other] Version/3.0\", \"verified\": true},\n    {\"fact\": \"Viridescent被一个盲眼男孩给予了Hunter's Path弓，该男孩在追寻其穿白甲兄弟的踪迹时迷失在森林中\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Viridescent\", \"verified\": true}\n  ],\n  \"required_entities\": [\"Viridescent Venerer\", \"Deepwood Memories\", \"Gilded Dreams\", \"Viridescent\", \"King Deshret\", \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"Nabu Malikata\", \"Cataclysm\", \"Sumeru\", \"Irminsul\"],\n  \"required_relations\": [\n    {\"head\": \"Viridescent Venerer\", \"relation\": \"聚焦人物\", \"tail\": \"Viridescent\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Viridescent\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Deepwood Memories\", \"relation\": \"扩展故事\", \"tail\": \"Viridescent\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Viridescent\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Gilded Dreams\", \"relation\": \"归属于\", \"tail\": \"King Deshret\", \"doc_source\": \"[Artifact] Gilded Dreams (Equipment Card)\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Viridescent\", \"relation\": \"活跃于\", \"tail\": \"Cataclysm (500年前)\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Viridescent\"},\n    {\"head\": \"King Deshret\", \"relation\": \"共同统治须弥\", \"tail\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"King Deshret\", \"relation\": \"共同统治须弥\", \"tail\": \"Nabu Malikata\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\"},\n    {\"head\": \"Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\", \"relation\": \"死于\", \"tail\": \"Cataclysm\", \"doc_source\": \"[NPC] Greater Lord Rukkhadevata\"}\n  ],\n  \"required_reasoning_steps\": [\n    \"识别Gilded Dreams对应King Deshret时代——须弥远古三神王文明时期（魔神战争时代及之前），代表须弥文明的起源与辉煌\",\n    \"识别Deepwood Memories与须弥森林及Greater Lord Rukkhadevata相关，文档明确指出其扩展了Viridescent的故事，与灾变时期森林衰败有关联；同时需注意文档中关于Deepwood Memories的具体历史时代对应信息有限\",\n    \"识别Viridescent Venerer对应五百年前灾变时期，Viridescent在灾变中从猎人变为怪物猎手，最终被侵蚀并死亡，代表须弥文明遭受的巨大打击\",\n    \"将三个时期串联：King Deshret的远古文明（Gilded Dreams）→ Greater Lord Rukkhadevata治理下的森林文明时代（Deepwood Memories的背景）→ 灾变带来的毁灭与转折（Viridescent Venerer），形成须弥文明从繁盛到衰落再到重生的叙事弧线\"\n  ],\n  \"hallucination_traps\": [\n    {\"trap\": \"误认为Deepwood Memories主要讲述King Deshret或沙漠文明的故事\", \"correct\": \"Deepwood Memories扩展了Viridescent的故事，与森林相关；Gilded Dreams才与King Deshret相关\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"误认为Viridescent Venerer对应的是魔神战争时期\", \"correct\": \"Viridescent生活在五百年前的灾变时期（cataclysm），而非更早的魔神战争时期\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"误将Gilded Dreams的历史时期归为灾变时期\", \"correct\": \"Gilded Dreams归属于King Deshret，其文明时代远早于灾变，属于魔神战争或更早的时期\"},\n    {\"trap\": \"认为三个圣遗物套装的故事完全独立无关联\", \"correct\": \"它们共同构成须弥文明演化的不同阶段，且灾变是连接它们的关键事件节点\"}\n  ", "_review_flags": [], "_needs_human_review": false, "_meta": {"question_id": "T4-E11", "tier": 4, "question": "Which historical eras do the three Sumeru artifact sets — Viridescent Venerer, Deepwood Memories, and Gilded Dreams — each correspond to? How do these three historical periods together form the complete narrative arc of Sumeru civilization's evolution?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 4, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 6, "total": 18}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 17555, "oracle_out": 2000, "qc_in": 19918, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 41473}, "cost_usd": 0.8621}}
{"question_id": "T4-E12", "tier": 4, "question_type": "factual", "key_facts": [{"fact": "The Akademiya's official power structure is led by Lesser Lord Kusanali and the Six Great Sages, with the Matra as a subordinate faction.", "doc_source": "[Concept] Akademiya", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The sages handled much of the day-to-day governing affairs of Sumeru, effectively functioning as the governing body beyond just an academic institution.", "doc_source": "[Concept] Akademiya", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Grand Sage Azar was removed from his position, after which Alhaitham became the Acting Grand Sage, indicating a power vacuum and restructuring.", "doc_source": "[Other] Vultur Volans Chapter", "verified": true}, {"fact": "After the former sages were removed and the Akasha System suspended, scholar Chandra explains that no one wanted to manually sift out papers and people were unsure of what to do, revealing the actual dependency on the old power structures.", "doc_source": "[Quest] Cry From the Eleazar Hospital", "verified": false}, {"fact": "In Alhaitham's Story Quest, researchers at the Akademiya express both positive and negative opinions about his role as Acting Grand Sage, revealing factional sentiments about the new power arrangement.", "doc_source": "[Other] Vultur Volans Chapter", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Siraj, a prominent Vahumana scholar said to become the next sage, was conducting forbidden experiments (related to human evolution, one of the Akademiya's cardinal sins), and had previously submitted a thesis to Azar — revealing that the power structure enabled or overlooked ethically problematic research.", "doc_source": "[Other] Vultur Volans Chapter", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Alhaitham had rejected Siraj's thesis paper because it touched human evolution (one of the six sins), but Azar had asked for his opinion on it, suggesting the Grand Sage was at least considering it — revealing a gap between official rules and how power actually operated.", "doc_source": "[Other] Vultur Volans Chapter", "verified": true}, {"fact": "The Akasha System was used to harvest dreams from people like Dunyarzad, and Nahida had to use her power to keep Dunyarzad's dying dream alive, revealing that the Akademiya's infrastructure was used for exploitation beyond its stated purpose.", "doc_source": "[Quest] Dawn (Quest)", "verified": true}, {"fact": "Panah at the city entrance describes the Akasha Terminal as Greater Lord Rukkhadevata's lasting legacy and a treasure trove of knowledge, presenting the official narrative, while the actual system was being used by the sages for control.", "doc_source": "[Quest] The Trail of the God of Wisdom", "verified": true}, {"fact": "After the Akasha System's suspension, the people of Sumeru were now able to dream once more, revealing that the system had been suppressing their dreams — a fact not part of the official narrative presented to citizens.", "doc_source": "[Other] Sumeru/Culture", "verified": true}], "required_entities": ["Sumeru Akademiya", "Six Great Sages", "Azar", "Alhaitham", "Akasha System", "Lesser Lord Kusanali", "Matra", "Siraj", "Chandra", "Panah", "Dunyarzad", "Nahida"], "required_relations": [{"head": "Azar", "relation": "held_position_of", "tail": "Grand Sage", "doc_source": "[Other] Vultur Volans Chapter"}, {"head": "Alhaitham", "relation": "became_acting", "tail": "Grand Sage", "doc_source": "[Other] Vultur Volans Chapter"}, {"head": "Siraj", "relation": "submitted_thesis_to", "tail": "Azar", "doc_source": "[Other] Vultur Volans Chapter"}, {"head": "Alhaitham", "relation": "rejected_thesis_of", "tail": "Siraj", "doc_source": "[Other] Vultur Volans Chapter"}, {"head": "Akasha System", "relation": "harvested_dreams_from", "tail": "Dunyarzad", "doc_source": "[Quest] Dawn (Quest)"}, {"head": "Sumeru Akademiya", "relation": "governs", "tail": "Sumeru", "doc_source": "[Concept] Akademiya"}, {"head": "Akasha System", "relation": "suppressed_dreams_of", "tail": "people of Sumeru", "doc_source": "[Other] Sumeru/Culture"}], "required_reasoning_steps": ["Identify the official narrative of the Akademiya's power structure (wisdom-serving institution led by sages under the Archon).", "Contrast with evidence from NPC dialogues showing the system enabled forbidden research (Siraj's experiments, Azar's complicity), dream harvesting, and citizen dependency on the Akasha.", "Recognize that Chandra's and Panah's dialogues represent the citizen-level perspective revealing structural dysfunction and information asymmetry.", "Synthesize how researcher reactions to Alhaitham's appointment reveal factional politics and uncertainty after the power restructuring."], "hallucination_traps": [{"trap": "Claiming specific named non-quest NPCs in Sumeru City provide extensive dialogue about power corruption when the documents mostly reference quest-related NPC dialogues.", "correct": "The provided documents primarily contain quest NPC dialogues (Chandra, Panah, researchers in Alhaitham's Story Quest) rather than ambient non-quest NPC dialogue about power workings."}, {"trap": "Attributing knowledge about the Akasha's dream harvesting to common citizens.", "correct": "The official narrative presented by NPCs like Panah frames the Akasha as a benevolent knowledge system; the dream harvesting was hidden from the public."}, {"trap": "Confusing the Matra (enforcement arm) with the Sages (governing body) in terms of who wielded actual political power.", "correct": "The Matra are a subordinate faction; the Six Great Sages and Grand Sage held governing authority."}], "min_acceptable_facts": 3, "coverage_notes": "The provided documents contain very limited ambient/non-quest NPC dialogue from Sumeru City. Most evidence about the Akademiya's actual power workings comes from quest dialogues (Archon Quests, Story Quests) rather than from dedicated non-main-quest NPCs. The documents lack dialogue from NPCs like shopkeepers, random citizens, or Matra members that might reveal informal power dynamics. Chandra's dialogue is from an Archon Quest context. The question asks specifically about 'non-main-quest NPCs' but the documents primarily provide main-quest and story-quest NPC dialogue content.", "_review_flags": ["key_facts[3]: verified=false — After the former sages were removed and the Akasha System su", "coverage_notes: The provided documents contain very limited ambient/non-quest NPC dialogue from Sumeru City. Most ev"], "_needs_human_review": true, "_meta": {"question_id": "T4-E12", "tier": 4, "question": "Among all non-main-quest NPCs in Sumeru City connected to the Akademiya's power structure, what do their dialogues reveal about the actual workings of power beyond the official narrative?", "docs_fetched": {"layer_a": 3, "layer_b": 8, "layer_c": 3, "total": 14}, "tokens": {"oracle_in": 14195, "oracle_out": 1724, "qc_in": 16280, "qc_out": 2000, "total": 34199}, "cost_usd": 0.7364}}
